7a03d73ac5c3ade4fb201a9281c0ba224dde7e53","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90134688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17","id":90134688,"login":"whiterabb17","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMTM0Njg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/whiterabb17","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/7a03d73ac5c3ade4fb201a9281c0ba224dde7e53","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDdhMDNkNzNhYzVjM2FkZTRmYjIwMWE5MjgxYzBiYTIyNGRkZTdlNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/d4962486b869e8e7defee1ddd7ac4f0c7a1c35e0","sha":"d4962486b869e8e7defee1ddd7ac4f0c7a1c35e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/d4962486b869e8e7defee1ddd7ac4f0c7a1c35e0"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/035d1ae814d496557bedda81ee1a1f7d0da630b5","sha":"035d1ae814d496557bedda81ee1a1f7d0da630b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/035d1ae814d496557bedda81ee1a1f7d0da630b5"}],"sha":"7a03d73ac5c3ade4fb201a9281c0ba224dde7e53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/7a03d73ac5c3ade4fb201a9281c0ba224dde7e53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/035d1ae814d496557bedda81ee1a1f7d0da630b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T05:54:59Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T05:54:59Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add Resume to the scan page and fix the resume endpoint\n\nThe scan page had RESCAN and STOP but no way to resume a failed scan;\nResume only lived in the scan list''s row menu. It now shows a RESUME button\nnext to STOP for failed, aborted and partially complete scans, and reports\nthe server''s answer in the page''s snackbar.\n\nThe endpoint behind both buttons:\n- refused with \"Max recovery limit (3) exceeded. Use the manual Resume\n  button to override\" once auto-recovery had run three times, though it is\n  the manual Resume and resume_scan_temporal resets the counter for a\n  manual resume. The cap now only applies to automatic recovery.\n- resumed a running, pending or paused scan too, starting a second\n  workflow over the same scan. Only failed, aborted and partially complete\n  scans are resumed now.\n- returned the exception text on an unexpected error; it returns the\n  generic message (rule 8.1).\n\nThe list menu and the scan page share isResumableScanStatus, and the\nresume mutation refreshes the scan summary as well as the list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"1051237285b6078197a9be4e61b6c86efea65425","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/1051237285b6078197a9be4e61b6c86efea65425"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/035d1ae814d496557bedda81ee1a1f7d0da630b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 1051237285b6078197a9be4e61b6c86efea65425\nparent 63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790834099 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790834099 +0000\n\nAdd Resume to the scan page and fix the resume endpoint\n\nThe scan page had RESCAN and STOP but no way to resume a failed scan;\nResume only lived in the scan list''s row menu. It now shows a RESUME button\nnext to STOP for failed, aborted and partially complete scans, and reports\nthe server''s answer in the page''s snackbar.\n\nThe endpoint behind both buttons:\n- refused with \"Max recovery limit (3) exceeded. Use the manual Resume\n  button to override\" once auto-recovery had run three times, though it is\n  the manual Resume and resume_scan_temporal resets the counter for a\n  manual resume. The cap now only applies to automatic recovery.\n- resumed a running, pending or paused scan too, starting a second\n  workflow over the same scan. Only failed, aborted and partially complete\n  scans are resumed now.\n- returned the exception text on an unexpected error; it returns the\n  generic message (rule 8.1).\n\nThe list menu and the scan page share isResumableScanStatus, and the\nresume mutation refreshes the scan summary as well as the list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIab1pA+\nh4eNa4Ab4iedScaCxPulgGj9eI062ROiMUa23fRb505CFNuRI51T3lTv+OC559fxvmpZ0JrgvZyX\nxgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T05:55:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/035d1ae814d496557bedda81ee1a1f7d0da630b5","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDAzNWQxYWU4MTRkNDk2NTU3YmVkZGE4MWVlMWExZjdkMGRhNjMwYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35","sha":"63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35"}],"sha":"035d1ae814d496557bedda81ee1a1f7d0da630b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/035d1ae814d496557bedda81ee1a1f7d0da630b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T05:33:18Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T05:33:18Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Keep the per-target fuzz lock for as long as the target is fuzzed\n\nDirectory fuzzing holds a Redis lock per target with a fixed 1800 s TTL.\nA target that took longer (here 70 minutes) outlived its lock, and when\nthe work was done release() raised LockNotOwnedError, failing the step.\nOn its last retry that failed the whole scan. A worker killed mid-target\nalso left its lock behind for up to 30 minutes, which the retry waited on.\n\nreNgine/utils/redis_lock.renewed_lock takes the lock with a 300 s TTL and\nrenews it every 60 s from a background thread (thread_local=False so the\nthread can see the token). A dead holder''s lock frees itself within five\nminutes, inside the step''s 15-minute heartbeat timeout. A lock lost or\nexpired anyway is logged instead of failing the work done under it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"04d1f99732fae5331a91e5fa6d566d1abddfe770","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/04d1f99732fae5331a91e5fa6d566d1abddfe770"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35","verification":{"payload":"tree 04d1f99732fae5331a91e5fa6d566d1abddfe770\nparent b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790832798 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790832798 +0000\n\nKeep the per-target fuzz lock for as long as the target is fuzzed\n\nDirectory fuzzing holds a Redis lock per target with a fixed 1800 s TTL.\nA target that took longer (here 70 minutes) outlived its lock, and when\nthe work was done release() raised LockNotOwnedError, failing the step.\nOn its last retry that failed the whole scan. A worker killed mid-target\nalso left its lock behind for up to 30 minutes, which the retry waited on.\n\nreNgine/utils/redis_lock.renewed_lock takes the lock with a 300 s TTL and\nrenews it every 60 s from a background thread (thread_local=False so the\nthread can see the token). A dead holder''s lock frees itself within five\nminutes, inside the step''s 15-minute heartbeat timeout. A lock lost or\nexpired anyway is logged instead of failing the work done under it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBlOmczl\n+cJZPGVgJ3ScY9G/vekF00m/phuatxOws6Ui3eaL9CPD5xSzUtHUGvfv2SFqyggCkVMUToS6CbK8\nDQI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T05:33:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDYzNDQ0ODM5YjlmOTBkNGRhYTFhYzU2NzA3N2U1ZDg0YjIwMDZhMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff","sha":"b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff"}],"sha":"63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/63444839b9f90d4daa1ac567077e5d84b2006a35"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T05:15:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T05:15:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Mark a dead attempt''s timeline row as interrupted when Temporal retries it\n\nWhen the orchestrator or executor container is recreated mid-task (e.g.\nmake up during a scan), the running attempt dies without finalising its\nScanActivity row. Temporal retries the activity, the retry can only claim\nINITIATED rows, so it creates a second row and the timeline shows the task\nrunning twice until the scan ends and the stale row turns Aborted.\n\nOn attempt 2+, the RUNNING row of the same scan, task name and Temporal\nactivity id is now set to FAILED with time_ended and \"Interrupted: the\nworker running this attempt stopped (e.g. a container restart); Temporal\nstarted attempt N.\" A pinned row (singular tool runs) is still reclaimed\ninstead. Rows of other activities and tasks are not touched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"3835233a4cc26fd443546532edca86bb744316d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/3835233a4cc26fd443546532edca86bb744316d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff","verification":{"payload":"tree 3835233a4cc26fd443546532edca86bb744316d8\nparent 30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790831754 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790831754 +0000\n\nMark a dead attempt''s timeline row as interrupted when Temporal retries it\n\nWhen the orchestrator or executor container is recreated mid-task (e.g.\nmake up during a scan), the running attempt dies without finalising its\nScanActivity row. Temporal retries the activity, the retry can only claim\nINITIATED rows, so it creates a second row and the timeline shows the task\nrunning twice until the scan ends and the stale row turns Aborted.\n\nOn attempt 2+, the RUNNING row of the same scan, task name and Temporal\nactivity id is now set to FAILED with time_ended and \"Interrupted: the\nworker running this attempt stopped (e.g. a container restart); Temporal\nstarted attempt N.\" A pinned row (singular tool runs) is still reclaimed\ninstead. Rows of other activities and tasks are not touched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDMplQyN\nLSwg4JXEw29ZKN4lPzp6VoTJSSWp5j5xdpVs95ZeQq40WK9wEtq/+pLURh3upoGlhqS7b8meLytV\n8A4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T05:15:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGIyMmRmOTNlMTMxYzM2YTAwZDZjN2RkYjYwNWMxZmZhYzQ1ZDkxZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98","sha":"30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98"}],"sha":"b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/b22df93e131c36a00d6c7ddb605c1ffac45d91ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:00:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:00:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Retry rate-limited LLM calls and let Anthropic write longer replies\n\n- A 429, Anthropic''s 529, a 5xx or a failed connection used to fail the\n  call outright. The provider is now asked up to twice more, waiting as\n  long as Retry-After says (at most 20 s) or 2 s then 4 s. Read timeouts\n  and other 4xx are not retried. The worst case (three 60 s attempts plus\n  40 s of waiting) stays under the 5-minute heartbeat timeout of the\n  activities that call the LLM. The AI Hub connection test does not retry.\n- Anthropic calls asked for at most 1024 output tokens, which cut long\n  reports off. The default is now 4096, the most every Claude model\n  supports; a caller''s max_tokens still wins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"ad7895b82c13a7f001b40cd219b241626f4faaba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/ad7895b82c13a7f001b40cd219b241626f4faaba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98","verification":{"payload":"tree ad7895b82c13a7f001b40cd219b241626f4faaba\nparent 4f713cf70e427f378206e6d29b99fe02ddded34b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790798411 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790798411 +0000\n\nRetry rate-limited LLM calls and let Anthropic write longer replies\n\n- A 429, Anthropic''s 529, a 5xx or a failed connection used to fail the\n  call outright. The provider is now asked up to twice more, waiting as\n  long as Retry-After says (at most 20 s) or 2 s then 4 s. Read timeouts\n  and other 4xx are not retried. The worst case (three 60 s attempts plus\n  40 s of waiting) stays under the 5-minute heartbeat timeout of the\n  activities that call the LLM. The AI Hub connection test does not retry.\n- Anthropic calls asked for at most 1024 output tokens, which cut long\n  reports off. The default is now 4096, the most every Claude model\n  supports; a caller''s max_tokens still wins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNSGc4aO\n9nTGl0tgaH/6CKmD13hsoGkYsTvk8ia9dcoEZ0cHUtKRY2IOfZRHFcb6prAWEAGOsfeGc3uGnrzp\nywU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:00:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDMwNDM5Y2UzZmZhY2M2YTY2OTg2MmVkZjExNWUwZWUwMGY0NmJiOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/4f713cf70e427f378206e6d29b99fe02ddded34b","sha":"4f713cf70e427f378206e6d29b99fe02ddded34b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/4f713cf70e427f378206e6d29b99fe02ddded34b"}],"sha":"30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/30439ce3ffacc6a669862edf115e0ee00f46bb98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/4f713cf70e427f378206e6d29b99fe02ddded34b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:54:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:54:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add an OpenAI-compatible LLM provider with a configurable base URL\n\nThe cloud providers'' URLs were hard-coded, so a gateway that speaks the\nOpenAI chat completions API (OpenRouter, a self-hosted LiteLLM, vLLM,\nLM Studio) could not be used.\n\n- New provider openai_compatible with LLMConfig.base_url (migration\n  dashboard 0024). The URL must be http(s) with a host and no credentials,\n  query or fragment; the AI Hub rejects anything else.\n- The model list comes from <base>/models without OpenAI''s gpt-* filter,\n  and the model field also takes ids the gateway does not list.\n- reNgine/llm_client.py holds the provider HTTP calls. The report\n  generators and the AI Hub connection test both used to carry their own\n  copy; they now share one, so the max_completion_tokens fallback also\n  applies to the gateway.\n- The connection test needs a model now instead of falling back to\n  gpt-3.5-turbo, claude-3-haiku-20240307 or gemini-1.5-flash.\n- update_llm_settings rejects unknown providers instead of creating a row.\n- documents/llm-integration.md lists the real LLMConfig fields.\n\nVigolium''s AI audit agents only take the openai and anthropic providers;\nwith openai_compatible it uses piolium, as for Ollama and Gemini.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"4d2ab4573397b2dd1e9841b3b97a4d5045e1f9bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/4d2ab4573397b2dd1e9841b3b97a4d5045e1f9bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/4f713cf70e427f378206e6d29b99fe02ddded34b","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d2ab4573397b2dd1e9841b3b97a4d5045e1f9bc\nparent 1501286d79419dc2eb3081e66825a056ed4e5daf\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790798068 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790798068 +0000\n\nAdd an OpenAI-compatible LLM provider with a configurable base URL\n\nThe cloud providers'' URLs were hard-coded, so a gateway that speaks the\nOpenAI chat completions API (OpenRouter, a self-hosted LiteLLM, vLLM,\nLM Studio) could not be used.\n\n- New provider openai_compatible with LLMConfig.base_url (migration\n  dashboard 0024). The URL must be http(s) with a host and no credentials,\n  query or fragment; the AI Hub rejects anything else.\n- The model list comes from <base>/models without OpenAI''s gpt-* filter,\n  and the model field also takes ids the gateway does not list.\n- reNgine/llm_client.py holds the provider HTTP calls. The report\n  generators and the AI Hub connection test both used to carry their own\n  copy; they now share one, so the max_completion_tokens fallback also\n  applies to the gateway.\n- The connection test needs a model now instead of falling back to\n  gpt-3.5-turbo, claude-3-haiku-20240307 or gemini-1.5-flash.\n- update_llm_settings rejects unknown providers instead of creating a row.\n- documents/llm-integration.md lists the real LLMConfig fields.\n\nVigolium''s AI audit agents only take the openai and anthropic providers;\nwith openai_compatible it uses piolium, as for Ollama and Gemini.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIIEI3TO\nPlP4Y6xMcLs9ActC2Rsfebm3HxweoNUuYL9zU2G80eSguOtpfEx/wjkGvf/BWRkdtOUtsmQLm8CU\nxQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:00:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clau