-09-30T19:41:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:41:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Drop the unused openai package\n\nreNgine/llm.py imported openai (0.28.0, 2023) but every provider call goes\nthrough requests; nothing in web/ uses the SDK and no installed package\nrequires it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"186923cbaf079887763cf0f5a6c133a09d5ee1d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/186923cbaf079887763cf0f5a6c133a09d5ee1d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/1501286d79419dc2eb3081e66825a056ed4e5daf","verification":{"payload":"tree 186923cbaf079887763cf0f5a6c133a09d5ee1d8\nparent 28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790797275 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790797275 +0000\n\nDrop the unused openai package\n\nreNgine/llm.py imported openai (0.28.0, 2023) but every provider call goes\nthrough requests; nothing in web/ uses the SDK and no installed package\nrequires it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNQ5/y63\nLJ+nF9Z/6JNnrvmPGF8DWk2jm9lmrr5bEZU8wMfV7EpUZecSGvIPNp1RsFbq8X/9bvyOCr7AhUN8\nzQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T20:00:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/1501286d79419dc2eb3081e66825a056ed4e5daf","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDE1MDEyODZkNzk0MTlkYzJlYjMwODFlNjY4MjVhMDU2ZWQ0ZTVkYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8","sha":"28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8"}],"sha":"1501286d79419dc2eb3081e66825a056ed4e5daf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/1501286d79419dc2eb3081e66825a056ed4e5daf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:12:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:12:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Load missing Vigolium settings with the backend''s defaults\n\nWith a Vigolium section or key missing, the tasks fall back to their own\ndefaults (harvest 30/100/60s, discovery 40/100/30s, the Tier 6 scan''s\ntimeout 300s), but the editor loaded 20/50/10s and 15s and wrote them on\nsave, so saving an engine unchanged shortened those runs. The form''s\nfallbacks and new-engine defaults now match the tasks. Built-in engines\nset these keys explicitly and are unaffected.\n\nDrops the TODO entry about the editor losing amass_intel_discovery, baddns\nand post_crawl_osint: unknown top-level keys are carried through since\n001a901, and the three now have cards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"ca6ebcbb944bfb48d0aafe909cda068f193848e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/ca6ebcbb944bfb48d0aafe909cda068f193848e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8","verification":{"payload":"tree ca6ebcbb944bfb48d0aafe909cda068f193848e0\nparent 2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790795561 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790795561 +0000\n\nLoad missing Vigolium settings with the backend''s defaults\n\nWith a Vigolium section or key missing, the tasks fall back to their own\ndefaults (harvest 30/100/60s, discovery 40/100/30s, the Tier 6 scan''s\ntimeout 300s), but the editor loaded 20/50/10s and 15s and wrote them on\nsave, so saving an engine unchanged shortened those runs. The form''s\nfallbacks and new-engine defaults now match the tasks. Built-in engines\nset these keys explicitly and are unaffected.\n\nDrops the TODO entry about the editor losing amass_intel_discovery, baddns\nand post_crawl_osint: unknown top-level keys are carried through since\n001a901, and the three now have cards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQESkZktg\nK9y2K0iuL9XSn6NhV+3/Zk3VwZtw4Kvah2P5U+jZpqYRWEbvYicpX/1inQGt6bj6ZKLWZTsBBn+9\nWgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T19:12:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDI4MjU1ZWI3ZWE4MTM0YWQ2NjI4OGZlYjI0OTk5MTFhOGExZjQzYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd","sha":"2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd"}],"sha":"28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/28255eb7ea8134ad66288feb2499911a8a1f43a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:04:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:06:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Expose the OSINT and discovery switches the backend reads\n\nNew cards:\n- Post-Crawl OSINT (Tier 4a): post_crawl_osint.metagoofil (exifray\n  document metadata) and .swaggerspy (path probe of live subdomains).\n- Amass Intel (Tier 1): the amass_intel_discovery key schedules it;\n  use_amass_config is now read from that section, falling back to\n  subdomain_discovery.use_amass_config.\n- BadDNS (Tier 1): the top-level baddns key runs the standalone step. The\n  card explains how it differs from baddns in the subdomain discovery\n  tools and warns, with a one-click fix, when both would run it at once.\n\nOSINT card gains the keys osint_discovery and dorking read: emailfinder,\nmicrosoft_recon, misconfig, domain_security.spoofcheck,\napi_leaks.{porch_pirate,postleaks,swaggerspy}, dork_engines and\ngithub_analysis (uses_tools, gato, github_orgs).\n\nBugs:\n- post_crawl_osint was missing from the task plan: no timeline row, its\n  retry rows filed under Tier 7, and a resume dropped it.\n- Structured custom dorks (lookup_site mappings, as in the built-in OSINT\n  engine) reached the tag input as objects; they are now kept as written.\n- The OSINT intensity select only ever skipped the metainfo lookup for\n  anything but normal; it is gone and the stale value is no longer saved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"d3d06ab88b1f2e35dfd3f7e49306fec3cdb00c0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/d3d06ab88b1f2e35dfd3f7e49306fec3cdb00c0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd","verification":{"payload":"tree d3d06ab88b1f2e35dfd3f7e49306fec3cdb00c0e\nparent f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790795053 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790795173 +0000\n\nExpose the OSINT and discovery switches the backend reads\n\nNew cards:\n- Post-Crawl OSINT (Tier 4a): post_crawl_osint.metagoofil (exifray\n  document metadata) and .swaggerspy (path probe of live subdomains).\n- Amass Intel (Tier 1): the amass_intel_discovery key schedules it;\n  use_amass_config is now read from that section, falling back to\n  subdomain_discovery.use_amass_config.\n- BadDNS (Tier 1): the top-level baddns key runs the standalone step. The\n  card explains how it differs from baddns in the subdomain discovery\n  tools and warns, with a one-click fix, when both would run it at once.\n\nOSINT card gains the keys osint_discovery and dorking read: emailfinder,\nmicrosoft_recon, misconfig, domain_security.spoofcheck,\napi_leaks.{porch_pirate,postleaks,swaggerspy}, dork_engines and\ngithub_analysis (uses_tools, gato, github_orgs).\n\nBugs:\n- post_crawl_osint was missing from the task plan: no timeline row, its\n  retry rows filed under Tier 7, and a resume dropped it.\n- Structured custom dorks (lookup_site mappings, as in the built-in OSINT\n  engine) reached the tag input as objects; they are now kept as written.\n- The OSINT intensity select only ever skipped the metainfo lookup for\n  anything but normal; it is gone and the stale value is no longer saved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM2pk6zo\nX51XV/Do/g5ugll79oRx7TItIVI2VohtFaOkyXLrpsWiIyWitqObEasr0MT64IrSpU0kXuuUshu6\n8gY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T19:12:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDJmMWE4ODM4NDA4NzIzMGU0MWE1ZjkzNWJlZWJiZWQ5ZGNhMDJiY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4","sha":"f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4"}],"sha":"2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/2f1a88384087230e41a5f935beebbed9dca02bcd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:04:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:04:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Expose the dalfox, s3scanner and nuclei options the scan reads\n\nThe Vulnerability Scan card gets option blocks for the scanner keys the\ntasks read, each with the task''s own default so saving an engine unchanged\ndoes not change the scan:\n\n- Dalfox (vulnerability_scan.dalfox): WAF evasion, deep scan, remote\n  payloads/wordlists, scan timeout, blind XSS server, user agent, request\n  timeout, delay and workers.\n- S3Scanner (vulnerability_scan.s3scanner): providers and threads.\n- Nuclei: template update switch and max_templates_per_batch.\n\nBugs:\n- dalfox read DEEP_SCAN / REMOTE_PAYLOADS / REMOTE_WORDLISTS / SCAN_TIMEOUT\n  in uppercase while the reference YAML writes them lowercase, so those\n  settings never applied. It now reads lowercase first, uppercase after.\n- A dalfox user agent or blind XSS server went unquoted into a bash\n  command; a browser user agent broke it. Both are shell-quoted now.\n- cPanel proxy type \"static\" meant nothing to the task, which knows\n  \"single\"; the form offers single, loads static as single, and the task\n  accepts both.\n- The cPanel wordlist default pointed at a file nothing creates; it is now\n  the one the entrypoints download, and a missing configured file falls\n  back to it.\n- The card''s Timeout field wrote vulnerability_scan.timeout, which no task\n  uses; it is gone and a hand-set value is kept. Concurrency, rate limit,\n  retries and intensity now load the engine-wide value when the section\n  has none, as the tasks do.\n\nThe card''s scanner blocks move into their own components.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"72094ebdfbfb88446ac14f92a993265e7b7bed04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/72094ebdfbfb88446ac14f92a993265e7b7bed04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4","verification":{"payload":"tree 72094ebdfbfb88446ac14f92a993265e7b7bed04\nparent a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790795040 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790795077 +0000\n\nExpose the dalfox, s3scanner and nuclei options the scan reads\n\nThe Vulnerability Scan card gets option blocks for the scanner keys the\ntasks read, each with the task''s own default so saving an engine unchanged\ndoes not change the scan:\n\n- Dalfox (vulnerability_scan.dalfox): WAF evasion, deep scan, remote\n  payloads/wordlists, scan timeout, blind XSS server, user agent, request\n  timeout, delay and workers.\n- S3Scanner (vulnerability_scan.s3scanner): providers and threads.\n- Nuclei: template update switch and max_templates_per_batch.\n\nBugs:\n- dalfox read DEEP_SCAN / REMOTE_PAYLOADS / REMOTE_WORDLISTS / SCAN_TIMEOUT\n  in uppercase while the reference YAML writes them lowercase, so those\n  settings never applied. It now reads lowercase first, uppercase after.\n- A dalfox user agent or blind XSS server went unquoted into a bash\n  command; a browser user agent broke it. Both are shell-quoted now.\n- cPanel proxy type \"static\" meant nothing to the task, which knows\n  \"single\"; the form offers single, loads static as single, and the task\n  accepts both.\n- The cPanel wordlist default pointed at a file nothing creates; it is now\n  the one the entrypoints download, and a missing configured file falls\n  back to it.\n- The card''s Timeout field wrote vulnerability_scan.timeout, which no task\n  uses; it is gone and a hand-set value is kept. Concurrency, rate limit,\n  retries and intensity now load the engine-wide value when the section\n  has none, as the tasks do.\n\nThe card''s scanner blocks move into their own components.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPgtFbYn\nOZ2P8h3Rgt3dhNWFwzhNK/WknZXVztjiC/CYj6YQ01OHdlAXXiUXr3DQ8PnW0K3taDfXZ6mxGWsG\nXwI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T19:12:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGY4YjIyNDQwMGRjMDg5MWMzMzI0YmY0MjdhYzhmMTY0ZTNiZGFhZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e","sha":"a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e"}],"sha":"f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f8b224400dc0891c3324bf427ac8f164e3bdaaf4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:35:57Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:35:57Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make the engine editor''s switches match what the scan runs\n\nBugs:\n- Vigolium Harvest/Discovery/Analysis (and the Code Scan audit) ran with\n  their card off: the form dropped the section, and the backend runs a\n  missing one. Off now writes run_vigolium_*: false, and a missing section\n  loads as on.\n- Saving from the form deleted osint.leaks_and_secrets, which the OSINT\n  pipeline reads, and the old leaks_and_secrets.run_semgrep.\n\nDead settings removed or wired to the key that is read:\n- LeakLookup moved from secret scanning, where nothing read it, to OSINT\n  with LeakSearch; secret scanning gets Betterleaks.\n- CredSpy now schedules the post-crawl OSINT step it runs in.\n- Screenshot and WAF Bypass lose fields the tasks never read, subdomain\n  discovery its bbot box (bbot only runs in subscans); hand-set values\n  are kept.\n- SpiderFoot offers the normal/fast/deep intensities it reads.\n- Attack path modeling can be switched off (attack_path_modeling.enabled).\n- Tier 7 appears in the tab view too.\n\nNew switches for existing backend options: react2shell, post-scan\nprocessing and semgrep (vulnerability_scan.run_semgrep, the old key still\nread), network enumeration in port scan, testssl and crt.sh in\nfirewall/VPN, the DNS security checks, and inql.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"d86caf3b401650b267c4fff9205d072e2def7e04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/d86caf3b401650b267c4fff9205d072e2def7e04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e","verification":{"payload":"tree d86caf3b401650b267c4fff9205d072e2def7e04\nparent e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790793357 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790793357 +0000\n\nMake the engine editor''s switches match what the scan runs\n\nBugs:\n- Vigolium Harvest/Discovery/Analysis (and the Code Scan audit) ran with\n  their card off: the form dropped the section, and the backend runs a\n  missing one. Off now writes run_vigolium_*: false, and a missing section\n  loads as on.\n- Saving from the form deleted osint.leaks_and_secrets, which the OSINT\n  pipeline reads, and the old leaks_and_secrets.run_semgrep.\n\nDead settings removed or wired to the key that is read:\n- LeakLookup moved from secret scanning, where nothing read it, to OSINT\n  with LeakSearch; secret scanning gets Betterleaks.\n- CredSpy now schedules the post-crawl OSINT step it runs in.\n- Screenshot and WAF Bypass lose fields the tasks never read, subdomain\n  discovery its bbot box (bbot only runs in subscans); hand-set values\n  are kept.\n- SpiderFoot offers the normal/fast/deep intensities it reads.\n- Attack path modeling can be switched off (attack_path_modeling.enabled).\n- Tier 7 appears in the tab view too.\n\nNew switches for existing backend options: react2shell, post-scan\nprocessing and semgrep (vulnerability_scan.run_semgrep, the old key still\nread), network enumeration in port scan, testssl and crt.sh in\nfirewall/VPN, the DNS security checks, and inql.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA+DERcP\neFrYjl+MaTKYrqVVmwL0SIUwdDn4TP6vb5ydAjuOdy+dgv+RcpcO1XS84PKSZeOjMo8WI2zqcoib\nMQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:36:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGE0ZjVlZmUwZDE3MzVhNGI3NjJlZjdmNzM4ZDUzZTA3YjI4MTU2MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58","sha":"e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58"}],"sha":"a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/a4f5efe0d1735a4b762ef7f738d53e07b281562e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:10:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:10:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make ffuf a choice in directory fuzzing\n\nffuf always ran and the engine card showed it as a disabled box. run_ffuf\n(default true, so existing engines behave as before) now switches it like\nrun_dirsearch and run_feroxbuster. With all three off the step logs a\nwarning and returns before crawling endpoints or creating DirectoryScan rows,\nand the card warns about it. A single-tool run of dir_file_fuzz still runs\nffuf, since its CLI arguments are ffuf''s.\n\nThe engine list''s tool count follows run_ffuf and now counts feroxbuster.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"6e0b2e5041bf98b5de9d0fea24d32922ea03f00b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/6e0b2e5041bf98b5de9d0fea24d32922ea03f00b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e0b2e5041bf98b5de9d0fea24d32922ea03f00b\nparent 82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790791827 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790791827 +0000\n\nMake ffuf a choice in directory fuzzing\n\nffuf always ran and the engine card showed it as a disabled box. run_ffuf\n(default true, so existing engines behave as before) now switches it like\nrun_dirsearch and run_feroxbuster. With all three off the step logs a\nwarning and returns before crawling endpoints or creating DirectoryScan rows,\nand the card warns about it. A single-tool run of dir_file_fuzz still runs\nffuf, since its CLI arguments are ffuf''s.\n\nThe engine list''s tool count follows run_ffuf and now counts feroxbuster.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEKCJMsc\nvoohydzwFN0VlsVw/yAm3zy1zzjU0I28gA+3MkgCibM+mJ0DE3ObOodEiZx+WQOMdFdHFlsE1LA4\nnQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:10:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGU2YmFjYjQzNjI3YjI0NTZjNjIxNjA1OTliM2Y2MzYxMjVlYWVmNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f","sha":"82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f"}],"sha":"e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/e6bacb43627b2456c62160599b3f636125eaef58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:58:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:58:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Spend ffuf''s time on the requests a dirsearch wordlist means\n\nThe default wordlist is dirsearch''s dicc: 9680 words, 558 with a %EXT%\nplaceholder. ffuf got it with -e for every configured extension, so it\nappended each extension to every word and sent the %EXT% lines literally:\n212,960 requests per target with the default extensions, of which the\n300 s max_time covered about a fifth.\n\n- A wordlist with %EXT% is expanded once per scan into the shared results\n  volume: each placeholder word once per extension, other words as-is,\n  duplicates dropped. ffuf and feroxbuster use it without -e/--extensions\n  (20,003 requests per target for the defaults). Plain wordlists keep -e.\n- dirsearch is off by default in the code, the built-in engines and the\n  editor: it repeated ffuf''s requests on every target. It stays available.\n- Duplicate extensions are dropped (fixtures listed ''conf'' twice, which cost\n  ffuf a full extra pass), and the editor''s tag input ignores them.\n- The Dir/File Fuzz card and docs say what runs: ffuf on every target,\n  dirsearch and feroxbuster as optional extra passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"9cded74c0d0a48b12eabf5363c8c35497c5d8a42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/9cded74c0d0a48b12eabf5363c8c35497c5d8a42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cded74c0d0a48b12eabf5363c8c35497c5d8a42\nparent 73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790791097 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790791097 +0000\n\nSpend ffuf''s time on the requests a dirsearch wordlist means\n\nThe default wordlist is dirsearch''s dicc: 9680 words, 558 with a %EXT%\nplaceholder. ffuf got it with -e for every configured extension, so it\nappended each extension to every word and sent the %EXT% lines literally:\n212,960 requests per target with the default extensions, of which the\n300 s max_time covered about a fifth.\n\n- A wordlist with %EXT% is expanded once per scan into the shared results\n  volume: each placeholder word once per extension, other words as-is,\n  duplicates dropped. ffuf and feroxbuster use it without -e/--extensions\n  (20,003 requests per target for the defaults). Plain wordlists keep -e.\n- dirsearch is off by default in the code, the built-in engines and the\n  editor: it repeated ffuf''s requests on every target. It stays available.\n- Duplicate extensions are dropped (fixtures listed ''conf'' twice, which cost\n  ffuf a full extra pass), and the editor''s tag input ignores them.\n- The Dir/File Fuzz card and docs say what runs: ffuf on every target,\n  dirsearch and feroxbuster as optional extra passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH7XcfP3\nu7DdodFcFDSCuSTb7bYRhp1l/zk/q8aKOG0JhM4ppXCaVm+vPhNinAPYMChlZ8MYB2AkvcBJKIqM\n8Qo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:58:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDgyZDgzYTNlNzY4YmEwMzY4NzE2NmM5ZDY4ODA0YTNiYTU4ZDAzMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d","sha":"73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d"}],"sha":"82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/82d83a3e768ba03687166c9d68804a3ba58d030f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:34:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:34:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Resolve the hardware profile per step and add the switch for it\n\nThe code for the previous commit, whose message describes this change but\nwhich only carried the test-file rename: git add aborted on a stale path.\n\n- TemporalTaskProxy resolves the profile when each activity starts, from the\n  scan row it already loads, falling back to the workflow input only when\n  the scan or every profile is gone. Workflows are unchanged.\n- POST /api/action/scan/<id>/hardware-profile/ (same permission as\n  stop/pause) and a selector next to STOP on the scan detail page for\n  pending, running and paused scans.\n- Precedence: tool section value, then the profile, then the engine''s\n  global value, which the editor always writes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"dd1317b96eba1829dbe170a2382b2aea20d5f025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/dd1317b96eba1829dbe170a2382b2aea20d5f025"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d","verification":{"payload":"tree dd1317b96eba1829dbe170a2382b2aea20d5f025\nparent b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790789643 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790789643 +0000\n\nResolve the hardware profile per step and add the switch for it\n\nThe code for the previous commit, whose message describes this change but\nwhich only carried the test-file rename: git add aborted on a stale path.\n\n- TemporalTaskProxy resolves the profile when each activity starts, from the\n  scan row it already loads, falling back to the workflow input only when\n  the scan or every profile is gone. Workflows are unchanged.\n- POST /api/action/scan/<id>/hardware-profile/ (same permission as\n  stop/pause) and a selector next to STOP on the scan detail page for\n  pending, running and paused scans.\n- Precedence: tool section value, then the profile, then the engine''s\n  global value, which the editor always writes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHZgPr9w\ntPeDVZn7SnvQ6ECkuUl0vWJNbsEnq0mNetwVeOuqXrLZWmZzWJPQA60M+/aBOiH86MXfpQRROcn+\n/Qs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:34:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDczZjQ4NDU5MmFkYWU0ZmY1NmFhZTQwNjIyYTQxOWI0OTM5M2MyMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78","sha":"b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78"}],"sha":"73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/73f484592adae4ff56aae40622a419b49393c20d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:33:46Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:33:46Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Let a running scan switch its hardware profile\n\nThe profile was resolved once at scan start and frozen in the workflow\ninput, so a scan started on the small default profile ran every step with\nit, and there was no way to change that short of restarting the scan.\n\n- TemporalTaskProxy resolves the profile when each activity starts, from the\n  scan row it already loads (hardware_profile joined in), falling back to the\n  workflow input only when the scan or every profile is gone. Workflows are\n  unchanged.\n- POST /api/action/scan/<id>/hardware-profile/ sets it, with the same\n  permission as stop/pause; the scan detail page has a selector next to STOP\n  for pending, running and paused scans. Steps that start afterwards use it;\n  tools already running keep their settings.\n- Precedence is now: tool section value, then the profile, then the engine''s\n  global value. The engine editor always writes the global limits, so with\n  the global value ahead of the profile the profile picked for a scan only\n  ever set its delay.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"ce0e388f578ed5fc9465e91c9a56cee4116d0e14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/ce0e388f578ed5fc9465e91c9a56cee4116d0e14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78","verification":{"payload":"tree ce0e388f578ed5fc9465e91c9a56cee4116d0e14\nparent f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790789626 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790789626 +0000\n\nLet a running scan switch its hardware profile\n\nThe profile was resolved once at scan start and frozen in the workflow\ninput, so a scan started on the small default profile ran every step with\nit, and there was no way to change that short of restarting the scan.\n\n- TemporalTaskProxy resolves the profile when each activity starts, from the\n  scan row it already loads (hardware_profile joined in), falling back to the\n  workflow input only when the scan or every profile is gone. Workflows are\n  unchanged.\n- POST /api/action/scan/<id>/hardware-profile/ sets it, with the same\n  permission as stop/pause; the scan detail page has a selector next to STOP\n  for pending, running and paused scans. Steps that start afterwards use it;\n  tools already running keep their settings.\n- Precedence is now: tool section value, then the profile, then the engine''s\n  global value. The engine editor always writes the global limits, so with\n  the global value ahead of the profile the profile picked for a scan only\n  ever set its delay.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD07jiP9\nhLOpU2SsCRrqsiemWgqanEXCNtunUpdMO9cOCbdcHJ2EUrON1C5bxMXrzumVXTWDD6ucQbl7j7fx\nIwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:33:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGIwNjAwODI2MjFmMDFmNDY3YTFlMTJlMDVmMTA4MzQ0ODFjOGFjNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a","sha":"f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a"}],"sha":"b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/b060082621f01f467a1e12e05f10834481c8ac78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:26:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:26:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Keep LinkFinder''s JS pass in scope and bounded\n\n- JS downloads go to <scan results>/linkfinder_js/, outside\n  web_api_discovery/, which Semgrep and Retire.js scan: vendor bundles were\n  reported as SAST findings with container paths as their URL.\n- lf_*.txt now holds only de-duplicated in-scope absolute URLs. The CPDE\n  collector reads it too, and was attaching analytics query keys from\n  third-party URLs to the target.\n- Each download has a 30 s wall-clock deadline, checked after every socket\n  read (urllib3 2''s read1; iter_content on 1.26), and each subdomain a 120 s\n  budget. A server trickling bytes could otherwise hold one file, and every\n  retry, until the activity timed out.\n- A malformed host such as \"http://[x/\" is noise instead of a ValueError that\n  dropped the rest of the file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"054cb37f84c2248a47957f056820ee20f8d7e7c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/054cb37f84c2248a47957f056820ee20f8d7e7c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a","verification":{"payload":"tree 054cb37f84c2248a47957f056820ee20f8d7e7c0\nparent 0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790789186 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790789186 +0000\n\nKeep LinkFinder''s JS pass in scope and bounded\n\n- JS downloads go to <scan results>/linkfinder_js/, outside\n  web_api_discovery/, which Semgrep and Retire.js scan: vendor bundles were\n  reported as SAST findings with container paths as their URL.\n- lf_*.txt now holds only de-duplicated in-scope absolute URLs. The CPDE\n  collector reads it too, and was attaching analytics query keys from\n  third-party URLs to the target.\n- Each download has a 30 s wall-clock deadline, checked after every socket\n  read (urllib3 2''s read1; iter_content on 1.26), and each subdomain a 120 s\n  budget. A server trickling bytes could otherwise hold one file, and every\n  retry, until the activity timed out.\n- A malformed host such as \"http://[x/\" is noise instead of a ValueError that\n  dropped the rest of the file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP1BE+KE\nACRBmaOIM+IEyloCcApMPU54IQK0BFyM8ykGkr+zckZui8y4ZgP2QxqDn2w/CAYLzAqyP/w200AH\n1AI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:33:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGY3MzQyNTQ1OWQ2NDVlYmZkMGZmMGZhYTQ2MmY1ZWZiMDRkZGYxMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433","sha":"0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433"}],"sha":"f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f73425459d645ebfd0ff0faa462f5efb04ddf12a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:21:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:21:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Accept bare hostnames in save_endpoint and retry each kiterunner wordlist\n\nsave_endpoint''s host check parsed a scheme-less ''host[/path]'' as having no\nhost, so the subscan starter''s root endpoint was rejected and never\ncrawled. Bare hosts are parsed as network locations again, a trailing dot on\nthe Domain name is ignored, and a malformed URL is skipped instead of\nraising ValueError into the caller.\n\nThe kiterunner wordlist download was keyed on routes-small only, so a failed\nroutes-large was never retried, and a failed tar could leave a truncated\nfile behind. Each list is now fetched on its own into a temp directory and\nmoved into place only once extracted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"4d83e41ff779c897cd305331440a06742d0d7369","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/4d83e41ff779c897cd305331440a06742d0d7369"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d83e41ff779c897cd305331440a06742d0d7369\nparent 001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790788914 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790788914 +0000\n\nAccept bare hostnames in save_endpoint and retry each kiterunner wordlist\n\nsave_endpoint''s host check parsed a scheme-less ''host[/path]'' as having no\nhost, so the subscan starter''s root endpoint was rejected and never\ncrawled. Bare hosts are parsed as network locations again, a trailing dot on\nthe Domain name is ignored, and a malformed URL is skipped instead of\nraising ValueError into the caller.\n\nThe kiterunner wordlist download was keyed on routes-small only, so a failed\nroutes-large was never retried, and a failed tar could leave a truncated\nfile behind. Each list is now fetched on its own into a temp directory and\nmoved into place only once extracted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG1FGmJs\nP6baohO44ez4Sk6oMx2zOsrIeGoJe7jiiaKX8PAtCiFe+u3icFc++6sIuhw7vrSZ0Ylf6eb/o630\nVg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:21:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDBiZjJjYjkxZjBlMjcwMzM1NDg0MjU5OWQ1ODM0OGVjMDI1MzA0MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0","sha":"001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0"}],"sha":"0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/0bf2cb91f0e2703354842599d58348ec02530433"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:21:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:21:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Keep unknown keys inside engine sections across editor saves\n\nOnly top-level keys the form doesn''t know survived a save; a key a newer\nbackend reads inside port_scan, or nuclei settings the form has no field for\n(max_templates_per_batch, concurrency), were dropped whenever the form\nrewrote the section.\n\nFORM_OWNED_KEYS now lists, per mapping, every key the form reads or writes.\nEverything else is carried under what the form writes, but only into a\nmapping the form actually wrote, so an owned key it leaves out (nmap options\nwith nmap off, a disabled section) stays out. A guard test fills every form\nfield and fails if the serialiser writes a key missing from the table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"e281b810da5fe769e7b810b0b8adc8a41ac50255","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/e281b810da5fe769e7b810b0b8adc8a41ac50255"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0","verification":{"payload":"tree e281b810da5fe769e7b810b0b8adc8a41ac50255\nparent abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790788914 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790788914 +0000\n\nKeep unknown keys inside engine sections across editor saves\n\nOnly top-level keys the form doesn''t know survived a save; a key a newer\nbackend reads inside port_scan, or nuclei settings the form has no field for\n(max_templates_per_batch, concurrency), were dropped whenever the form\nrewrote the section.\n\nFORM_OWNED_KEYS now lists, per mapping, every key the form reads or writes.\nEverything else is carried under what the form writes, but only into a\nmapping the form actually wrote, so an owned key it leaves out (nmap options\nwith nmap off, a disabled section) stays out. A guard test fills every form\nfield and fails if the serialiser writes a key missing from the table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI4ZZioK\nTrTSLyoKQgT4g+zD1xBNybkSs9dmQ5h17GjG5uVNfV4cp8CWUp5aXB66VaQl9rewDViOT/vDrWC6\nvgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:21:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDAwMWE5MDEwMDQyNjVjNzhmMjUzM2NlODc5NzAxMWUxOWRiZmM0YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af","sha":"abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af"}],"sha":"001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/001a901004265c78f2533ce8797011e19dbfc4a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:14:48Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:14:48Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Test where naabu''s -rate comes from\n\nThe engine editor writes port_scan.rate_limit; the legacy port_scan.rate key\nand the engine''s global rate_limit remain the override and the fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"71ecdb791009b83c3eadef78e39da896cea1df7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/71ecdb791009b83c3eadef78e39da896cea1df7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af","verification":{"payload":"tree 71ecdb791009b83c3eadef78e39da896cea1df7f\nparent f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790788488 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790788488 +0000\n\nTest where naabu''s -rate comes from\n\nThe engine editor writes port_scan.rate_limit; the legacy port_scan.rate key\nand the engine''s global rate_limit remain the override and the fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGkssztE\nsUBHu2+clKnXaiREGG8ivDu6cs5E8cQmbU7EYZnMWZvIHzb94BrOdgOUeyWgZYTSesoYPhJXWgkj\nfgI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:14:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGFiYjhjZWMyN2E4MjhlYjZjMGM0MWU5MGM2ZTdkMjljZDY1NWE3YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96","sha":"f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96"}],"sha":"abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/abb8cec27a828eb6c0c41e90c6e7d29cd655a7af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:04:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:04:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix the regressions in the scan engine fixes and cover them with tests\n\nThe previous commit broke CI and shipped several behavioural bugs:\n\n- Engine editor: the whole loaded YAML was used as the serialiser''s base, so a\n  section switched off, a global reset to its default, or the old\n  leaks_and_secrets spelling came back on save. Only top-level keys the form\n  does not own are carried through now, kept in a ref instead of state set\n  from inside another updater. Tier 7 settings are written at all for the\n  first time (correlation.py reads tier_7.high_noise_modules).\n- LinkFinder: scope was the page host minus its first label, so scanning\n  example.com put every *.com host in scope and created Subdomain rows for\n  them. Scope is now the scan''s Domain; new in-scope hosts go through\n  save_subdomain (out-of-scope list, validation) and own their endpoints.\n  JS downloads stream with a size cap, no redirects, the proxy pool, and\n  narrowed, logged exceptions. lf_output only appears once both passes are\n  done, so a retry does not skip the JS-file pass.\n- Hardware profile: a section without a value got the profile''s value ahead\n  of the engine''s global one. Precedence is now section, engine global,\n  profile.\n- save_endpoint compares against the lower-cased domain name.\n- CPDE collector tests wrote tool output to the scan root; they now use\n  web_api_discovery/ as the task does, plus a test that the root is ignored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"2d58de4255bab847f3a3ec8c9dddd8b0d1d6d844","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/2d58de4255bab847f3a3ec8c9dddd8b0d1d6d844"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d58de4255bab847f3a3ec8c9dddd8b0d1d6d844\nparent 6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790787844 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790787844 +0000\n\nFix the regressions in the scan engine fixes and cover them with tests\n\nThe previous commit broke CI and shipped several behavioural bugs:\n\n- Engine editor: the whole loaded YAML was used as the serialiser''s base, so a\n  section switched off, a global reset to its default, or the old\n  leaks_and_secrets spelling came back on save. Only top-level keys the form\n  does not own are carried through now, kept in a ref instead of state set\n  from inside another updater. Tier 7 settings are written at all for the\n  first time (correlation.py reads tier_7.high_noise_modules).\n- LinkFinder: scope was the page host minus its first label, so scanning\n  example.com put every *.com host in scope and created Subdomain rows for\n  them. Scope is now the scan''s Domain; new in-scope hosts go through\n  save_subdomain (out-of-scope list, validation) and own their endpoints.\n  JS downloads stream with a size cap, no redirects, the proxy pool, and\n  narrowed, logged exceptions. lf_output only appears once both passes are\n  done, so a retry does not skip the JS-file pass.\n- Hardware profile: a section without a value got the profile''s value ahead\n  of the engine''s global one. Precedence is now section, engine global,\n  profile.\n- save_endpoint compares against the lower-cased domain name.\n- CPDE collector tests wrote tool output to the scan root; they now use\n  web_api_discovery/ as the task does, plus a test that the root is ignored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGhE70Vr\nWsPhJ3ivG2lUXJnhyR3axPakYmQC78ytM6phd4MwpF++8z168R0aE+Avlny21CtbHEOsCqaw00G5\nJQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:04:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGY5MjA3ZDRkODIyN2U2YTM4YjQ1NTU2MGYxNDZiZjA0YzM3MjZjOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837","sha":"6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837"}],"sha":"f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f9207d4d8227e6a38b455560f146bf04c3726c96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:45:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:45:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix scan engine, CPDE paths, LinkFinder, and hardware profile\n\n- Hardware profile (core.py): values are now defaults only — explicit\n  engine YAML values take precedence. Previously the profile\n  unconditionally overwrote every section''s threads/rate_limit/delay.\n\n- Port scan (port_scan.py): also read rate_limit key from section config\n  (engine editor writes rate_limit; code was reading the legacy ''rate'' key).\n\n- CPDE path bug (url_param_collector.py): arjun_*, kr_*, lf_*.txt and\n  paramspider results are all written to web_api_discovery/ — collectors\n  now look there instead of the scan root.\n\n- Acunetix (acunetix.py): when start_scan_on_submit=True but the scan\n  fails to start, log FAILED and return False instead of SUBMITTED.\n\n- save_endpoint (utils/task.py): replace substring domain check with\n  urlparse hostname comparison (security rule 3.1).\n\n- LinkFinder (api_discovery.py):\n  - Second pass: query DB for JS endpoints already crawled, download each,\n    run linkfinder against local copy — bypasses 403 on the HTML page.\n  - Improved parser: handle //host/path (protocol-relative), relative\n    paths; discovered new subdomains are added to Subdomain model.\n  - External hosts silently dropped.\n\n- Kiterunner wordlist (entrypoint.sh): use file-existence check instead\n  of directory check; each wget/tar is chained so failures are visible.\n  api_discovery.py now logs a clear error if the wordlist file is absent.\n\n- Frontend (useEngineConfig.ts): preserve unknown YAML keys across\n  save/reload by storing the raw parsed object and passing it as a\n  passthrough base into the serializer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"a96ba539c9b8b2bf26260bd19f7c9a2f77fcbf61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/a96ba539c9b8b2bf26260bd19f7c9a2f77fcbf61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837","verification":{"payload":"tree a96ba539c9b8b2bf26260bd19f7c9a2f77fcbf61\nparent 73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790786752 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790786752 +0000\n\nFix scan engine, CPDE paths, LinkFinder, and hardware profile\n\n- Hardware profile (core.py): values are now defaults only — explicit\n  engine YAML values take precedence. Previously the profile\n  unconditionally overwrote every section''s threads/rate_limit/delay.\n\n- Port scan (port_scan.py): also read rate_limit key from section config\n  (engine editor writes rate_limit; code was reading the legacy ''rate'' key).\n\n- CPDE path bug (url_param_collector.py): arjun_*, kr_*, lf_*.txt and\n  paramspider results are all written to web_api_discovery/ — collectors\n  now look there instead of the scan root.\n\n- Acunetix (acunetix.py): when start_scan_on_submit=True but the scan\n  fails to start, log FAILED and return False instead of SUBMITTED.\n\n- save_endpoint (utils/task.py): replace substring domain check with\n  urlparse hostname comparison (security rule 3.1).\n\n- LinkFinder (api_discovery.py):\n  - Second pass: query DB for JS endpoints already crawled, download each,\n    run linkfinder against local copy — bypasses 403 on the HTML page.\n  - Improved parser: handle //host/path (protocol-relative), relative\n    paths; discovered new subdomains are added to Subdomain model.\n  - External hosts silently dropped.\n\n- Kiterunner wordlist (entrypoint.sh): use file-existence check instead\n  of directory check; each wget/tar is chained so failures are visible.\n  api_discovery.py now logs a clear error if the wordlist file is absent.\n\n- Frontend (useEngineConfig.ts): preserve unknown YAML keys across\n  save/reload by storing the raw parsed object and passing it as a\n  passthrough base into the serializer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLEYd7Lk\nmAs8RsxSTpUA2tTXiqRdhgD/rxCOCyKGvMwf/MQX/Z0fZFFoaaNfj4OkBhggvPkLoHkYBF3hMZgd\nfAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T16:45:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDZhMzBhNzE4NzY3YTBlZmJhYmMxOWUwMWQ2OGM5ZDYzYmViM2I4Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3","sha":"73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3"}],"sha":"6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6a30a718767a0efbabc19e01d68c9d63beb3b837"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:23:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:23:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add an Email Security section to the engine editor\n\nThe email security step (SPF/DMARC/DKIM, relay, STARTTLS, Reacher mailbox\nverification) runs on every master scan with port_scan, because the backend\ntreats a missing email_security section as enabled. The engine form had no\nsection for it and rebuilt the YAML from known sections on load, so a\ndisable added through the YAML tab was dropped the next time the engine\nwas edited.\n\nThe new Tier 2 card toggles email_security.enabled and\nmailbox_verification.enabled and edits max_candidates, timeout, delay_ms\nand the optional Reacher http_url, clamped to the backend''s bounds. The\nserialiser always writes both enabled flags so switching off survives a\nreload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"e5e8abbf3d97c72c1448bcd3a1046f3aeeded518","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/e5e8abbf3d97c72c1448bcd3a1046f3aeeded518"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3","verification":{"payload":"tree e5e8abbf3d97c72c1448bcd3a1046f3aeeded518\nparent fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790785380 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790785380 +0000\n\nAdd an Email Security section to the engine editor\n\nThe email security step (SPF/DMARC/DKIM, relay, STARTTLS, Reacher mailbox\nverification) runs on every master scan with port_scan, because the backend\ntreats a missing email_security section as enabled. The engine form had no\nsection for it and rebuilt the YAML from known sections on load, so a\ndisable added through the YAML tab was dropped the next time the engine\nwas edited.\n\nThe new Tier 2 card toggles email_security.enabled and\nmailbox_verification.enabled and edits max_candidates, timeout, delay_ms\nand the optional Reacher http_url, clamped to the backend''s bounds. The\nserialiser always writes both enabled flags so switching off survives a\nreload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDUtgw4V\n2X6qlJcIIxqzKqsUAiJEaQzGvIcfJTqZVhddoXBGYm4CU70dUh4Fq7VwKZ53aO9B29ChBCk7xajL\nAwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T16:23:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDczZmQ1YTkzZDRlNzM1NTc3MWQzODdmNGU3MWIyNjJiZjcxNjA4YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a","sha":"fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a"}],"sha":"73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/73fd5a93d4e7355771d387f4e71b262bf71608b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:52:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:52:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Keep model instances out of SeedEndpointsForCrawlActivity''s result\n\nThe activity returns {**ctx, ''seed_urls'': ...}, and it passed that same\nctx to save_endpoint, which caches the Domain and ScanHistory instances\nin ctx[''_domain_obj''] / ctx[''_scan_obj'']. When the activity created at\nleast one endpoint, Temporal failed to serialise the result\n(\"Object of type Domain is not JSON serializable\") and retried it. The\nretry found the endpoints already there, skipped save_endpoint and\nsucceeded, so every first scan logged a traceback and an extra failed\nrow in the timeline.\n\nsave_endpoint now works on a copy of ctx, so its cache stays out of the\nreturned dict and is still reused across the subdomains of one call.\n\nFound on the first scan on the test server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"50705eafa8b5af97c8a91a0248ece35db4098554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/50705eafa8b5af97c8a91a0248ece35db4098554"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a","verification":{"payload":"tree 50705eafa8b5af97c8a91a0248ece35db4098554\nparent 106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790783527 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790783527 +0000\n\nKeep model instances out of SeedEndpointsForCrawlActivity''s result\n\nThe activity returns {**ctx, ''seed_urls'': ...}, and it passed that same\nctx to save_endpoint, which caches the Domain and ScanHistory instances\nin ctx[''_domain_obj''] / ctx[''_scan_obj'']. When the activity created at\nleast one endpoint, Temporal failed to serialise the result\n(\"Object of type Domain is not JSON serializable\") and retried it. The\nretry found the endpoints already there, skipped save_endpoint and\nsucceeded, so every first scan logged a traceback and an extra failed\nrow in the timeline.\n\nsave_endpoint now works on a copy of ctx, so its cache stays out of the\nreturned dict and is still reused across the subdomains of one call.\n\nFound on the first scan on the test server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQED6wVQa\nhlRdYySsezhJxs+D6gkOiqcsjPAMRvJAB3OfrDJyErYeqpeWHOYMFNCNGZEdqlLLb+S4W1yndDqe\nCQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T15:52:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGZkMjRhOGRkNDE2MjBjZjljMmJhZTExMGY5OWQ2ZDAzZTA1Y2ZkMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264","sha":"106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264"}],"sha":"fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/fd24a8dd41620cf9c2bae110f99d6d03e05cfd2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:40:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:40:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Run secret scanning for engines saved from the engine editor\n\nMasterScanWorkflow (and subscan/assessment) start the secret scanning\nstep only when the engine has a top-level `secret_scanning` section. The\nengine editor wrote that section as `leaks_and_secrets` and did not read\n`secret_scanning` at all. Since it rebuilds the YAML from the sections it\nknows, opening and saving a built-in engine dropped secret scanning, and\nan engine configured in the editor never ran it.\n\n- Editor: reads `secret_scanning` (after osint.leaks_and_secrets and\n  top-level leaks_and_secrets, which older saves use) and writes the\n  section back as `secret_scanning`.\n- EngineType.tasks: a top-level `leaks_and_secrets` without\n  `secret_scanning` also yields the `secret_scanning` task, so engines\n  already saved by the old editor run the step without being re-saved.\n  The step itself already falls back to the leaks_and_secrets settings.\n  This is resolved before the workflow starts, so running workflows are\n  not affected.\n- TODO: vigolium''s known-issue scan needs its own git checkout of\n  templates instead of the shared nuclei_templates volume; the editor\n  still drops amass_intel_discovery, baddns and post_crawl_osint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"486a78430affdc32df713eca2af4c04ba95825bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/486a78430affdc32df713eca2af4c04ba95825bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264","verification":{"payload":"tree 486a78430affdc32df713eca2af4c04ba95825bf\nparent 554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790782819 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790782819 +0000\n\nRun secret scanning for engines saved from the engine editor\n\nMasterScanWorkflow (and subscan/assessment) start the secret scanning\nstep only when the engine has a top-level `secret_scanning` section. The\nengine editor wrote that section as `leaks_and_secrets` and did not read\n`secret_scanning` at all. Since it rebuilds the YAML from the sections it\nknows, opening and saving a built-in engine dropped secret scanning, and\nan engine configured in the editor never ran it.\n\n- Editor: reads `secret_scanning` (after osint.leaks_and_secrets and\n  top-level leaks_and_secrets, which older saves use) and writes the\n  section back as `secret_scanning`.\n- EngineType.tasks: a top-level `leaks_and_secrets` without\n  `secret_scanning` also yields the `secret_scanning` task, so engines\n  already saved by the old editor run the step without being re-saved.\n  The step itself already falls back to the leaks_and_secrets settings.\n  This is resolved before the workflow starts, so running workflows are\n  not affected.\n- TODO: vigolium''s known-issue scan needs its own git checkout of\n  templates instead of the shared nuclei_templates volume; the editor\n  still drops amass_intel_discovery, baddns and post_crawl_osint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMKZ61gE\nSTRiNsL2A+3yRdUvCskk40hFxGiKOzO9Kih5SMa/W/+Cqi4tIGFj1DrduPXOrCrNOW1c5SoZWkcC\n8wk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T15:40:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDEwNmVhZTg3Y2U2ZWM5ZGY1MjViMGQ0OTI0ZWY0MGNhYzZlZGYyNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073","sha":"554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073"}],"sha":"106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/106eae87ce6ec9df525b0d4924ef40cac6edf264"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:30:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:30:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Honour the run_<tool> checkboxes in web_api_discovery\n\nThe engine editor shows favirecon, sourcemapper, grpcurl, julius and\ngqlspection as run_<tool> checkboxes and writes them into the\nweb_api_discovery section, but the backend only ever read uses_tools.\nTicking a box did nothing, and engines saved from the editor carried\nrun_*: true flags for tools that never ran.\n\n- resolve_api_discovery_tools() (common_func/scan_config.py) builds the\n  tool list from uses_tools plus every tool whose run_<tool> flag is true.\n  A false flag does not remove a tool listed in uses_tools: the checkbox\n  and the list are alternative ways to switch the same tool on.\n- scan_init (scan and subscan), the maintenance activity that rebuilds the\n  scan context, and web_api_discovery''s own fallback all use it.\n- The editor used to show every checkbox ticked when the flag was absent,\n  so opening and saving an engine switched all five tools on. It now\n  mirrors uses_tools for an absent flag; engines that already carry\n  run_*: true keep them ticked and will now run those tools.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"96d63c48e14998b2810e144feb89a05731808c18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/96d63c48e14998b2810e144feb89a05731808c18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073","verification":{"payload":"tree 96d63c48e14998b2810e144feb89a05731808c18\nparent 6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790782222 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790782222 +0000\n\nHonour the run_<tool> checkboxes in web_api_discovery\n\nThe engine editor shows favirecon, sourcemapper, grpcurl, julius and\ngqlspection as run_<tool> checkboxes and writes them into the\nweb_api_discovery section, but the backend only ever read uses_tools.\nTicking a box did nothing, and engines saved from the editor carried\nrun_*: true flags for tools that never ran.\n\n- resolve_api_discovery_tools() (common_func/scan_config.py) builds the\n  tool list from uses_tools plus every tool whose run_<tool> flag is true.\n  A false flag does not remove a tool listed in uses_tools: the checkbox\n  and the list are alternative ways to switch the same tool on.\n- scan_init (scan and subscan), the maintenance activity that rebuilds the\n  scan context, and web_api_discovery''s own fallback all use it.\n- The editor used to show every checkbox ticked when the flag was absent,\n  so opening and saving an engine switched all five tools on. It now\n  mirrors uses_tools for an absent flag; engines that already carry\n  run_*: true keep them ticked and will now run those tools.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAY3Bs0B\njyB2pldNlmj44MKAZF6L56IDxQxKmvW5lYu/+UT5oRr1FNlFqf4vTgD5Q79fHc/accEX/fbJlOdV\n9AA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T15:30:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDU1NGZhZGM0OTk2ZmJkNmU1NTg1YjI4OGQyMmUwYTE4YWMxOTcwNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d","sha":"6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d"}],"sha":"554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/554fadc4996fbd6e5585b288d22e0a18ac197073"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:05:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:05:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add SecurityTrails as a subdomain discovery source\n\nSecurityTrails lists the known subdomains of an apex domain (what\nsecuritytrails.com/list/apex_domain/<domain> shows in the browser). The\nscan uses the documented REST API instead of that page:\nGET https://api.securitytrails.com/v1/domain/<domain>/subdomains with the\nkey in the APIKEY header. One lookup spends one query of the account''s\nmonthly quota, so the tool is opt-in and never part of the defaults.\n\n- API Vault: new SECURITYTRAILS field. The key is stored in a new\n  SecurityTrailsAPIKey model (dashboard 0023), saved and cleared through\n  /scanEngine/<slug>/api_vault (`key_securitytrails`), included in config\n  export/import and the Django admin.\n- Engine: `securitytrails` in subdomain_discovery.uses_tools. It needs no\n  binary; the step writes subdomains_securitytrails.txt next to the other\n  tools'' output so the usual merge, scope check and save apply. Without a\n  vault key it is skipped before any request. A rejected key, spent quota\n  or network error is logged and the scan continues with the other tools.\n- The engine editor offers it in the tool picker; the reference YAML\n  lists it commented out.\n- The vault page''s KeyField moved out of the page component. It was\n  redefined on every render, so each keystroke remounted the inputs; this\n  also clears the baselined react-hooks/static-components errors.\n\nTests: API client (parsing, truncation warning, 401/403/429/5xx, network\nerror without leaking details, domain validation), the discovery step\n(no key means no request), vault save/read/clear, and the vault form\nsending the key under the name the view reads.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"bad95b0b1b31fa678eefeb74694ae93faa087dff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/bad95b0b1b31fa678eefeb74694ae93faa087dff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d","verification":{"payload":"tree bad95b0b1b31fa678eefeb74694ae93faa087dff\nparent f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790780747 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790780747 +0000\n\nAdd SecurityTrails as a subdomain discovery source\n\nSecurityTrails lists the known subdomains of an apex domain (what\nsecuritytrails.com/list/apex_domain/<domain> shows in the browser). The\nscan uses the documented REST API instead of that page:\nGET https://api.securitytrails.com/v1/domain/<domain>/subdomains with the\nkey in the APIKEY header. One lookup spends one query of the account''s\nmonthly quota, so the tool is opt-in and never part of the defaults.\n\n- API Vault: new SECURITYTRAILS field. The key is stored in a new\n  SecurityTrailsAPIKey model (dashboard 0023), saved and cleared through\n  /scanEngine/<slug>/api_vault (`key_securitytrails`), included in config\n  export/import and the Django admin.\n- Engine: `securitytrails` in subdomain_discovery.uses_tools. It needs no\n  binary; the step writes subdomains_securitytrails.txt next to the other\n  tools'' output so the usual merge, scope check and save apply. Without a\n  vault key it is skipped before any request. A rejected key, spent quota\n  or network error is logged and the scan continues with the other tools.\n- The engine editor offers it in the tool picker; the reference YAML\n  lists it commented out.\n- The vault page''s KeyField moved out of the page component. It was\n  redefined on every render, so each keystroke remounted the inputs; this\n  also clears the baselined react-hooks/static-components errors.\n\nTests: API client (parsing, truncation warning, 401/403/429/5xx, network\nerror without leaking details, domain validation), the discovery step\n(no key means no request), vault save/read/clear, and the vault form\nsending the key under the name the view reads.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPtHnOoE\nf1rlVVNWx85hLhDiKNviFLv/Q7bgt6DPxjwNoB0MC9Yf5Sw6s48m1fNGJkFHIjT3TDxTa39YiRP1\ndQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T15:06:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDZhMjQxNzljNTFhMjQ3ZTk0NDg1MzhlZDA5N2Y3YTA1ZWJhNzk1N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17","sha":"f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17"}],"sha":"6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6a24179c51a247e9448538ed097f7a05eba7957d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:21:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:21:55Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Remove Exploit-DB and the Searchsploit action\n\nWhy:\n- The `exploitdb` named volume was mounted by web, the orchestrator and the\n  Go executor over /usr/src/exploitdb, which the image already populated.\n  On a fresh install Docker copies the image content into an empty named\n  volume once per container; the three copies race and `make up` fails with\n  \"mkdir .../_data/exploits/netbsd_x86: file exists\". This was hit on the\n  first clean deployment of this branch.\n- The volume only duplicated the image (~360 MB, ~48k files) and was never\n  refreshed on rebuild, so an upgraded image kept serving the old copy.\n- Nothing in the scan pipeline used it: the only consumer was a manual\n  \"SEARCHSPLOIT\" menu item on the subdomains page. The `searchsploit` entry\n  in full_yaml_config.yaml described a task that does not exist. Public\n  exploit evidence still comes from SploitScan and the CVE enrichment\n  (ExploitDB references included), which do not need a local copy.\n\nWhat:\n- docker: drop the git clone and searchsploit symlink from the Dockerfiles,\n  the clone/rc-copy steps from the web and orchestrator entrypoints, and the\n  `exploitdb` volume and its mounts from docker-compose.yml and\n  docker-compose.dev.yml.\n- API: remove RunSearchsploitAction and POST\n  /api/action/subdomain/<id>/searchsploit/ (and its /mapi/ twin);\n  openapi.json and frontend/src/types/api.ts regenerated.\n- Frontend: remove SearchsploitModal, its menu item, the API helper and\n  its tests; drop the now-unread selectedId state on the subdomains page.\n- Docs and reference YAML no longer list searchsploit.\n- tests/test_exploitdb_removed.py fails if a compose file, Dockerfile or\n  entrypoint references exploit-db again, or the route comes back.\n\nExisting installs keep an orphaned r3ngine_exploitdb volume; remove it with\n`docker volume rm r3ngine_exploitdb` after `make up`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"1c90cbc1de3d770118c79a42277f9eb472b148fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/1c90cbc1de3d770118c79a42277f9eb472b148fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c90cbc1de3d770118c79a42277f9eb472b148fa\nparent 6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790778115 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790778115 +0000\n\nRemove Exploit-DB and the Searchsploit action\n\nWhy:\n- The `exploitdb` named volume was mounted by web, the orchestrator and the\n  Go executor over /usr/src/exploitdb, which the image already populated.\n  On a fresh install Docker copies the image content into an empty named\n  volume once per container; the three copies race and `make up` fails with\n  \"mkdir .../_data/exploits/netbsd_x86: file exists\". This was hit on the\n  first clean deployment of this branch.\n- The volume only duplicated the image (~360 MB, ~48k files) and was never\n  refreshed on rebuild, so an upgraded image kept serving the old copy.\n- Nothing in the scan pipeline used it: the only consumer was a manual\n  \"SEARCHSPLOIT\" menu item on the subdomains page. The `searchsploit` entry\n  in full_yaml_config.yaml described a task that does not exist. Public\n  exploit evidence still comes from SploitScan and the CVE enrichment\n  (ExploitDB references included), which do not need a local copy.\n\nWhat:\n- docker: drop the git clone and searchsploit symlink from the Dockerfiles,\n  the clone/rc-copy steps from the web and orchestrator entrypoints, and the\n  `exploitdb` volume and its mounts from docker-compose.yml and\n  docker-compose.dev.yml.\n- API: remove RunSearchsploitAction and POST\n  /api/action/subdomain/<id>/searchsploit/ (and its /mapi/ twin);\n  openapi.json and frontend/src/types/api.ts regenerated.\n- Frontend: remove SearchsploitModal, its menu item, the API helper and\n  its tests; drop the now-unread selectedId state on the subdomains page.\n- Docs and reference YAML no longer list searchsploit.\n- tests/test_exploitdb_removed.py fails if a compose file, Dockerfile or\n  entrypoint references exploit-db again, or the route comes back.\n\nExisting installs keep an orphaned r3ngine_exploitdb volume; remove it with\n`docker volume rm r3ngine_exploitdb` after `make up`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCy/jZHx\neWQXDuUY9QUYphiLih4Vvy7yWgHOj1Bn6Ixu4hn3j/aLUEcPMsc4MUfeGIwCPVIf8Irl20a+bcuD\nxAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T14:22:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGY2ZjUwYzJhMzAxMDZhOGVmNTI3YzcyMDEyOWJmZWViMmQwMzdhMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752","sha":"6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752"}],"sha":"f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/f6f50c2a30106a8ef527c720129bfeeb2d037a17"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:36:56Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:36:56Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"install.sh: check free disk space first and stop when the build fails\n\nOn a fresh Ubuntu server the image build ran out of space after about 25\nminutes: the default LVM layout had given the root volume only half the\ndisk. install.sh then printed \"reNgine is installed!!!\" and went on to\nmigrate and create the admin user against containers that never started,\nbecause it ignored the exit codes of make build and make up.\n\n- Before building, compare the free space under Docker''s root dir with\n  MIN_FREE_GB (default 60). If it is lower, exit with the lvextend command\n  that usually fixes it. SKIP_DISK_CHECK=1 skips the check.\n- make certs, make build and make up are chained. A failure reports\n  \"installation failed\" and skips migrate and account creation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"85cc78d374d1a7618e5998ed3b9ece14703737e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/85cc78d374d1a7618e5998ed3b9ece14703737e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752","verification":{"payload":"tree 85cc78d374d1a7618e5998ed3b9ece14703737e1\nparent 5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790768216 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790768216 +0000\n\ninstall.sh: check free disk space first and stop when the build fails\n\nOn a fresh Ubuntu server the image build ran out of space after about 25\nminutes: the default LVM layout had given the root volume only half the\ndisk. install.sh then printed \"reNgine is installed!!!\" and went on to\nmigrate and create the admin user against containers that never started,\nbecause it ignored the exit codes of make build and make up.\n\n- Before building, compare the free space under Docker''s root dir with\n  MIN_FREE_GB (default 60). If it is lower, exit with the lvextend command\n  that usually fixes it. SKIP_DISK_CHECK=1 skips the check.\n- make certs, make build and make up are chained. A failure reports\n  \"installation failed\" and skips migrate and account creation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMkdE0Nl\nmntPK/++3oTzYWu8HORCa71uapyIB1MQLWaT5rUDZ7ncwIZzifIcJZzIc5QwuJ2QtafO1/Y/+AfL\nWg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:37:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDZlYjlmNTQzMzJlYWYxYjIxZWY2N2Q1MzY0ZjBiOWRkNTQ2MjM3NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f","sha":"5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f"}],"sha":"6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/6eb9f54332eaf1b21ef67d5364f0b9dd54623752"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:16:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:16:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 8: no silent exception handlers, no `any`, hermetic tests\n\nSwallowed exceptions (60 -> 0 in web/, guarded by a static test)\n- Each broad `except: pass` is now narrowed to what the code can raise, or\n  logs with exc_info. None swallow silently any more.\n- Bugs found and fixed on the way:\n  - WebSocket JWT auth accepted deactivated users until the token expired.\n  - OpSec metadata stripping was a stub; strip_directory now cleans PDF/JPEG/\n    PNG under the results dir and skips symlinks.\n  - The plugin install status returned internal error text (pg_dump and\n    migration stderr) to the client. Only PluginInstallError messages are\n    shown now; everything else gets the generic message.\n  - An evidence purge wrote \"file deleted\" to the chain of custody before\n    trying, and even when the storage delete failed. It now records the\n    real outcome.\n- Removed two duplicated, identical serializer definitions.\n\nFrontend types\n- API types regenerated from the drf-yasg schema (openapi.json was in the\n  wrong format for the generator). frontend/README.md has the steps.\n- No `any`, `@ts-ignore` or no-explicit-any disables left (147 -> 0); the\n  ESLint baseline shrank from 638 to 488 entries.\n- Bugs the types exposed, now fixed:\n  - TagInput styling was ignored (renderTags was removed in MUI v9).\n  - Subscan engine always showed \"DEFAULT\".\n  - Notification icons were keyed on the wrong field.\n  - The proxy fetch panel expected the wrong status name, and NOT_FOUND\n    polled forever.\n  - The assessment timeline read fields the stream never sends.\n  - A null dork type crashed.\n  - A null email could be sent to the breach check.\n  - Search showed \"OTHERS (undefined)\".\n  - The organisation create request sent an ignored field.\n  - The directories list was typed with the wrong schema.\n\nTests\n- The test runner rejects creating files or directories from a mock-derived\n  path; the trufflehog test no longer litters the cwd.\n- tldextract uses its bundled snapshot in tests (no network).\n- kaleido rendering is stubbed; assertions check the figure passed to the\n  renderer instead.\n- One real-sleep watchdog test is tagged integration and has a stubbed twin.\n- The suite passes with the network disabled and as a non-root user.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"6b4555e77cd2c4d0bc94e47a40774c7081b8204d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/6b4555e77cd2c4d0bc94e47a40774c7081b8204d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f","verification":{"payload":"tree 6b4555e77cd2c4d0bc94e47a40774c7081b8204d\nparent 3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790759760 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790759760 +0000\n\nPhase 8: no silent exception handlers, no `any`, hermetic tests\n\nSwallowed exceptions (60 -> 0 in web/, guarded by a static test)\n- Each broad `except: pass` is now narrowed to what the code can raise, or\n  logs with exc_info. None swallow silently any more.\n- Bugs found and fixed on the way:\n  - WebSocket JWT auth accepted deactivated users until the token expired.\n  - OpSec metadata stripping was a stub; strip_directory now cleans PDF/JPEG/\n    PNG under the results dir and skips symlinks.\n  - The plugin install status returned internal error text (pg_dump and\n    migration stderr) to the client. Only PluginInstallError messages are\n    shown now; everything else gets the generic message.\n  - An evidence purge wrote \"file deleted\" to the chain of custody before\n    trying, and even when the storage delete failed. It now records the\n    real outcome.\n- Removed two duplicated, identical serializer definitions.\n\nFrontend types\n- API types regenerated from the drf-yasg schema (openapi.json was in the\n  wrong format for the generator). frontend/README.md has the steps.\n- No `any`, `@ts-ignore` or no-explicit-any disables left (147 -> 0); the\n  ESLint baseline shrank from 638 to 488 entries.\n- Bugs the types exposed, now fixed:\n  - TagInput styling was ignored (renderTags was removed in MUI v9).\n  - Subscan engine always showed \"DEFAULT\".\n  - Notification icons were keyed on the wrong field.\n  - The proxy fetch panel expected the wrong status name, and NOT_FOUND\n    polled forever.\n  - The assessment timeline read fields the stream never sends.\n  - A null dork type crashed.\n  - A null email could be sent to the breach check.\n  - Search showed \"OTHERS (undefined)\".\n  - The organisation create request sent an ignored field.\n  - The directories list was typed with the wrong schema.\n\nTests\n- The test runner rejects creating files or directories from a mock-derived\n  path; the trufflehog test no longer litters the cwd.\n- tldextract uses its bundled snapshot in tests (no network).\n- kaleido rendering is stubbed; assertions check the figure passed to the\n  renderer instead.\n- One real-sleep watchdog test is tagged integration and has a stubbed twin.\n- The suite passes with the network disabled and as a non-root user.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGsm4iu+\n8SzH5EiEyINxRRIeob3W4J9/hkQ1/s9m0ZRT3iivFBIdcAZZaHvCdUoIFHBBEXgIlDf48XcrBpxB\nLwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T09:16:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDU5ODM3ODVkYTc4YzE2Zjk2MmYwYWQ4ZDM2MjA1YWRmZjIwNmU0M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc","sha":"3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc"}],"sha":"5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/5983785da78c16f962f0ad8d36205adff206e43f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:34:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:34:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 10: per-worker executor queues, no docker.sock, current infrastructure images\n\nRemote workers: Go executor queues\n- The executor polled the shared go-executor-queue and ignored\n  --worker-name, so a remote executor took the master''s tool runs and wrote\n  their output into its own volume. It now serves\n  go-executor-queue-<WORKER_NAME> (the master keeps go-executor-queue).\n  Python puts the queue into GoExecutorTaskWorkflow''s input, so workflows\n  never read the environment; old histories fall back to the old queue.\n- Queue names and worker-name validation live in one place on each side\n  (utils/task_queues.py, executor/queue.go). The ScanWorker serializer uses\n  the same name rule.\n- The worker compose runs the executor from R3NGINE_IMAGE with the master''s\n  entrypoint and shares the orchestrator''s volumes. The image it pointed at\n  did not exist.\n- Verified here with a real Temporal and two executors: each job ran only on\n  its own executor. The integration test for this is tagged integration.\n  CI runs go test.\n\nNo docker.sock\n- Plugin install restart: the web process SIGTERMs its service root, and\n  restart: always brings the container back.\n- Tool probing runs as ToolProbeActivity on the orchestrator instead of\n  docker exec from web.\n- Tor and Ollama are compose services behind the tor/ollama profiles\n  (COMPOSE_PROFILES). The app only checks whether they are reachable. The UI\n  shows their status and how to enable them; turning on TOR mode while Tor\n  is down is refused.\n- Tor needs TOR_CONTROL_PASSWORD from .env; the entrypoint no longer falls\n  back to \"changeme\". The docker Python package is no longer needed.\n- A test guards against docker.sock mounts coming back.\n\nInfrastructure images (each upgrade exercised on real data in Docker)\n- redis:alpine -> redis:8.10-alpine, which is what the tag resolves to\n  today.\n- neo4j:5.12.0 -> neo4j:5.26-community (LTS). Graph, index and APOC calls\n  survived the upgrade.\n- temporalio/auto-setup:1.22.4 (a development image) ->\n  temporalio/server:1.31.3, with one-shot schema and namespace jobs. The\n  schema job refuses to start the server on an old schema.\n  scripts/temporal_upgrade.sh (make temporal-upgrade, also run by\n  make fullupgrade) backs up and steps through each minor version. Old\n  workflows, running workflows and schedules survived.\n- nginx pinned to 1.31-alpine; the dev temporal-ui is updated.\n- documents/upgrading-infrastructure.md has the steps, backups and rollback.\n- A test rejects untagged third-party images.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"6ca38f7703ca9dfb9d48b0a813643b56547d7a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/6ca38f7703ca9dfb9d48b0a813643b56547d7a47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ca38f7703ca9dfb9d48b0a813643b56547d7a47\nparent 9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790757282 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790757282 +0000\n\nPhase 10: per-worker executor queues, no docker.sock, current infrastructure images\n\nRemote workers: Go executor queues\n- The executor polled the shared go-executor-queue and ignored\n  --worker-name, so a remote executor took the master''s tool runs and wrote\n  their output into its own volume. It now serves\n  go-executor-queue-<WORKER_NAME> (the master keeps go-executor-queue).\n  Python puts the queue into GoExecutorTaskWorkflow''s input, so workflows\n  never read the environment; old histories fall back to the old queue.\n- Queue names and worker-name validation live in one place on each side\n  (utils/task_queues.py, executor/queue.go). The ScanWorker serializer uses\n  the same name rule.\n- The worker compose runs the executor from R3NGINE_IMAGE with the master''s\n  entrypoint and shares the orchestrator''s volumes. The image it pointed at\n  did not exist.\n- Verified here with a real Temporal and two executors: each job ran only on\n  its own executor. The integration test for this is tagged integration.\n  CI runs go test.\n\nNo docker.sock\n- Plugin install restart: the web process SIGTERMs its service root, and\n  restart: always brings the container back.\n- Tool probing runs as ToolProbeActivity on the orchestrator instead of\n  docker exec from web.\n- Tor and Ollama are compose services behind the tor/ollama profiles\n  (COMPOSE_PROFILES). The app only checks whether they are reachable. The UI\n  shows their status and how to enable them; turning on TOR mode while Tor\n  is down is refused.\n- Tor needs TOR_CONTROL_PASSWORD from .env; the entrypoint no longer falls\n  back to \"changeme\". The docker Python package is no longer needed.\n- A test guards against docker.sock mounts coming back.\n\nInfrastructure images (each upgrade exercised on real data in Docker)\n- redis:alpine -> redis:8.10-alpine, which is what the tag resolves to\n  today.\n- neo4j:5.12.0 -> neo4j:5.26-community (LTS). Graph, index and APOC calls\n  survived the upgrade.\n- temporalio/auto-setup:1.22.4 (a development image) ->\n  temporalio/server:1.31.3, with one-shot schema and namespace jobs. The\n  schema job refuses to start the server on an old schema.\n  scripts/temporal_upgrade.sh (make temporal-upgrade, also run by\n  make fullupgrade) backs up and steps through each minor version. Old\n  workflows, running workflows and schedules survived.\n- nginx pinned to 1.31-alpine; the dev temporal-ui is updated.\n- documents/upgrading-infrastructure.md has the steps, backups and rollback.\n- A test rejects untagged third-party images.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM/YPn3m\nx24LRv2mm0zK8c5Ti02CvpQvglls6icvNeMG892PY+MmcxPw9/vIoOfJ2yMnrwgRikuMZ4HDwikj\nCg0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T08:34:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDNjZTVkYjQ3OGViODk2NjhlODMyZThiYmJjNTVhMzc0ZTRhMmZhZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e","sha":"9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e"}],"sha":"3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/3ce5db478eb89668e832e8bbbc55a374e4a2fafc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:05:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:05:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 9: fill the empty WHOIS and bucket tabs, fix summary display bugs\n\n- WHOIS tab was always empty: neither summary endpoint sent WHOIS data.\n  The scan and target summaries now share one domain_info builder\n  (api/summary_domain_info.py) that adds registrar.url and a whois block\n  (statuses, registrant/admin/tech contacts, raw record). Existing keys\n  are unchanged. A shared WhoisPanel shows the data on both pages, with the\n  registrar link passed through getSafeUrl.\n- WHOIS contacts never stored address, state or postal code: the parser\n  wrote street/province/postal_code while the save read\n  address/state/zip_code. The keys are now mapped.\n- Buckets: the count covered this scan while the list covered every scan of\n  the target. Both now read scan.buckets in one query.\n- dnssec and other booleans render as Yes/No instead of blank.\n- Summary vulnerability rows are typed as what the backend sends (numeric\n  severity, short rows). That exposed VulnerabilityInfoModal reading CVSS,\n  source, tags and references from those short rows, which always showed\n  N/A; it now loads the full record while open.\n- The stress dashboard''s protocol breakdown panel was removed: no tool\n  output provides per-protocol counts.\n- ErrorDistribution uses ECharts like the other stress charts; @nivo/bar\n  and d3-scale removed (GeoMap takes scaleLinear from d3).\n- Summary query counts stay flat, and tests check that growing buckets,\n  DNS records, statuses or contacts does not add queries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"a2e7178ee877f87c1a281dfb29353ee5afaa0984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/a2e7178ee877f87c1a281dfb29353ee5afaa0984"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e","verification":{"payload":"tree a2e7178ee877f87c1a281dfb29353ee5afaa0984\nparent 20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790712339 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790712339 +0000\n\nPhase 9: fill the empty WHOIS and bucket tabs, fix summary display bugs\n\n- WHOIS tab was always empty: neither summary endpoint sent WHOIS data.\n  The scan and target summaries now share one domain_info builder\n  (api/summary_domain_info.py) that adds registrar.url and a whois block\n  (statuses, registrant/admin/tech contacts, raw record). Existing keys\n  are unchanged. A shared WhoisPanel shows the data on both pages, with the\n  registrar link passed through getSafeUrl.\n- WHOIS contacts never stored address, state or postal code: the parser\n  wrote street/province/postal_code while the save read\n  address/state/zip_code. The keys are now mapped.\n- Buckets: the count covered this scan while the list covered every scan of\n  the target. Both now read scan.buckets in one query.\n- dnssec and other booleans render as Yes/No instead of blank.\n- Summary vulnerability rows are typed as what the backend sends (numeric\n  severity, short rows). That exposed VulnerabilityInfoModal reading CVSS,\n  source, tags and references from those short rows, which always showed\n  N/A; it now loads the full record while open.\n- The stress dashboard''s protocol breakdown panel was removed: no tool\n  output provides per-protocol counts.\n- ErrorDistribution uses ECharts like the other stress charts; @nivo/bar\n  and d3-scale removed (GeoMap takes scaleLinear from d3).\n- Summary query counts stay flat, and tests check that growing buckets,\n  DNS records, statuses or contacts does not add queries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDf9qw79\n+zC17NkPxXinQYlvlADM3/zV3aGLfdMdxMNwQQb96T22WbNs6bh4VaHQcILpuFTQwM52z3jKo+ZN\n0w8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T20:05:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDlhNjhkYTk2NDkzYTdkZDYzNmY0MDkyYmIwM2UzYTg3ODMxYjRiMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5","sha":"20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5"}],"sha":"9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/9a68da96493a7dd636f4092bb03e3a87831b4b1e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:37:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:37:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add a compact vulnerability list format and a TODO of open work\n\nCompact list (owner chose the opt-in option)\n- GET /api/listVulnerability/?compact=1 returns the vulnerability''s own\n  fields plus minimal relations: scan_history {id}, subdomain {id, name},\n  endpoint {id, http_url}, target_domain {id, name}, tags, references and\n  the CVE columns the table shows. Kept keys have the same names and values\n  as the default format, so a compact row is a subset of a default row.\n- Only the list action honours the flag. Without it the response is\n  byte-identical to before, so MCP clients, reports and the legacy page are\n  unaffected.\n- 88 -> 7 queries per page; a populated row 12.6 KB -> 1.4 KB.\n- The vulnerability table and the scan Exploits tab request compact rows\n  (typed as VulnerabilityCompact); the detail modal still loads /{id}/.\n- Tests cover: default format intact, compact rows being a subset, flag\n  parsing, and the same ids/order/pagination with and without the flag\n  across 15 filter cases. Also a compact query-count test and a vitest test\n  for the api call.\n\ndocuments/TODO.md\n- Records the two deferred issues (the Go executor on remote workers shares\n  the master''s queue; docker.sock is mounted into web and the worker) with\n  the options considered, the decision on the vulnerability list, and other\n  known follow-ups.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"6fe3484d2a997c7c0c695f214ee5d36ca7853a8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/6fe3484d2a997c7c0c695f214ee5d36ca7853a8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5","verification":{"payload":"tree 6fe3484d2a997c7c0c695f214ee5d36ca7853a8f\nparent d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790710673 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790710673 +0000\n\nAdd a compact vulnerability list format and a TODO of open work\n\nCompact list (owner chose the opt-in option)\n- GET /api/listVulnerability/?compact=1 returns the vulnerability''s own\n  fields plus minimal relations: scan_history {id}, subdomain {id, name},\n  endpoint {id, http_url}, target_domain {id, name}, tags, references and\n  the CVE columns the table shows. Kept keys have the same names and values\n  as the default format, so a compact row is a subset of a default row.\n- Only the list action honours the flag. Without it the response is\n  byte-identical to before, so MCP clients, reports and the legacy page are\n  unaffected.\n- 88 -> 7 queries per page; a populated row 12.6 KB -> 1.4 KB.\n- The vulnerability table and the scan Exploits tab request compact rows\n  (typed as VulnerabilityCompact); the detail modal still loads /{id}/.\n- Tests cover: default format intact, compact rows being a subset, flag\n  parsing, and the same ids/order/pagination with and without the flag\n  across 15 filter cases. Also a compact query-count test and a vitest test\n  for the api call.\n\ndocuments/TODO.md\n- Records the two deferred issues (the Go executor on remote workers shares\n  the master''s queue; docker.sock is mounted into web and the worker) with\n  the options considered, the decision on the vulnerability list, and other\n  known follow-ups.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPav3Fog\nBEF16rbFwTUkVPNOHKyJkRm4I5dXqksORcP6TJl2+Ht+rPD5G3dpByERv/v5+SIfB+Mw5QtfUQCM\nHQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T19:37:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDIwNzM0ZGE3NDlmYjRlNTJjMTQwZTVjYmM5ZmMzOWM5YmM1ZjQ0ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792","sha":"d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792"}],"sha":"20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/20734da749fb4e52c140e5cbc9fc39c9bc5f44f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:03:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T19:03:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 5: make list endpoints cost the same at any page size\n\n- The six list endpoints the UI pages through ran queries per row. Each now\n  costs a fixed number of queries whether it returns 1 row or a full page\n  (queries for 1 -> 5 rows, before -> after):\n  - subdomain datatable: 31 -> 111 became 24 -> 24;\n  - endpoints: 8 -> 24 became 8 -> 8;\n  - vulnerabilities: 88 -> 424 became 88 -> 88;\n  - listScans: 13 -> 45 became 6 -> 6;\n  - listScanHistory: 15 -> 63 became 5 -> 5;\n  - targets: 29 -> 129 became 25 -> 25;\n  - directory summary: 4 -> 8 became flat.\n- The work is done by list serializers (list_serializer_class) over the rows\n  actually serialized, after pagination, so every many=True caller benefits.\n  Single-object serialization keeps the old per-row path, and the precomputed\n  values are tested against it.\n- The ScanStatus annotations moved into with_scan_history_serializer_data()\n  and are shared by the three scan list views.\n- DirectoryViewSet is read-only now. Clients only ever use GET on that route,\n  but as a ModelViewSet it let sys admins and pentesters create, update and\n  delete EndPoint rows. Write methods now return 405.\n- tests/test_list_endpoint_query_count.py: 17 tests. Each flatness test\n  failed on the old code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"da3b5e74fb7b348aa1605d536e7aad4e584c8aef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/da3b5e74fb7b348aa1605d536e7aad4e584c8aef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792","verification":{"payload":"tree da3b5e74fb7b348aa1605d536e7aad4e584c8aef\nparent 825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790708614 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790708614 +0000\n\nPhase 5: make list endpoints cost the same at any page size\n\n- The six list endpoints the UI pages through ran queries per row. Each now\n  costs a fixed number of queries whether it returns 1 row or a full page\n  (queries for 1 -> 5 rows, before -> after):\n  - subdomain datatable: 31 -> 111 became 24 -> 24;\n  - endpoints: 8 -> 24 became 8 -> 8;\n  - vulnerabilities: 88 -> 424 became 88 -> 88;\n  - listScans: 13 -> 45 became 6 -> 6;\n  - listScanHistory: 15 -> 63 became 5 -> 5;\n  - targets: 29 -> 129 became 25 -> 25;\n  - directory summary: 4 -> 8 became flat.\n- The work is done by list serializers (list_serializer_class) over the rows\n  actually serialized, after pagination, so every many=True caller benefits.\n  Single-object serialization keeps the old per-row path, and the precomputed\n  values are tested against it.\n- The ScanStatus annotations moved into with_scan_history_serializer_data()\n  and are shared by the three scan list views.\n- DirectoryViewSet is read-only now. Clients only ever use GET on that route,\n  but as a ModelViewSet it let sys admins and pentesters create, update and\n  delete EndPoint rows. Write methods now return 405.\n- tests/test_list_endpoint_query_count.py: 17 tests. Each flatness test\n  failed on the old code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGIBvbZz\n79ghnUVNMSwDq8xbEGLEvoZhqCnzRENd1nz/IyJWiZQuSpgCpM9MHYCpYVVB35hiUUv78I7c7zOp\nQQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T19:03:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGQxZjZmZjFiZDY1NDg4ZmQxYTRiNTQ0YjA4N2U5NzkxZDRmZjk3OTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44","sha":"825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44"}],"sha":"d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/d1f6ff1bd65488fd1a4b544b087e9791d4ff9792"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:40:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:40:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 3: split the largest backend modules and format log calls safely\n\nModule splits (pure moves; every moved definition verified AST-identical)\n- temporal/activities/__init__.py (4.7k lines) -> core, scan_lifecycle,\n  discovery, enumeration, vuln_scan, post_processing, intel, proxies,\n  maintenance, plugin_auth, stress. Same 117 registered activity names.\n- temporal/workflows/__init__.py (3.9k lines) -> _common (retry presets),\n  master_scan, subscan, jobs, recon, stress. Same 32 workflow names, so\n  running executions still replay; 288 execute_activity calls unchanged.\n- common_func.py (3.3k lines) -> package of 10 domain modules. The\n  star-import surface 33 modules depend on is unchanged (683 names).\n- api/views/__init__.py (2.3k lines) -> existing domain modules plus\n  scan_status, subdomains, endpoints, notes; api/serializers.py -> package.\n- tasks/osint.py and tasks/crawl.py -> packages.\n- Each package __init__ re-exports the old names, so imports and the\n  temporal_activities/temporal_workflows/tasks shims keep working.\n- Test patch targets moved to where names are looked up. In nine test\n  files the old targets would have stopped applying without failing,\n  letting tests run real tools, network calls and DB writes.\n\nLogging\n- 652 logger calls built their message with an f-string; they now pass\n  values as arguments (security rule 2.1). Each rewritten call was checked\n  to render the same message. A test rejects new f-string log calls.\n- Activity logs never reached temporal.log: the logger was configured\n  under the shim''s name, which nothing logs as. Fixed and tested.\n\nFixes found on the way\n- Aborting a scan did not stop Go-executor commands promptly: the cancel\n  event was imported from the shim, which does not export underscore\n  names, so every check failed silently and only the slower DB poll\n  worked. It is now read in the calling thread. Test fails on the old code.\n\nDocs and tooling\n- CLAUDE.md, .claude rules/skills and architecture-overview describe the\n  new layout; stale Django 4.x/Celery/mobile references removed.\n- settings_test_local reads RENGINE_TEST_DB_NAME so two suites can run\n  side by side.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"e6c8d631f22e811cad486b8e052bb8280254cb02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/e6c8d631f22e811cad486b8e052bb8280254cb02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44","verification":{"payload":"tree e6c8d631f22e811cad486b8e052bb8280254cb02\nparent ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790707211 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790707211 +0000\n\nPhase 3: split the largest backend modules and format log calls safely\n\nModule splits (pure moves; every moved definition verified AST-identical)\n- temporal/activities/__init__.py (4.7k lines) -> core, scan_lifecycle,\n  discovery, enumeration, vuln_scan, post_processing, intel, proxies,\n  maintenance, plugin_auth, stress. Same 117 registered activity names.\n- temporal/workflows/__init__.py (3.9k lines) -> _common (retry presets),\n  master_scan, subscan, jobs, recon, stress. Same 32 workflow names, so\n  running executions still replay; 288 execute_activity calls unchanged.\n- common_func.py (3.3k lines) -> package of 10 domain modules. The\n  star-import surface 33 modules depend on is unchanged (683 names).\n- api/views/__init__.py (2.3k lines) -> existing domain modules plus\n  scan_status, subdomains, endpoints, notes; api/serializers.py -> package.\n- tasks/osint.py and tasks/crawl.py -> packages.\n- Each package __init__ re-exports the old names, so imports and the\n  temporal_activities/temporal_workflows/tasks shims keep working.\n- Test patch targets moved to where names are looked up. In nine test\n  files the old targets would have stopped applying without failing,\n  letting tests run real tools, network calls and DB writes.\n\nLogging\n- 652 logger calls built their message with an f-string; they now pass\n  values as arguments (security rule 2.1). Each rewritten call was checked\n  to render the same message. A test rejects new f-string log calls.\n- Activity logs never reached temporal.log: the logger was configured\n  under the shim''s name, which nothing logs as. Fixed and tested.\n\nFixes found on the way\n- Aborting a scan did not stop Go-executor commands promptly: the cancel\n  event was imported from the shim, which does not export underscore\n  names, so every check failed silently and only the slower DB poll\n  worked. It is now read in the calling thread. Test fails on the old code.\n\nDocs and tooling\n- CLAUDE.md, .claude rules/skills and architecture-overview describe the\n  new layout; stale Django 4.x/Celery/mobile references removed.\n- settings_test_local reads RENGINE_TEST_DB_NAME so two suites can run\n  side by side.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOpN6Nvd\nAzjBtWRb5EuAb/9OeCd0JqAhyAljekpaUkdX3sEId5BqGGSnv3zb+FMkcSgoNOW6ZZScPoLOLats\nKAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T18:40:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDgyNWMxY2FmNjhiZDhkZjVlOGIxNWRjMjliYzZjYmUyNjhiMGRlNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a","sha":"ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a"}],"sha":"825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/825c1caf68bd8df5e8b15dc29bc6cbe268b0de44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:30:21Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:30:21Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 4: route frontend calls through the API layer and type the worst files\n\nAPI layer\n- Every backend call made directly from a component (axios or fetch) now\n  goes through a typed function in the feature''s api module, with the same\n  URL, method, body, headers and response handling. Covered by vitest tests\n  that assert the request each function sends.\n\nTypes\n- The ten files with the most `any`/`@ts-ignore` (StressTestingPage,\n  ScanDetailPage, GraphCanvas, TargetSummary, scan types, SubdomainsTab,\n  DistributionCharts, the vulnerability modal/table, main.tsx) are fully\n  typed, as are the api hooks that returned `any` (target summary, GPT\n  report, graph data, plugin manifest). 161 -> 150 left in src/.\n- Typing exposed display bugs, now fixed: S3 bucket public read/write read\n  fields that do not exist and always showed \"NO\"; vulnerability references\n  rendered as \"[object Object]\"; DNS rows showed \"-> undefined\"; the target\n  monitoring date column was always empty; unsupported cytoscape styles.\n\nFixes\n- The assessment execution page read its route id with react-router-dom''s\n  useParams under the TanStack router, which has no react-router context,\n  so the page threw on open. It uses TanStack''s useParams now.\n- Links and window.open targets built from API data go through\n  getSafeUrl/openSafeUrl (http/https or same-origin path only; rejects\n  javascript:, data:, protocol-relative and control characters), per\n  security rule 4.2. Unit-tested.\n\nDependencies\n- Removed 15 packages with no usage: react-router-dom, cytoscape-cola,\n  cytoscape-dagre, react-cytoscapejs, prismjs, prism-react-renderer,\n  react-simple-code-editor, tailwind-merge, tslib (still installed via\n  @dnd-kit) and six unused @types packages. Lockfile regenerated by npm.\n- ESLint baseline pruned: 17 rule entries, 273 suppressed violations gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"b3b4eea6be0f9ab954b27716edc4c3146b6674cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/b3b4eea6be0f9ab954b27716edc4c3146b6674cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a","verification":{"payload":"tree b3b4eea6be0f9ab954b27716edc4c3146b6674cb\nparent e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790706621 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790706621 +0000\n\nPhase 4: route frontend calls through the API layer and type the worst files\n\nAPI layer\n- Every backend call made directly from a component (axios or fetch) now\n  goes through a typed function in the feature''s api module, with the same\n  URL, method, body, headers and response handling. Covered by vitest tests\n  that assert the request each function sends.\n\nTypes\n- The ten files with the most `any`/`@ts-ignore` (StressTestingPage,\n  ScanDetailPage, GraphCanvas, TargetSummary, scan types, SubdomainsTab,\n  DistributionCharts, the vulnerability modal/table, main.tsx) are fully\n  typed, as are the api hooks that returned `any` (target summary, GPT\n  report, graph data, plugin manifest). 161 -> 150 left in src/.\n- Typing exposed display bugs, now fixed: S3 bucket public read/write read\n  fields that do not exist and always showed \"NO\"; vulnerability references\n  rendered as \"[object Object]\"; DNS rows showed \"-> undefined\"; the target\n  monitoring date column was always empty; unsupported cytoscape styles.\n\nFixes\n- The assessment execution page read its route id with react-router-dom''s\n  useParams under the TanStack router, which has no react-router context,\n  so the page threw on open. It uses TanStack''s useParams now.\n- Links and window.open targets built from API data go through\n  getSafeUrl/openSafeUrl (http/https or same-origin path only; rejects\n  javascript:, data:, protocol-relative and control characters), per\n  security rule 4.2. Unit-tested.\n\nDependencies\n- Removed 15 packages with no usage: react-router-dom, cytoscape-cola,\n  cytoscape-dagre, react-cytoscapejs, prismjs, prism-react-renderer,\n  react-simple-code-editor, tailwind-merge, tslib (still installed via\n  @dnd-kit) and six unused @types packages. Lockfile regenerated by npm.\n- ESLint baseline pruned: 17 rule entries, 273 suppressed violations gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGD8xgsr\nYQ51mawlV07EJRcncvck9TaGt7tvlBnekNTpNCWNs3naFbJiV2OmUZnL/Qat5NJ+OSKuqp1QBORM\nDwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T18:30:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGZmNGQ2MDdjMjczODdhNTNjYTFiOTk4MzRkNmM0N2JmNWU2OGM3OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4","sha":"e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4"}],"sha":"ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/ff4d607c27387a53ca1b99834d6c47bf5e68c79a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:41:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:41:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 2: keep long activities alive and stop hiding scan-path failures\n\nHeartbeats\n- Eleven activities were scheduled with a heartbeat_timeout shorter than\n  their run time but never heartbeated, so the server killed healthy runs\n  on a timer and the retry policy started them again. They now run under\n  @keep_alive (reNgine/temporal/heartbeat.py), which heartbeats from a\n  thread that carries the activity context.\n- tests/test_activity_heartbeats.py fails for any new activity in that\n  situation; the rule is documented in .claude/rules/r3ngine-temporal.md.\n\nSwallowed errors\n- Schedule deletion ignored every error, so an unreachable Temporal left\n  a schedule starting scans while the UI showed it gone. Only not-found\n  is ignored now (delete_schedule_if_exists); callers already log others.\n- feroxbuster parsing wrapped the DB flush in \"except: pass\": a failed\n  save was hidden and the batch kept growing. Only JSON decoding is\n  guarded now, for ffuf too.\n- Bulk stop counted scans it failed to abort; bulk pause/resume and\n  plugin activity bookkeeping failed silently. They log and count real\n  results.\n- The hardware profile lookup, duplicated in scan and subscan start,\n  is one helper that logs when it falls back to engine defaults.\n- Workflows log (via workflow.logger) when timeline pre-population or\n  TOR circuit rotation fails.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"c5a8197e2ae2766bdb8b6907cd39f2872c12ed8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/c5a8197e2ae2766bdb8b6907cd39f2872c12ed8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4","verification":{"payload":"tree c5a8197e2ae2766bdb8b6907cd39f2872c12ed8c\nparent 0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790692914 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790692914 +0000\n\nPhase 2: keep long activities alive and stop hiding scan-path failures\n\nHeartbeats\n- Eleven activities were scheduled with a heartbeat_timeout shorter than\n  their run time but never heartbeated, so the server killed healthy runs\n  on a timer and the retry policy started them again. They now run under\n  @keep_alive (reNgine/temporal/heartbeat.py), which heartbeats from a\n  thread that carries the activity context.\n- tests/test_activity_heartbeats.py fails for any new activity in that\n  situation; the rule is documented in .claude/rules/r3ngine-temporal.md.\n\nSwallowed errors\n- Schedule deletion ignored every error, so an unreachable Temporal left\n  a schedule starting scans while the UI showed it gone. Only not-found\n  is ignored now (delete_schedule_if_exists); callers already log others.\n- feroxbuster parsing wrapped the DB flush in \"except: pass\": a failed\n  save was hidden and the batch kept growing. Only JSON decoding is\n  guarded now, for ffuf too.\n- Bulk stop counted scans it failed to abort; bulk pause/resume and\n  plugin activity bookkeeping failed silently. They log and count real\n  results.\n- The hardware profile lookup, duplicated in scan and subscan start,\n  is one helper that logs when it falls back to engine defaults.\n- Workflows log (via workflow.logger) when timeline pre-population or\n  TOR circuit rotation fails.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIywqwFM\nw9AReB71zOWDD+YvC6DXrhGltTgcB2kI63WF+24yn5e4SnYdttMfHdR4ChlhSswZKb2wCNWoAT4S\nXQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T14:43:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGU4MTFmNGYxMjQ3ZWIxMzM1NTE3YzdiZmYzYmRiNzc4YzZkNmQ1YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0","sha":"0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0"}],"sha":"e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/e811f4f1247eb1335517c7bff3bdb778c6d6d5a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:24:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:24:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 1: close the security findings from the audit\n\nRemote workers\n- Tokens are generated server-side, shown once and stored as SHA-256\n  (migration hashes existing ones, so deployed workers keep working); the\n  API never returns them, and only sys admins may create or delete workers.\n- The heartbeat URL was not exempt from LoginRequiredMiddleware, so every\n  heartbeat was redirected to the login page and no worker ever came online.\n- Worker IP comes from X-Real-IP (set by nginx), not client-chosen\n  X-Forwarded-For; the worker verifies the master''s TLS certificate before\n  sending its token (MASTER_CA_BUNDLE / MASTER_TLS_VERIFY).\n- The Remote Workers page called /api/settings/workers/, which does not\n  exist; it now uses /api/workers/ and shows the issued token once.\n\nFile deletion\n- \"Delete all screenshots\" ran rm -rf over the whole results root; it now\n  removes only screenshots directories and their records.\n- Scan results are removed in one place, the ScanHistory pre_delete signal,\n  through a helper that refuses anything outside RENGINE_RESULTS; views no\n  longer shell out to rm -rf with a path taken from the database.\n\nTool management\n- Update/uninstall changed state on GET, which DRF does not CSRF-check;\n  browsers must POST (token-authenticated mobile clients may still GET).\n- Uninstall called a field that does not exist, so it always failed; it now\n  removes the go binary or git checkout without a shell, confined to their\n  directories. Missing tool_id/name returns 400 instead of 500.\n\nException text\n- About 50 responses returned str(e) to the client (rule 8); they now log\n  the exception and return INTERNAL_ERROR_MESSAGE. A static test fails on\n  any new occurrence. HackerOne''s handle_exception no longer turns DRF''s\n  401/403/400 into 500s.\n\nShell injection\n- Crawled URLs and hostnames were interpolated unquoted into shell=True\n  commands (arjun, LinkFinder, InQL, sourcemapper, gqlspection, jwt_tool,\n  graphql-cop, second-order, dirsearch, ffuf, feroxbuster, ...), letting a\n  scanned site run commands on the scanner. They are now shlex-quoted.\n\nAlso: scan-results export uses a per-request temp dir instead of a shared\n/tmp path; non-security MD5 uses are marked usedforsecurity=False.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"4dcc61e4c1e67345e782cb06f2fa38aff887b268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/4dcc61e4c1e67345e782cb06f2fa38aff887b268"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 4dcc61e4c1e67345e782cb06f2fa38aff887b268\nparent eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790688262 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790688262 +0000\n\nPhase 1: close the security findings from the audit\n\nRemote workers\n- Tokens are generated server-side, shown once and stored as SHA-256\n  (migration hashes existing ones, so deployed workers keep working); the\n  API never returns them, and only sys admins may create or delete workers.\n- The heartbeat URL was not exempt from LoginRequiredMiddleware, so every\n  heartbeat was redirected to the login page and no worker ever came online.\n- Worker IP comes from X-Real-IP (set by nginx), not client-chosen\n  X-Forwarded-For; the worker verifies the master''s TLS certificate before\n  sending its token (MASTER_CA_BUNDLE / MASTER_TLS_VERIFY).\n- The Remote Workers page called /api/settings/workers/, which does not\n  exist; it now uses /api/workers/ and shows the issued token once.\n\nFile deletion\n- \"Delete all screenshots\" ran rm -rf over the whole results root; it now\n  removes only screenshots directories and their records.\n- Scan results are removed in one place, the ScanHistory pre_delete signal,\n  through a helper that refuses anything outside RENGINE_RESULTS; views no\n  longer shell out to rm -rf with a path taken from the database.\n\nTool management\n- Update/uninstall changed state on GET, which DRF does not CSRF-check;\n  browsers must POST (token-authenticated mobile clients may still GET).\n- Uninstall called a field that does not exist, so it always failed; it now\n  removes the go binary or git checkout without a shell, confined to their\n  directories. Missing tool_id/name returns 400 instead of 500.\n\nException text\n- About 50 responses returned str(e) to the client (rule 8); they now log\n  the exception and return INTERNAL_ERROR_MESSAGE. A static test fails on\n  any new occurrence. HackerOne''s handle_exception no longer turns DRF''s\n  401/403/400 into 500s.\n\nShell injection\n- Crawled URLs and hostnames were interpolated unquoted into shell=True\n  commands (arjun, LinkFinder, InQL, sourcemapper, gqlspection, jwt_tool,\n  graphql-cop, second-order, dirsearch, ffuf, feroxbuster, ...), letting a\n  scanned site run commands on the scanner. They are now shlex-quoted.\n\nAlso: scan-results export uses a per-request temp dir instead of a shared\n/tmp path; non-security MD5 uses are marked usedforsecurity=False.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKympmez\nwbyJACNe0lFoChAkYNnWYnfh9ZJA/eRpEyP3Z6oQSmSnctSaYZ6PA75uMV/TQvBpkXXXMBYuD50y\neA0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T13:24:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDBlMTcxM2FiYWUyYWY0OTI1OTNhMmQzNDE5NzVhMmM4ODg2NzU4YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88","sha":"eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88"}],"sha":"0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/0e1713abae2af492593a2d341975a2c8886758c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:00:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:00:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Check the second-order config where the scan now writes it\n\nThe test still looked in /usr/local/config, which only passed locally\nbecause a previous root run had left the file there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"96a8ea30cfb8279ccf36767d0e99369ac6adc59a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/96a8ea30cfb8279ccf36767d0e99369ac6adc59a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88","verification":{"payload":"tree 96a8ea30cfb8279ccf36767d0e99369ac6adc59a\nparent 298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790686853 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790686853 +0000\n\nCheck the second-order config where the scan now writes it\n\nThe test still looked in /usr/local/config, which only passed locally\nbecause a previous root run had left the file there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLwxcK6/\n8+qbpIj7O6mY/kpZ36rLPBDU84BMZK4v1b0fEEYLnmItHCZqi/rVmoyAUXer+e5s9xgjZb6HjBRH\n1Qk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T13:00:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKGVlZDQ4ODUyNTQ0OWZiNjQ1MmQ2ZTk3NThmYjVhODI2Mzk2YTdmODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511","sha":"298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511"}],"sha":"eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/eed488525449fb6452d6e9758fb5a826396a7f88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:55:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:55:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make the backend suite pass without root, as it runs in CI\n\nThe first CI run failed only where code writes to container paths a\nnon-root runner cannot create:\n- second_order_scan wrote its merged config to /usr/local/config; it now\n  goes into the scan''s results dir, so concurrent scans no longer share it\n- the proxy list root and config-import wordlist/tool-config paths are\n  module constants, which tests point at temporary directories\n- cPanel and subscan tests created scans with an empty results_dir, which\n  resolved to ''/vulnerability'' and ''/subscans/<id>''\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"77eca1a5d3ccb3459e1faea29cb0ef8a45d899d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/77eca1a5d3ccb3459e1faea29cb0ef8a45d899d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511","verification":{"payload":"tree 77eca1a5d3ccb3459e1faea29cb0ef8a45d899d0\nparent 2d501e6a81f4deea767f01bd1b7b3c3be00d31a1\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790686558 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790686558 +0000\n\nMake the backend suite pass without root, as it runs in CI\n\nThe first CI run failed only where code writes to container paths a\nnon-root runner cannot create:\n- second_order_scan wrote its merged config to /usr/local/config; it now\n  goes into the scan''s results dir, so concurrent scans no longer share it\n- the proxy list root and config-import wordlist/tool-config paths are\n  module constants, which tests point at temporary directories\n- cPanel and subscan tests created scans with an empty results_dir, which\n  resolved to ''/vulnerability'' and ''/subscans/<id>''\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFLCBB5n\nh4Uln77een5z3Ce3XeF3DEw5Th+GOOf+sGjOgTEP/W3tXdpLLZxGqz5ZHHaB32IuxsqtpJYI3vop\nBQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T12:56:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511","node_id":"C_kwDOSRkBoNoAKDI5OGI5MGRiNmYxZmQzYWQ2NmQ4OTAyZTg1YmJhZDRhZGRhMjU1MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commit/2d501e6a81f4deea767f01bd1b7b3c3be00d31a1","sha":"2d501e6a81f4deea767f01bd1b7b3c3be00d31a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/2d501e6a81f4deea767f01bd1b7b3c3be00d31a1"}],"sha":"298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/298b90db6f1fd3ad66d8902e85bbad4adda25511"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/commits/2d501e6a81f4deea767f01bd1b7b3c3be00d31a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:32:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:32:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add CI and fix the test baseline so changes can be validated without a server\n\nCI (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs on every push: Django tests against a\nthrowaway Postgres (settings_test_local) plus a makemigrations check, flake8\nfor always-a-bug error classes, bandit (report only), the frontend type check,\nlint, vitest and build, and the Go executor build. The full image build is a\nmanual workflow that can publish to GHCR.\n\nThe app image is no longer hard-wired to the upstream registry:\nR3NGINE_IMAGE (default r3ngine:local) and `make pull --ignore-buildable`\nkeep `make pull` from replacing a local build with upstream''s image.\n\nReal bugs found by the new checks:\n- stress testing referenced TAStresserParser (NameError on every run)\n- vigolium fallback results dir referenced an undefined RENGINE_HOME\n- open(MagicMock) in tests opened fd 1 and closed stdout, so a later\n  Postgres connection reused fd 1 and failed with \"Bad file descriptor\";\n  the test runner now rejects mock file arguments outright\n- manual subdomain API did not report repeats within the input\n- nuclei_dast_scan and DomainSerializer re-imported names locally, which\n  bypassed patches; MasterScan/SubScan workflows used asyncio.sleep instead\n  of workflow.sleep (same timer command, replay-compatible)\n\nStale tests updated to the behaviour the code was deliberately changed to\n(patch targets after the views split, report filtering, tag-batch ceiling,\ntool gating, MCP enrich/validation endpoints). Tests needing live network,\nreal binaries or the docker stack are tagged `integration` and excluded.\nESLint''s existing violations are baselined in eslint-suppressions.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd","tree":{"sha":"1efc6e33e1688e24fe35ef6961170cd96c1457e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/trees/1efc6e33e1688e24fe35ef6961170cd96c1457e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/whiterabb17/r3ngine/git/commits/2d501e6a81f4deea767f01bd1b7b3c3be00d31a1","verification":{"payload":"tree 1efc6e33e1688e24fe35ef6961170cd96c1457e7\nparent 8d2f44465e5269ed73c4c0be7263cf69dcd107eb\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790685149 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790685149 +0000\n\nAdd CI and fix the test baseline so changes can be validated without a server\n\nCI (.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs on every push: Django tests against a\nthrowaway Postgres (settings_test_local) plus a makemigrations check, flake8\nfor always-a-bug error classes, bandit (report only), the frontend type check,\nlint, vitest and build, and the Go executor build. The full image build is a\nmanual workflow that can publish to GHCR.\n\nThe app image is no longer hard-wired to the upstream registry:\nR3NGINE_IMAGE (default r3ngine:local) and `make pull --ignore-buildable`\nkeep `make pull` from replacing a local build with upstream''s image.\n\nReal bugs found by the new checks:\n- stress testing referenced TAStresserParser (NameError on every run)\n- vigolium fallback results dir referenced an undefined RENGINE_HOME\n- open(MagicMock) in tests opened fd 1 and closed stdout, so a later\n  Postgres connection reused fd 1 and failed with \"Bad file descriptor\";\n  the test runner now rejects mock file arguments outright\n- manual subdomain API did not report repeats within the input\n- nuclei_dast_scan and DomainSerializer re-imported names locally, which\n  bypassed patches; MasterScan/SubScan workflows used asyncio.sleep instead\n  of workflow.sleep (same timer command, replay-compatible)\n\nStale tests updated to the behaviour the code was deliberately changed to\n(patch targets after the views split, report filtering, tag-batch ceiling,\ntool gating, MCP enrich/validation endpoints). Tests needing live network,\nreal binaries or the docker stack are tagged `integration` and excluded.\nESLint''s existing violations are baselined in eslint-suppressions.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E9ec9vQzQn9kv2Eukv4Rcd\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEilOOtI\njvMAy/ly3GLo37s+8MHOgQ+tiil+lCPHSbWHgL23Eov9KBwwMxVl0r/IUyMx3Ef