ents","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-micro-frontend-adapter-framework/commits/67e0d7c790adfdc0e41ef223e5537b154617f260/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:45:51Z","email":"iwan@arc-e-tect.com","name":"Iwan Eising"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T15:45:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build(release): release a breaking change before 1.0.0 as a minor version (#5)\n\nA 0.x version is still in development, and a release may break compatibility\nwithout a major version bump; semantic-release has no such rule, and a\nbreaking change would take a 0.x project to 1.0.0. release/zero-major-analyzer.js\nholds the rule: a major release becomes a minor one while the last release\nis 0.x, and stays major from 1.0.0 on, so reaching 1.0.0 is a decision\nrather than the side effect of a commit. Every release.config.js names it\nin place of @semantic-release/commit-analyzer, with the same options.","tree":{"sha":"d7d4844cd5e01f7ab5388f65a0e2cc2a9b0ea3f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-micro-frontend-adapter-framework/git/trees/d7d4844cd5e01f7ab5388f65a0e2cc2a9b0ea3f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-micro-frontend-adapter-framework/git/commits/67e0d7c790adfdc0e41ef223e5537b154617f260","verification":{"payload":"tree d7d4844cd5e01f7ab5388f65a0e2cc2a9b0ea3f4\nparent 11ac3def6ab2168fbb4370d64da289685e0cd34d\nauthor Iwan Eising <iwan@arc-e-tect.com> 1791128751 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791128751 -0700\n\nbuild(release): release a breaking change before 1.0.0 as a minor version (#5)\n\nA 0.x version is still in development, and a release may break compatibility\nwithout a major version bump; semantic-release has no such rule, and a\nbreaking change would take a 0.x project to 1.0.0. release/zero-major-analyzer.js\nholds the rule: a major release becomes a minor one while the last release\nis 0.x, and stays major from 1.0.0 on, so reaching 1.0.0 is a decision\nrather than the side effect of a commit. Every release.config.js names it\nin place of @semantic-release/commit-analyzer, with the same options.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwnSvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGZsQAKKzQ3sDb3k9+RmDhiOugnCd\nL1ATjR1qyNNQfWuUEWr4XKHNky5ytKgixNTQs+iMSz0PvQnupQyS+QuLDTx1rJu5\n2Qb1xPn2R9nLprDyIpG+4o69RvnbbXuB33s3Mg2gOEGJTkLBiUIspJLZe2o5/bix\nnQRGWbmjvk9TpTvwIHvUPLj+3wXR0C2sDqNmXU11izrbA73BiPaNbvPglGewG8ud\nG5mkquiHXFOabC58YTB0AVyDf6HpRPzMg+/zeh8pI18LKUMoiA2w0/mv0JLd5VHa\nD4v3G+iUbm6JIxCdNF/KtKCzDRAcet+S0rIc8OBY6U+b2lZ9pVQmgrfvmDmoQ61x\nOpZdyk2fXxmfTSytyQHfp4DXJxnyS5alYR76WSnHaEOkZ2F89gEasHdrDaEUpkr/\nY7noarfwVB1vIhe0as6zYgVkcPDPqq03CVEjutZTCQ1nDhxf1aNJ4ittRUQS+1oR\nJX/jiv04Vf9BLX2EYADImBaaY2QQpxgQg350GxCOniZZYhcK0i/ennLabiiN0jLo\n6Z8oLWmIlZXFYRy02n5i333UXN02TiOPdEl2nPQK1+96HS2xM6KS1ann7r/WkK0z\n1cndhEbTzCD1MLZG/KMT7sLJhSkGOHnBY0l8X0g5SL6U/A2YrYPJnGVc151Pat2l\n57VmebU9KWR45nvKj1AF\n=FHDW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T15:45:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/use