58784e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12331140?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Arc-E-Tect","id":12331140,"login":"Arc-E-Tect","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzMxMTQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arc-E-Tect","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-micro-frontend-adapter-framework/commits/6f4e664f82c1197ab72ba6a7fff551cac9e5f520/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T21:37:03Z","email":"iwan@arc-e-tect.com","name":"Iwan Eising"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T21:37:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add example project showcasing a vanilla MFA implementation (#1)\n\n## Why\n\nReaders of the book need a complete, runnable reference implementation of the MFA pattern\nthat is as simple as possible — no authentication, no TLS, no Kafka, no session persistence —\nso the structural pattern (Browser → MFE → MFA → MS) can be studied in isolation.\n\n## How\n\nThe `vanilla` Spring profile on the MFA replaces all security/session infrastructure beans\nwith no-op stubs (VanillaSessionStoreAdapter, VanillaWebClientConfiguration).\nSpring Boot''s relaxed binding maps `MFE_ADAPTER_MICROSERVICE_BASE_URL` → `mfe-adapter.microservice.base-url`\nso the MS location can be overridden for Docker without code changes.","tree":{"sha":"f8844c6b84b9fa644608ddd9b382ee2b242df5f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-micro-frontend-adapter-framework/git/trees/f8844c6b84b9fa644608ddd9b382ee2b242df5f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Arc-E-Tect/sedr-micro-frontend-adapter-framework/git/commits/6f4e664f82c1197ab72ba6a7fff551cac9e5f520","verification":{"payload":"tree f8844c6b84b9fa644608ddd9b382ee2b242df5f5\nparent 355333e9295d37eaf9a546d69c312bd3881731b0\nauthor Iwan Eising <iwan@arc-e-tect.com> 1778881023 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778881023 -0700\n\nfeat: add example project showcasing a vanilla MFA implementation (#1)\n\n## Why\n\nReaders of the book need a complete, runnable reference implementation of the MFA pattern\nthat is as simple as possible — no authentication, no TLS, no Kafka, no session persistence —\nso the structural pattern (Browser → MFE → MFA → MS) can be studied in isolation.\n\n## How\n\nThe `vanilla` Spring profile on the MFA replaces all security/session infrastructure beans\nwith no-op stubs (VanillaSessionStoreAdapter, VanillaWebClientConfiguration).\nSpring Boot''s relaxed binding maps `MFE_ADAPTER_MICROSERVICE_BASE_URL` → `mfe-adapter.microservice.base-url`\nso the MS location can be overridden for Docker without code changes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqB5H/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0k4QADQSbfufjxjuOE317ygDk0IT\nzkGo3DX99UgDwJL+f5p58VSCfYL9cpll0GprWkaX+7+LO2UqWXlXEWMsndDKBuoY\nkfR889keu9KFhqdEO36cEpTyJfxFXGJADuDqqqTmu4aAzzsvrdTnwq5sQDbgmnu3\nezQMR4dZqzxseH8XMOXB260JMGeC6YwU7APsTGWPuJQ29aQ2vY1YB8bS7eULKjtR\nix65bcjJwKsQFBINX8UQ8/smd3+BeRu/MO1/qi7qVH0/zK7SpqwzJJ8RSEzkEXxi\n4lAF6oW+sS+GDZLMkvyq7vpEWV1qSnW0FVYWTKgKXRRJQuIGDuk/h9wJ0de9p8bP\nSg7ka5y2atGXgQNZpud4fNSYBYwOvgGvCqbJ6T8x8IuMbIk/fRHZHu/S0y8THeDU\n629uHIcneubnIdJPX5qRq3RQdkCX2P0OEYYneWUy2FQY1isfF6DSq3ZE3yVirQZ+\nlxa/MtUnXSflk8COZKiP2cIWs96qnmoTj7F/mi6qZ/Clcz0Mx