://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MultiAgency/dashboard/commits/d3c8186d3177430fc14cb829b67cfc3fb89e2bcf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T02:23:37Z","email":"itexpert120@outlook.com","name":"Zeeshan Ahmad"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T02:23:37Z","email":"itexpert120@outlook.com","name":"Zeeshan Ahmad"},"message":"feat: client agreements (retainers and project agreements)\n\n- An Agreements tab on each client engagement: retainers and project\n  agreements with a date range, an agreed amount in one token and a note\n  (migration 0018). Owners and admins create, edit and delete them; one\n  with budget entries can''t be deleted or change token. Renew on a\n  retainer fills in the next cycle with the same amount, all editable.\n- A budget or deallocation on a project shared with a client must be\n  attached to one of that client''s agreements, in its token; its budget\n  date defaults to the agreement''s start. Internal projects keep plain\n  budgets. Transfers stay exempt for now.\n- Editing a budget entry can attach it to an agreement or move it, so\n  existing entries can be cleaned up. The history keeps the agreement.\n- Agreements show allocated of agreed. Reports, on both sides, can run\n  for an agreement: its dates, every budget attached to it in full, and\n  allocated of agreed. Saved reports carry the agreement''s engagement,\n  dates and title.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0fe8fa50b85891eeba85b7eb598e5dec6db100f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MultiAgency/dashboard/git/trees/f0fe8fa50b85891eeba85b7eb598e5dec6db100f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MultiAgency/dashboard/git/commits/d3c8186d3177430fc14cb829b67cfc3fb89e2bcf","verifica