.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/commits/9627abe3a689fb62278e0468f72f6c782c196b42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-04T18:17:38Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-04T18:17:38Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(lvt): drop Split-rate bar at shift endpoints (0 and 100)\n\nAt shift = 0 the Split-rate dataset is mathematically identical to\nToday''s uniform rate (landRate = uniformRate, impRate = uniformRate);\nat shift = 1 it equals Pure LVT. The middle bar is redundant at either\nendpoint and visually misreads as ''a third value'' even though it''s\nidentical to one of the others.\n\nParcelComparisonChart now takes a `shift: number` prop and excludes\nthe Split-rate dataset when |shift| is within ENDPOINT_EPSILON (0.001)\nof either boundary. Component.tsx passes inputs.shift through.\n\nTests:\n- existing two smoke tests updated with the new required prop\n- four new dataset-filtering tests via a vi.hoisted BarChart spy:\n  - mid-shift (0.5) → 3 datasets in canonical order\n  - shift 0 → Split-rate dropped, 2 datasets\n  - shift 1 → Split-rate dropped, 2 datasets\n  - shift 0.0009 (within epsilon) → Split-rate dropped\n\n35 calc-winston-salem-lvt tests pass; workspace 306/306 green;\ntypecheck clean; build succeeds.","tree":{"