ow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/calculators/commit/83e28807dc48a9bdaa91f73823c27561cef32304","node_id":"C_kwDOSSB8ZNoAKDgzZTI4ODA3ZGM0OGE5YmRhYTkxZjczODIzYzI3NTYxY2VmMzIzMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/calculators/commit/0bead3f19f2e1089a5ad7a1ab1b476dbd7933bb7","sha":"0bead3f19f2e1089a5ad7a1ab1b476dbd7933bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/commits/0bead3f19f2e1089a5ad7a1ab1b476dbd7933bb7"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/calculators/commit/3b22f1608b4506fa76538ca3210cf2560d8e8038","sha":"3b22f1608b4506fa76538ca3210cf2560d8e8038","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/commits/3b22f1608b4506fa76538ca3210cf2560d8e8038"}],"sha":"83e28807dc48a9bdaa91f73823c27561cef32304","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/commits/83e28807dc48a9bdaa91f73823c27561cef32304"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/commits/3b22f1608b4506fa76538ca3210cf2560d8e8038/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-04T14:40:04Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-04T14:40:04Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"fix(theme): chart tokens use @media instead of light-dark, federate the css\n\nTwo cancelling bugs surfaced as a clean asymmetry: native deploy had\nworking surfaces but no chart colors; federated host had working chart\ncolors but no surfaces. Different root causes, same theming layer.\n\nBug 1 — federated host gets no surface backgrounds.\n  theme.css was only imported by apps/remote/src/bootstrap.tsx, which is\n  the standalone-app entry. Module Federation doesn''t load bootstrap.tsx\n  when a host imports an expose like CalculatorsApp; it loads the chunk\n  that exposes the named module. Consequence: the host received every\n  CSS Module that referenced var(--calc-color-surface) etc., but no\n  module defined those variables on :root, so they fell back to unset\n  (transparent / browser-default). Surfaces, borders, brand accents —\n  all missing in federated mode.\n\n  Fix: theme.css is now a side-effect import of @calc/ui''s index.ts and\n  is also imported directly from CalculatorsApp.tsx, CalculatorsRoutes\n  .tsx, and CalculatorsLoadError.tsx. Any federation entry point pulls\n  it into the chunk graph. mf-manifest.json now lists theme-*.css as\n  a sync CSS asset on all three shell exposes, so the MF runtime\n  fetches and injects it on host import.\n\nBug 2 — native deploy renders charts with no series colors.\n  Chart.js dataset colors are read in JS via\n  getComputedStyle(:root).getPropertyValue(''--calc-chart-series-pi'').\n  getPropertyValue returns the *authored* value of the custom\n  property — NOT the resolved color. With light-dark(#2d6a4f, #34d399)\n  authored, Chart.js received the literal string\n  ''light-dark(#2d6a4f, #34d399)'' as backgroundColor, couldn''t parse\n  it as a color, and rendered bars with no fill. (In federated mode\n  the variable was undefined, so readToken''s fallback hex kicked in —\n  which is why charts worked there but not natively, the inverse of\n  bug 1.)\n\n  Fix: the ~17 chart-series, axis, and reserve-tier tokens now use\n  plain hex values, with a single @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)\n  block in :root that overrides them. getPropertyValue returns a real\n  hex string Chart.js handles correctly. Other tokens (surfaces,\n  borders, text, brand accents — consumed in CSS via var() and\n  resolved by the engine) keep their light-dark() values where the\n  syntax works correctly.\n\nVerified:\n- 302 tests pass; lint, typecheck clean\n- dist/assets/theme-*.css contains plain-hex chart tokens above the\n  @media block, light-dark() tokens for non-JS-read variables\n- mf-manifest.json shell exposes (CalculatorsApp, CalculatorsRoutes,\n  CalculatorsLoadError) carry theme-*.css as a sync CSS asset","tree":{"sha":"e1f6944b2a756ad41632bf87e05fc616794b7c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/git/trees/e1f6944b2a756ad41632bf87e05fc616794b7c1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/git/commits/3b22f1608b4506fa76538ca3210cf2560d8e8038","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https: