026-05-02T05:20:24Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(U11): Vercel deployment + multi-directive CSP + runbook\n\nvercel.json:\n- buildCommand pins the workspace install + remote build\n- outputDirectory targets apps/remote/dist (where MF emits remoteEntry\n  + manifest)\n- Multi-directive CSP per KTD #11 applied site-wide: default-src ''self'';\n  script-src ''self''; connect-src ''self''; img-src ''self'' data:;\n  style-src ''self'' ''unsafe-inline''; font-src ''self'' data:;\n  frame-ancestors ''self'' https://*.substack.com https://substack.com\n- Per-asset CORS headers on /remoteEntry.js, /mf-manifest.json, and\n  /assets/* (currently ''*'' for preview deploys; KTD #25 production gate\n  requires the portfolio-host-specific origin before merge-to-prod)\n- Asset cache: federation entry/manifest 5min must-revalidate (so URL\n  changes propagate quickly across MF runtime); /assets/* immutable\n  long-cache (hashed file names guarantee uniqueness)\n- SPA rewrite that explicitly excludes MF artifacts from the catch-all\n  via negative lookahead\n\ndocs/deployment.md — full runbook:\n- First-time Vercel project setup\n- CSP rationale per directive (transport-enforced \"inputs don''t leave\n  your browser\" via script-src + the deliberately-permissive\n  *.substack.com frame-ancestors)\n- CORS production gate procedure with curl verification commands\n- Four-check post-deploy verification list (CSP, CORS-prod, HTTPS,\n  Substack embed)\n- Vercel rollback procedure\n- Cloudflare Pages fallback notes per KTD #10\n- Operational notes (no env vars, no telemetry, KTD #7 commit history)\n\nProduction deployment requires: (a) an actual Vercel project + (b)\npost-deploy curl verification. Both are out-of-scope for an automated\nagent run; the runbook captures them so the user can execute end-to-end.\n\nRefs: U11, R7, R20, R21, AE5, F2, KTD #10, KTD #11, KTD #25.","tree":{"sha":"39ac694bd7507e6a8de3023819cc8cc0d0e1155b","url":"https: