":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/commits/a0b60f2627e3b4e1b2e1b47f9caf3f7ea743fb57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T04:19:19Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T04:19:19Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"green: calc-surry-county-offer domain\n\nPure port of Surry County Offer Calculator JS to TypeScript:\n- monthlyPayment: textbook amortization formula with 0-rate and\n  non-positive-principal defenses\n- netProceedsCalc: sale − payoff − sale·realtorPct − sale·transferPct\n- concessionLimit: conventional-loan brackets (≤75/80/>80)\n- validateOfferInputs: typed errors keyed by OfferInputs field\n- computeOffer: ScenarioOutput | typed error union; PMI activates above\n  80% LTV at 0.7%/yr per industry convention; repairCash can be negative\n  in the math layer (UI clamps to ≥0 for the cash-summary path) since\n  the breakdown card surfaces concession − closing as-is per HTML\n\nTolerance correction in fixture assertions: toBeCloseTo''s numDigits\nparameter is decimal-places-of-precision, not absolute delta. Currency\nfields use numDigits=2 ($0.005 tolerance); monthly payments use\nnumDigits=0 ($0.50 tolerance) to absorb (1+r)^n rounding drift.\n\nRefs: U4, AE3.","tree":{"sha":"b634fc4a9812d0910ad81859e8a2c631ebecebc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/git/trees/b634fc4a9812d0910ad81859e8a2c631ebecebc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/calculators/git/commits/a0b60f2627e3b4e1b2e1b47f9caf3f7ea743fb57","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_ur