s{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/b3ee42e4ecef14c7970ad5b8f691a9d5454dce70","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGIzZWU0MmU0ZWNlZjE0Yzc5NzBhZDViOGY2OTFhOWQ1NDU0ZGNlNzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/d6fb91c3d5f67726641483992869a9f2e80b5f6e","sha":"d6fb91c3d5f67726641483992869a9f2e80b5f6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/d6fb91c3d5f67726641483992869a9f2e80b5f6e"}],"sha":"b3ee42e4ecef14c7970ad5b8f691a9d5454dce70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/b3ee42e4ecef14c7970ad5b8f691a9d5454dce70"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/d6fb91c3d5f67726641483992869a9f2e80b5f6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T17:50:46Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T17:50:46Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"Phase 3 follow-up: friction fixes + curation-UI hardening\n\nTwo rounds of fixes addressing the validation session''s findings.\n\nRound 1 (five items from phase3-followup-instructions.md):\n  1. Detail view: canonical_summary + per-test source/expected\n     (read from <lang_dir>/tests/). hello_world sorts first.\n  2. Detail view: kata pack inline + \"Open in kata workspace\" link.\n     Reads <lang_dir>/katas.json. Lazy — appears when pack exists.\n  3. Backfill customization from slot plan (forge.catalog.backfill):\n     plan-file → DB rows whose theme/phrasebook/persona/era are NULL.\n     Investigation confirmed data missing from both DB and slot.json\n     (resolver normalized + runner didn''t preserve slot.json).\n  4. Row click handler syncs STATE.selectedIndex with the clicked\n     idx; subsequent J/K continues from there.\n  5. \"Try the language\" detail panel with Launch REPL + Open kata\n     workspace deep-links. app.js handleDeepLink IIFE reads\n     ?lang=&view=playground|katas on boot.\n\nRound 2 (issues surfaced during re-validation):\n  - Approve UX: status badge updates immediately on decide(); 1.2s\n    toast confirms action before auto-advance. Cache-bust v=p3-fu-3\n    so browsers pick up the new JS/CSS.\n  - /api/languages parameterized with ?include_catalog=approved|all|\n    none, default ''approved''. Library tab uses default (generated/\n    + approved catalog); catalog UI launch buttons pass ''all'' so\n    pending candidates are evaluable in the playground.\n  - Each language entry now carries source + catalog_status fields\n    so the frontend can label by provenance.\n  - _resolve_lang_root() helper at module level in forge/gui/app.py\n    resolves lang names against both generated/ and the catalog DB''s\n    batches.output_dir. Replaces 25 hardcoded\n    WORKSPACE/\"generated\"/<name> paths.\n  - /api/run + /api/run-all PYTHONPATH now include the lang_dir''s\n    parent so `from <slot_id>.parser import parse` resolves whether\n    the language lives in generated/ or in a catalog batch.\n\nTests: 24 new follow-up tests in tests/test_phase3_followup.py\n(17 round 1 + 7 round 2). 959 passing total (was 935 at Phase 3\nmerge), 0 failing.\n\nDB schema unchanged from Phase 3 (still at v2). The backfill is\na one-time data fix; the runner bug it works around should be\naddressed in Phase 4 (slot.json wasn''t preserved in\ncatalog_raw_gate2_v2/).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c09b48ee7a0a3a17f4c9d57554ddf7b5f0a2cf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/8c09b48ee7a0a3a17f4c9d57554ddf7b5f0a2cf0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/d6fb91c3d5f67726641483992869a9f2e80b5f6e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organi