wing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/ddb65a02f75bd0b1dca563d881cab84dfdb3820e","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGRkYjY1YTAyZjc1YmQwYjFkY2E1NjNkODgxY2FiODRkZmRiMzgyMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/3971e1fcd7753aa68e70200eaa62daf6778f4582","sha":"3971e1fcd7753aa68e70200eaa62daf6778f4582","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/3971e1fcd7753aa68e70200eaa62daf6778f4582"}],"sha":"ddb65a02f75bd0b1dca563d881cab84dfdb3820e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/ddb65a02f75bd0b1dca563d881cab84dfdb3820e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/3971e1fcd7753aa68e70200eaa62daf6778f4582/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T04:50:16Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T04:50:16Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"Phase 3 follow-up: five friction-fix items\n\nThe validation session in PHASE3_VALIDATION_NOTES.md surfaced that\nthe curation UI was mechanically functional but informationally\ninsufficient — the user couldn''t actually evaluate languages\nbecause key artifacts (REPL, kata pack, canonical test outputs)\nweren''t surfaced and themed/phrasebook customization wasn''t\nfilterable. Five targeted fixes per phase3-followup-instructions.md.\n\nItem 1 — Canonical test results in detail view:\n  catalog_routes._row_to_detail() now includes:\n    - canonical_summary: {passed, total, pass_rate} from quality_report\n    - canonical_tests: list of {name, source, expected} read directly\n      from <lang_dir>/tests/. hello_world sorts first.\n  catalog.js renderCanonicalTests() shows pass-rate badge + a\n  collapsible per-test source/expected list.\n\nItem 2 — Kata pack inline + workspace link:\n  catalog_routes._read_kata_pack() reads <lang_dir>/katas.json.\n  catalog.js renderKataPack() shows id/title/difficulty + 2 sample\n  test calls per kata. Includes \"Open in kata workspace\" deep-link\n  button (Option B per instructions).\n\nItem 3 — Backfill customization from slot plan:\n  Investigation confirmed the data was missing from BOTH the DB\n  columns AND slot.json (the runner didn''t preserve slot.json).\n  forge/catalog/db.py:backfill_customization_from_plan() reads\n  slots/v1_phase1.json and updates DB rows whose theme/phrasebook/\n  persona/era columns are NULL. New CLI: forge.catalog.backfill.\n  Applied to catalog.db: 19 rows updated, surfacing 5 themes + 2\n  phrasebooks + 7 personas + 7 eras in the facets endpoint.\n\nItem 4 — Click-vs-arrow-key cursor sync:\n  catalog.js row click handler now sets STATE.selectedIndex = idx\n  before calling openDetailByIndex(idx), so subsequent J/K\n  navigation continues from where the click landed. 2-line fix.\n\nItem 5 — Launch REPL deep-link:\n  catalog.js renderLaunchRepl() injects a \"Try the language\" panel\n  at the top of the detail spec pane with two buttons:\n    /?lang=<slot_id>&view=playground\n    /?lang=<slot_id>&view=kata\n  app.js gains a handleDeepLink IIFE that reads ?lang=&view= on\n  boot, waits for the language dropdown to populate, and calls\n  openInPlayground() or switches to the katas tab. Accepts both\n  view=kata and view=katas spellings.\n\n17 new tests in tests/test_phase3_followup.py covering each item.\n84 total tests passing across phase3 follow-up + Phase 3 + Phase 2 DB.\n\nDocumented runner bug (slot.json not preserved) for Phase 4 fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fbd08611a700956d14de0bfc42b19708710002b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/fbd08611a700956d14de0bfc42b19708710002b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/3971e1fcd7753aa68e70200eaa62daf6778f4582","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url