://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/bea3158471ac1ba646c1acc0cc6b3f121b071483","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGJlYTMxNTg0NzFhYzFiYTY0NmMxYWNjMGNjNmIzZjEyMWIwNzE0ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/f93ff0a471c29e0ed7f39a5975a8653b364f2923","sha":"f93ff0a471c29e0ed7f39a5975a8653b364f2923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/f93ff0a471c29e0ed7f39a5975a8653b364f2923"}],"sha":"bea3158471ac1ba646c1acc0cc6b3f121b071483","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/bea3158471ac1ba646c1acc0cc6b3f121b071483"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/f93ff0a471c29e0ed7f39a5975a8653b364f2923/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T22:01:57Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T22:01:57Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"Phase 1.1: slot planner + 50-slot v1 phase-1 hand-curated slot file\n\nThe slot planner is the front of the catalog production pipeline:\nload a slot file from disk, validate every slot''s shape and options,\nreturn typed Slot objects the batch runner consumes. Phase 4 will\nreplace the hand-curated file with a distribution-aware planner; the\nschema and entry points stay the same.\n\nforge/catalog/planner.py\n    Slot                  -- frozen dataclass (slot_id, options,\n                              customization, seed, target_rarity, notes)\n    SlotPlanError         -- aggregates ALL validation errors so a\n                              curator can fix everything in one editing\n                              pass rather than hunt-and-peck\n    make_slot_plan(path)  -- load + validate + return list[Slot]\n    slot_to_dict(slot)    -- round-trip serializer for tests\n\nValidation checks shape (every required key present, types match,\nslot_ids unique, target_rarity in the allowed set, customization\ndict has the uniform required keys) AND runs each slot''s options\nthrough spec_builder.build_spec so bogus enum values fail at\nplan-load rather than mid-batch.\n\nforge/catalog/slots/v1_phase1.json\n    50 hand-curated slots covering the four working syntax families:\n    20 c_like, 10 python_like, 10 s_expression, 10 stack_based.\n    Includes ≥3 with feature_bans, ≥5 with phrasebook customization,\n    ≥5 with less-common personas, ≥3 with hostile-constraint combos.\n    Seeds are unique. No families the pipeline doesn''t currently\n    handle (BASIC, shell, ML defer to Phase 4).\n\ntests/test_catalog_planner.py\n    21 tests covering validation aggregation, duplicate detection,\n    bogus-options rejection, missing-file behavior, malformed-JSON\n    handling, round-trip identity, build_spec kwarg translation\n    (including the theme→keyword_theme rename), and the v1 slot\n    file''s load time, family coverage, distribution shape, diversity\n    signals, seed uniqueness, and supported-families-only constraint.","tree":{"sha":"32a173dc7f4e664ad52164b2dc74ea75e64072de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/32a173dc7f4e664ad52164b2dc74ea75e64072de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/f93ff0a471c29e0ed7f39a5975a8653b364f2923","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/f93ff0a471c29e0ed7f39a5975a8653b364f2923","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGY5M2ZmMGE0NzFjMjllMGVkN2YzOWE1OTc1YTg2NTNiMzY0ZjI5MjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/f72a362576152f7a2e88de6485b50389acf02cf1","sha":"f72a362576152f7a2e88de6485b50389acf02cf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/f72a362576152f7a2e88de6485b50389acf02cf1"}],"sha":"f93ff0a471c29e0ed7f39a5975a8653b364f2923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/f93ff0a471c29e0ed7f39a5975a8653b364f2923"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/f72a362576152f7a2e88de6485b50389acf02cf1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T21:57:18Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T21:57:18Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"Phase 1 carryover: pin tag-prefix discipline, harden lazy client, drop psutil branch\n\nThree small items deferred from the Phase 0 closeout review. Land them\non phase-1 before any 1.x work begins so the next phase builds on a\nfully-closed-out Phase 0.\n\nC1: lift COMPONENT_TAG_PREFIXES to module scope in\nforge/orchestrator/generator.py and add tests/test_telemetry_tag_\nprefixes.py. Four tests pin: every component name has a prefix\nentry, no orphan entries, prefix values are well-formed, and every\nemitted tag literal in the generator source is covered by some\nregistered prefix. Rename the per-test fallback tag from\ngen-test-{name} to gen-tests-{name} so it actually matches the\n\"tests\" prefix entry rather than silently dropping out of telemetry\nattribution.\n\nC2: remove the speculative __getattr__ fallback from _LazyLLMClient\nin forge/orchestrator/subprocess_runner.py. The proxy now exposes\nan explicit protocol (log_dir, model, telemetry, call_code,\ncall_json, call_chat) and any other attribute access raises\nAttributeError without materializing the real client. Add __repr__\nthat reveals lazy/materialized state for debug traces. Ten tests\nin tests/test_lazy_llm_client_introspection.py pin: hasattr,\ngetattr-with-default, repr, bool, dir, __class__, and direct\nattribute access on unknown names all stay side-effect-free; only\ncall_* methods materialize.\n\nC3: remove the dead psutil branch from\ntests/test_phase0_closeout.py::test_50_sequential_subprocess_isolation.\npsutil isn''t a project dependency and the check was a no-op on\nmachines without it installed. The structural sys.modules and\ncross-contamination assertions cover the same intent more reliably.\nComment in place explaining the rationale and how to re-enable\nruntime tracking ad hoc if a real regression appears.\n\nTest count: 686 passing + 10 skipped (gated) on the non-slow suite.\n14 new tests across the two new files; no regressions.","tree":{"sha":"4a0cc3940a19feb120da891cddf032ae653f91bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/4a0cc3940a19feb120da891cddf032ae653f91bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/f72a362576152f7a2e88de6485b50389acf02cf1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/f72a362576152f7a2e88de6485b50389acf02cf1","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGY3MmEzNjI1NzYxNTJmN2EyZTg4ZGU2NDg1YjUwMzg5YWNmMDJjZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/e93d0ae6c441384d0cff4fe2bbad61f33928e48a","sha":"e93d0ae6c441384d0cff4fe2bbad61f33928e48a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/e93d0ae6c441384d0cff4fe2bbad61f33928e48a"}],"sha":"f72a362576152f7a2e88de6485b50389acf02cf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/f72a362576152f7a2e88de6485b50389acf02cf1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/e93d0ae6c441384d0cff4fe2bbad61f33928e48a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:57:06Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T20:57:06Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"Phase 0 production hardening, S-expression + stack-based families, kata pipeline\n\nAdds two new syntax families, rebuilds the kata system around mechanical\nrescue, and lands the production-roadmap Phase 0 work that turns Forge\ninto a batch-capable generator.\n\nLanguage families\n-----------------\nS-expression: hand-written lisplang reference compiler under\ngenerated/lisplang/ with templated-from path in the generator. Tests\ncover Lisp grammar, special-form codegen (var_decl/fn_expr/let), nil\nsemantics, and the canonical 8-test suite.\n\nStack-based: hand-written forthlang reference under\ngenerated/forthlang/ with a context-sensitive tokenizer (`.\"`, `s\"`,\nbalanced-paren stack-effect comments) and dict-modeled linked-list /\ntree nodes. Generated stacky/ exercises a stack-effect-inferring\ntypechecker. ensure_stack_runtime_support() idempotently injects the\ncanonical Forth vocabulary (nil/true/false/list/dict/get/dset/...)\ninto runtime.py + typechecker.py + codegen.py for any stack-based\nlanguage whose phrasebook customization renamed those words.\n\nKata system\n-----------\nCurated packs in kata_packs.py (CLASSICS_C_LIKE, CLASSICS_C_LIKE_RECURSIVE,\nSTACK_CLASSICS_FORTH). _batch_validate fast-path; auto-validation\npipeline tags every shipped kata with status/tests_run/tests_passed/via.\nRescue ladder in load-pack:\n  direct -> stack_base_solution.build_base_solution (cascade or\n  curated_match, stack_based only) -> case_analysis_fallback\n  -> stub_rescue (NOT for stack_based) -> drop.\n\nThe ''no auto-check'' state is unreachable for stack_based languages by\nconstruction. SHA256 pack-hash cache keys load-pack endpoint.\n?force=true bypasses; ?strict=true disables LLM translation.\n\nPhase 0 production hardening (per forge-production-roadmap.md)\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nTelemetry (0.4): TelemetryRecorder captures per-LLM-call tokens +\nduration, repair attempts, per-component time + LLM count (tag-prefix\nattribution to avoid parallel double-counting), errors, canonical and\nkata pass rates, seed used. Streams events to generation_events.jsonl\nas they happen for crash-survival recovery; flushes generation_summary\n.json at end of run. events_to_summary() aggregates the .jsonl back\ninto a partial summary.\n\nRepair budget (0.2): RepairBudget dataclass with .batch() preset\n(10x10x5min). repair_run accepts budget=. Default keeps interactive\n3x2 behavior unchanged.\n\nResolver caching (0.3): On-disk content-hash cache at .forge_cache/\nspecs/. Key is sha256(base_spec | RESOLVER_PROMPT_VERSION |\nRESOLVER_SCHEMA_VERSION). Bumping either version constant invalidates\nall entries so iterating on the prompt during Phase 1 doesn''t silently\nreturn stale outputs. clear_resolver_cache() CLI knob.\n\nReproduce (0.5): generate_all(seed=...) stamps the seed into the\nsummary. reproduce_from_summary() reads summary + sibling\nresolved_spec.json and re-runs with the same seed. Anthropic API\ndoesn''t expose a server-side seed; reproductions aren''t byte-identical\nbut local randomness (crossbreeding) honors the seed.\n\nSubprocess isolation (0.1): run_one() / run_batch() / write_batch_\nsummary() in subprocess_runner.py. Each generation runs in a clean\nPython subprocess that imports forge.orchestrator.generator, runs\ngenerate_all, writes outputs to disk, and exits. Verified on 50\nsequential templated generations: zero cross-contamination, zero\nsys.modules leak in the parent. _LazyLLMClient proxy defers LLMClient\ninstantiation until first call so templated families run without\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY.\n\nRepo prep\n---------\nReference compilers (lisplang, forthlang, stacky) tracked in git.\nPreviously gitignored as ''generated'' artifacts; their absence broke\nclean clones with 95 missing-fixture failures. Per-language regenerated\nartifacts (katas.json, generation_summary.json, .forge_log/, *.out.py,\n__pycache__) stay ignored, including toylang''s katas.json which was\nincorrectly tracked from an earlier commit.\n\nREADME rewritten under 100 lines. Removed stale test-count badge,\nfixed <this-repo> placeholder, dropped duplicated architecture content\n(now in PROJECT_REPORT.md / ARCHITECTURE.md). PROJECT_REPORT.md added\nas engineering documentation.\n\ntest_compile_error_hints now uses tracked stub specs under\ntests/fixtures/{love,hardcombo}/resolved_spec.json. Previously the\ntests assumed local LLM-generated languages (love, hardcombo) were\npresent and silently broke on clean clones. The hint function only\nreads three spec fields, so a 14-line stub is enough to exercise\nevery branch deterministically.\n\nTest budget: 711 passing on workspace, 695 passing + 18 skipped on\nclean clone (the 16-skip delta is intentional: tests gated on\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY plus the @slow 50-sequential isolation test).\nPhase 0 added 40 new tests over the prior 600-test baseline.","tree":{"sha":"789cac32f9ca5074503fdee4166746bf54b16da1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/789cac32f9ca5074503fdee4166746bf54b16da1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/e93d0ae6c441384d0cff4fe2bbad61f33928e48a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/e93d0ae6c441384d0cff4fe2bbad61f33928e48a","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGU5M2QwYWU2YzQ0MTM4NGQwY2ZmNGZlMmJiYWQ2MWYzMzkyOGU0OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/0f7df8f1e25c29e5863f673dfeaae69dcea2915e","sha":"0f7df8f1e25c29e5863f673dfeaae69dcea2915e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/0f7df8f1e25c29e5863f673dfeaae69dcea2915e"}],"sha":"e93d0ae6c441384d0cff4fe2bbad61f33928e48a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/e93d0ae6c441384d0cff4fe2bbad61f33928e48a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/0f7df8f1e25c29e5863f673dfeaae69dcea2915e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T01:35:56Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T01:35:56Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"feat: Phase 1 of standout roadmap (themed IDE + lore + library museum)\n\nThe roadmap''s recommendation was unambiguous: ship one Tier 1 feature\nend-to-end before anything else. Picked §3.1 Themed mini-IDE because\nit changes \"what the tool IS\" (config tool -> museum of programming\naesthetics) for the lowest effort and risk. Paired with §5.2 Lore\nframing and §5.1 Library as museum since all three reinforce\n\"languages are artifacts, not tuples.\"\n\nDeferred per the roadmap''s own advice: §3.2 family tree (cosmetic\nwithout §3.3), §3.3 crossbreeding, §3.4 esolang mode, §3.5 time\nmachine, §3.6 battles. Skipped per §6: multiplayer REPL, block editor,\nfull type-checker fix.\n\n## §3.1 Per-language visual theme\n\nNew `forge/orchestrator/style_tokens.py`. Each persona, era, theme,\nand phrasebook contributes a `style_tokens` dict:\n\n  - DEFAULT_TOKENS: the shadcn-dark base everything inherits from\n  - ERA_TOKENS: 1960s gets CRT phosphor green-on-black with scanlines;\n    1970s amber phosphor; 1980s IBM-PC blue/yellow; 2000s Web 2.0\n    glossy; 2020s shadcn dark\n  - PERSONA_TOKENS: dijkstra clean academic white-on-near-black serif;\n    mccarthy lisp-machine slate + magenta; hickey clojure slate + teal;\n    stroustrup borland-blue with yellow accent; wirth pascal-blue +\n    yellow; wadler haskell purple + serif; matz ruby red rounded;\n    ousterhout tcl/tk gray practical\n  - THEME_TOKENS: pirate parchment serif with paper grain; shakespearean\n    ink-on-cream; corporate helvetica-on-gray; latin Trajan-flavored\n    serif; cozy warm cream + terracotta\n  - PHRASEBOOK_TOKENS: english_storybook book-page ivory; shakespeare\n    inherits from theme; child_speak bright pink rounded; ritual deep\n    purple + gold calligraphic\n\n`style_tokens_for(persona, era, theme, phrasebook)` merges in priority\nDEFAULT < phrasebook < persona < era < theme. `render_theme_css(tokens)`\nturns the merged dict into a `body[data-lang-theme] { :root vars }`\nblock plus an optional `.theme-deco` overlay (scanlines, parchment).\n\nTokens propagate through `spec_builder.build_spec` -> `spec.theme.tokens`\n+ `spec.theme.sources`. Schema updated to allow the new field.\n\n## Generator + GUI plumbing\n\n`generator._render_theme_css` writes `<lang>/theme.css` next to\npackage files. New `GET /api/theme/<lang>.css` endpoint serves it,\nbackfilling on demand if missing. Front-end has a disabled\n`<link id=\"lang-theme-link\">` in <head>; new `applyLangTheme(lang)`\nhelper swaps href + sets `<body data-lang-theme=\"<lang>\">` and inserts\na `.theme-deco` div for scanline / parchment overlays. Wired into the\nplayground language picker and `loadKataPack` so the surface picks\nup the language''s identity whenever it becomes active.\n\n## §5.2 Lore framing\n\nResolver prompt now asks for a top-level `origin_story` field: 2-3\nsentences in-world, presented deadpan as if the language were\nDISCOVERED rather than configured. Examples in the prompt:\n\"Found in a 1973 timeline where Lisp won the AI Winter.\"\n\"Recovered from the bilge of the Black Pearl.\"\nSchema updated. `/api/languages` now surfaces origin_story per entry.\n\n## §5.1 Library as museum\n\nEach Library card now leads with the language''s lore (origin_story,\nitalic), shows a mini-preview swatch rendered in the language''s actual\npalette (inline-styled so the GUI doesn''t need to load the per-lang\nCSS just to render the card), then spec-axis tags + actions. Top of\neach card has a 3px accent bar in the language''s own accent color\nfor instant visual differentiation across the grid.\n\nBackfilled origin_story + theme.css for the eight existing languages\nin `generated/`.\n\nTests: 404 passing, 9 skipped. No regressions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"99470d85d13dc06c63111fb7e310e13de51d711d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/99470d85d13dc06c63111fb7e310e13de51d711d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/0f7df8f1e25c29e5863f673dfeaae69dcea2915e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/0f7df8f1e25c29e5863f673dfeaae69dcea2915e","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKDBmN2RmOGYxZTI1YzI5ZTU4NjNmNjczZGZlYWFlNjlkY2VhMjkxNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/5df3ca8bcc510ab83385cdd90fc61cb7d9570f07","sha":"5df3ca8bcc510ab83385cdd90fc61cb7d9570f07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/5df3ca8bcc510ab83385cdd90fc61cb7d9570f07"}],"sha":"0f7df8f1e25c29e5863f673dfeaae69dcea2915e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/0f7df8f1e25c29e5863f673dfeaae69dcea2915e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/5df3ca8bcc510ab83385cdd90fc61cb7d9570f07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T01:35:14Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T01:35:14Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"docs: add ARCHITECTURE.md deep-dive\n\nA 910-line tour of every module, what it does, and how the pieces fit\ntogether. Twelve sections:\n\n  1. What is Language Forge\n  2. Top-level project layout\n  3. Two main user journeys (create a language / solve a kata)\n  4. Orchestrator module-by-module (14 modules detailed)\n  5. The Flask GUI (every endpoint + front-end architecture)\n  6. The hand-written toylang reference\n  7. Templates\n  8. Tests + audit suite\n  9. End-to-end flows (\"who calls whom\" call graphs)\n 10. Where the seams are (concrete improvement angles)\n 11. File-by-file reference table\n 12. Glossary (kata, stub-rescue, case-analysis, escalating fix-up,\n     rederive expected, runtime-shim, canonical test)\n\nSection 10 is the most actionable: nine improvement ideas from\nstatic-typed-language type inference to streaming kata generation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4bcfc71b053a76140e592f5f0c400272cd537c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/f4bcfc71b053a76140e592f5f0c400272cd537c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/5df3ca8bcc510ab83385cdd90fc61cb7d9570f07","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/5df3ca8bcc510ab83385cdd90fc61cb7d9570f07","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKDVkZjNjYThiY2M1MTBhYjgzMzg1Y2RkOTBmYzYxY2I3ZDk1NzBmMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/fc35f9239263dbfd9b77ab84d545ed6ef79b58a8","sha":"fc35f9239263dbfd9b77ab84d545ed6ef79b58a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/fc35f9239263dbfd9b77ab84d545ed6ef79b58a8"}],"sha":"5df3ca8bcc510ab83385cdd90fc61cb7d9570f07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/5df3ca8bcc510ab83385cdd90fc61cb7d9570f07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/fc35f9239263dbfd9b77ab84d545ed6ef79b58a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T23:01:12Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T23:01:12Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"feat(katas): show sample tests + mechanical case-analysis fallback\n\nTwo user-facing problems:\n\n1. Test cases were hidden until you clicked Run. Now visible upfront.\n2. The \"no auto-check\" stub still appeared on languages where mechanical\n   translation + LLM both gave up (typically heavily customized langs).\n\n## Sample tests in the Description tab\n\nAdded a \"Sample tests\" section under Constraints showing the public\ntest cases (those listed in `sample_test_indices`) with input → output\nformatting:\n\n    Sample tests\n    #1  Input    two_sum([2, 7, 11, 15], 9)\n        Output   [0, 1]\n    #2  Input    two_sum([3, 2, 4], 6)\n        Output   [1, 2]\n    + 2 hidden tests, run via Submit.\n\nHidden tests stay hidden; only the count is shown. Submit grades\nagainst everything; Run only grades against the visible ones.\n\n## Mechanical case-analysis fallback\n\nNew `forge/orchestrator/case_analysis.py` module. Generates a function\nthat hardcodes the answer for each test by discriminating on argument\nshape, e.g.:\n\n    func two_sum(nums, target) {\n        if (target == 9 && len(nums) == 4 && get(nums, 0) == 2 && ...) {\n            return list(0, 1);\n        }\n        if (target == 6 && len(nums) == 3 && get(nums, 0) == 3 && ...) {\n            return list(1, 2);\n        }\n        return list();\n    }\n\nAlways works for Turing-complete targets that have if/equality/return,\nplus `len()` + `get()` (universal stdlib in our generated languages).\nAnswers are precomputed by running the canonical c_like reference on\ntoylang.\n\nPipeline:\n  1. Parse canonical reference''s params + each test''s call args via\n     toylang''s parser (with the new universal unwrapper that descends\n     through passthru/logical_or/.../call when there are no operators —\n     fixes the \"complex arg: 1\" bug for bare integer args).\n  2. Run canonical on toylang, capture stdout per test for the answers.\n  3. Emit c_like source with cascading if-statements.\n  4. Transpile to target via the existing mechanical_translator\n     backends (CLikeBackend / PhrasebookBackend / PythonLikeBackend).\n  5. For static-typed python_like targets (e.g. hardcombo), hand-emit\n     typed Python directly using simple inference: param types from\n     test arg literals (int/string/list/dict/bool), return type from\n     the first expected output''s shape.\n  6. Re-derive expected outputs by running the candidate; absorbs any\n     print-formatter differences across languages.\n  7. Self-validate. Returns None if even this fails (caller falls back\n     to stub-rescue).\n\nThe kata gets `case_analysis_fallback: true` so the GUI can label it.\nAuto-check works; the answer is \"memorized\" rather than computed but\nthe grader still grades the user''s submission correctly.\n\n## Wired in two places\n\n- `kata_translator.translate_pack`: case-analysis runs after the\n  single-test reduction step, before stub_rescue.\n- `gui.app.load_kata_pack`: case-analysis runs after the curated/translated\n  validation passes, before stub_rescue.\n\n## Smoke results across all 7 generated languages (LLM stubbed)\n\n| lang       | time   | visible | functional | stubs |\n|------------|--------|---------|------------|-------|\n| toylang    | 0.6s   | 12      | 12         | 0     |\n| democ      | 1.0s   | 12      | 12         | 0     |\n| god        | 1.0s   | 12      | 12         | 0     |\n| smoke      | 1.0s   | 12      | 12         | 0     |\n| love       | 1.0s   | 12      | 12         | 0     |\n| kidX       | 4.0s   | 12      | 12         | 0     |\n| hardcombo  | 5.4s   | 12      | 2          | 10    |\n\nhardcombo is the only outlier — its LLM-generated typechecker has bugs\n(rejects `len(list)` because it expects only `len(string)`, `dict()` is\nundefined). That''s a Repair-button job, not something this layer can\nfix mechanically. 6 of 7 languages now have the full pack with no\nstubs; hardcombo improved from 0 to 2 functional.\n\n## Tests\n\n123 passing. Existing assertions that expected `stub_rescued: true` for\nunrescuable katas got relaxed to \"case_analysis_fallback OR stub_rescued\"\nsince case-analysis is the preferred path. Two new tests cover the\ncase-analysis happy path and the unparseable-reference bail-out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0436979d8f39cade67ba686f7a8d7426c2a740d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/0436979d8f39cade67ba686f7a8d7426c2a740d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/fc35f9239263dbfd9b77ab84d545ed6ef79b58a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/fc35f9239263dbfd9b77ab84d545ed6ef79b58a8","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGZjMzVmOTIzOTI2M2RiZmQ5Yjc3YWI4NGQ1NDVlZDZlZjc5YjU4YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/4d5a314ef9bb03951d7916fe1ce682e91be6b07a","sha":"4d5a314ef9bb03951d7916fe1ce682e91be6b07a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/4d5a314ef9bb03951d7916fe1ce682e91be6b07a"}],"sha":"fc35f9239263dbfd9b77ab84d545ed6ef79b58a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/fc35f9239263dbfd9b77ab84d545ed6ef79b58a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/4d5a314ef9bb03951d7916fe1ce682e91be6b07a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T22:27:37Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T22:27:37Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"fix: standalone REPL theme + cap kata translation wall-clock budget\n\nTwo fixes the user hit:\n\n1. **REPL HTML stuck on the old orange theme.** The browser-Pyodide REPL\n   served by /api/standalone/<lang> uses its own embedded CSS in\n   forge/templates/standalone_repl.html.j2 — independent of the main\n   GUI''s static/style.css that the previous retheme touched. Updated\n   the template''s :root variables, body gradient, primary button,\n   focus ring, and inline status colors to match the shadcn dark\n   palette (royal blue accent, slate surfaces, green/amber/red status\n   pills). Re-rendered generated/toylang/repl.html.\n\n2. **Kata generation could spin for 5+ minutes.** Each failing kata\n   could chew up to 17 LLM calls (5 escalating fix-ups + per-kata\n   fresh translation + 5 more fix-ups + single-test reduction + ...).\n   On a freshly-created language with broken codegen, all 12 katas\n   would fail and the wall time would compound.\n\n   Fixes in translate_pack:\n     - Default fix_attempts trimmed from 5 to 3.\n     - New time_budget_s parameter (default 90s). When exceeded,\n       remaining katas skip the LLM-heavy retry paths and go straight\n       to stub-rescue.\n     - Per-kata fresh-translation safety net no longer fires for katas\n       that the BATCH already produced output for (just couldn''t fix);\n       redundant work, jumps to single-test-reduction or stub-rescue\n       instead.\n\n   Same wall-clock guard added to generate_katas (default 120s for the\n   ✨ Generate path).\n\n   Net effect: a stubborn language hits the budget, stub-rescues the\n   rest, and the user sees the kata library populate within ~90-120s\n   instead of grinding indefinitely. All 12 problems still appear; ones\n   the LLM can''t translate get the \"no auto-check\" badge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a91713d3919e64e5c2ca8e1644d3fd330d265b1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/a91713d3919e64e5c2ca8e1644d3fd330d265b1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/4d5a314ef9bb03951d7916fe1ce682e91be6b07a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/4d5a314ef9bb03951d7916fe1ce682e91be6b07a","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKDRkNWEzMTRlZjliYjAzOTUxZDc5MTZmZTFjZTY4MmU5MWJlNmIwN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/bb1a765b3ff68725352dae48eb399eb1f9eba019","sha":"bb1a765b3ff68725352dae48eb399eb1f9eba019","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/bb1a765b3ff68725352dae48eb399eb1f9eba019"}],"sha":"4d5a314ef9bb03951d7916fe1ce682e91be6b07a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/4d5a314ef9bb03951d7916fe1ce682e91be6b07a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/bb1a765b3ff68725352dae48eb399eb1f9eba019/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T22:12:08Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T22:12:08Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"ui: retheme to shadcn-style dark palette (pranav.info inspired)\n\nDrop the LeetCode neutral-gray look in favour of shadcn/ui dark mode:\nblue-tinted near-black surfaces, subtle blue-gray borders, royal-blue\naccent. The reference site (pranav.info) uses the standard shadcn/ui\ndefault dark theme — same one we now mirror.\n\nSurface tokens (HSL → hex):\n  --bg     #0a0e16   was #1a1a1a   (was neutral, now blue-tinted)\n  --bg-2   #0d1220   was #202020\n  --card   #0a0e16   matches bg; cards differentiated by 1px border\n  --line   #1e293b   was #353535   (slate-800)\n  --line-2 #2a3a55   was #404040\n  --text   #f8fafc   was #f5f5f5   (slightly cooler)\n  --muted  #94a3b8   was #8a8a8a   (slate-400)\n\nAccent shifted from teal #00b8a3 → royal blue #3b82f6 (Tailwind blue-500,\nshadcn ring colour). Difficulty signals updated to standard shadcn-friendly\ngreen/amber/red so they stay distinct from the blue accent: easy=#22c55e,\nmedium=#f59e0b, hard=#ef4444.\n\nComponent changes:\n  - Primary button: white-on-blue with subtle 3px ring on hover (shadcn\n    \"primary\" pattern), no transform-on-hover. 13.5px font.\n  - Body gradient: single subtle blue radial from the top, removed the\n    stacked teal+blue gradients.\n  - Topbar background: blue-tinted alpha to blend with the new bg.\n  - Brand logo: blue gradient (was teal).\n  - Library section header (\"Problems\"): now uppercase tracked\n    (font-size 11px, letter-spacing 0.08em, muted colour) — matches\n    pranav.info''s \"PROJECTS\" / \"NAVIGATION\" / \"CONTACT\" labels.\n  - All `rgba(0, 184, 163, ...)` (teal) refs converted: ones tied to\n    .easy go to green-500, the rest go to blue-500.\n  - All `rgba(255, 184, 0, ...)` (LeetCode amber) → amber-500\n    `rgba(245, 158, 11, ...)`.\n  - All `rgba(255, 55, 95, ...)` (LeetCode coral) → red-500\n    `rgba(239, 68, 68, ...)`.\n  - Radius bumped to 12px / 8px / 6px (was 14/10/6) for a slightly\n    tighter shadcn feel.\n  - Shadows toned down to 1px subtle (was 12px 40px).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd0155c631f707bfa8155eb623ab7c91db9a9a39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/cd0155c631f707bfa8155eb623ab7c91db9a9a39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/bb1a765b3ff68725352dae48eb399eb1f9eba019","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/bb1a765b3ff68725352dae48eb399eb1f9eba019","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGJiMWE3NjViM2ZmNjg3MjUzNTJkYWU0OGViMzk5ZWIxZjllYmEwMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/9cdb4ceea5ea2ce24b83612dfbe3828597dc3615","sha":"9cdb4ceea5ea2ce24b83612dfbe3828597dc3615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/9cdb4ceea5ea2ce24b83612dfbe3828597dc3615"}],"sha":"bb1a765b3ff68725352dae48eb399eb1f9eba019","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/bb1a765b3ff68725352dae48eb399eb1f9eba019"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/9cdb4ceea5ea2ce24b83612dfbe3828597dc3615/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T21:50:45Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T21:50:45Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"ui(katas): retheme to LeetCode palette + tighten button alignment\n\nSwitch the primary accent from coral orange to LeetCode signature teal\n(#00B8A3). Add three named difficulty colors (easy=#00B8A3 teal,\nmedium=#FFB800 amber, hard=#FF375F red) and use them on the kata-list\nrows, problem-detail title pill, result panels, source badges, and\nsubmission history.\n\nSurfaces shifted to neutral grays (#1A1A1A bg, #262626 cards, #353535\nlines) to drop the blue undertone — matches LeetCode''s dark-mode look.\nBackground gradient retuned to teal/blue, ::selection now uses teal,\nbrand logo gradient swapped to teal-to-darker-teal.\n\nKata workspace cleanup:\n\n  - Topbar: equal 32px height across language picker, pack picker, Load\n    button, Generate button. Consistent gaps (10px) and labels styled\n    as small uppercase muted text.\n  - Library list: 3px row padding instead of 4px, hover uses bg-2\n    swatch, active row uses teal-tinted background. Kata title goes\n    teal when solved.\n  - Tag chips: rounded full-radius (LeetCode-style), subtle blue tint,\n    11px font.\n  - Tabs (Description/Submissions/Solution): teal underline on active,\n    muted on inactive, smooth color transition on hover.\n  - Action row: Submit pinned right via `.kata-actions .primary {\n    margin-left: auto }`; Run/Reset/Ask sit left as ghosts. All four\n    buttons share 34px height so they align cleanly.\n  - Result panel: passed = teal left-border on tinted background;\n    failed = red left-border. Per-test result rows colored to match.\n  - Helpers info callout: teal-tinted to indicate provided code,\n    inline `<code>` chips highlighted in accent green.\n  - Drop list (untranslated katas): amber-tinted to match medium\n    difficulty signal.\n\nRemoved the duplicate `.kata-row` / `.kata-actions` / `.kata-title-row`\nselectors that had been fighting each other since the LeetCode-style\nredesign was first stacked on top of the original kata UI. The block\nis now a single canonical 280-line section.\n\nCleaned up stray `rgba(255, 122, 69, ...)` references — every accent\nswatch now resolves to the teal palette.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eea4bed86791d21043e37e9a575e3eb4c9dc2f10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/eea4bed86791d21043e37e9a575e3eb4c9dc2f10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/9cdb4ceea5ea2ce24b83612dfbe3828597dc3615","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/9cdb4ceea5ea2ce24b83612dfbe3828597dc3615","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKDljZGI0Y2VlYTVlYTJjZTI0YjgzNjEyZGZiZTM4Mjg1OTdkYzM2MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/dce657abf39e7a7f0478aa2b732c94ffdfe3c896","sha":"dce657abf39e7a7f0478aa2b732c94ffdfe3c896","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/dce657abf39e7a7f0478aa2b732c94ffdfe3c896"}],"sha":"9cdb4ceea5ea2ce24b83612dfbe3828597dc3615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/9cdb4ceea5ea2ce24b83612dfbe3828597dc3615"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/dce657abf39e7a7f0478aa2b732c94ffdfe3c896/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T21:38:22Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T21:38:22Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"test(audit): add kata + language-generation audit suite\n\nTwo standalone audit scripts plus a README explaining how to run them\nand what they cover. They walk every interesting code path in their\nrespective subsystems, exercise it, and write a single human-readable\nreport file with intent + result + fix per check.\n\nThese run outside pytest because their job is to write a structured\nreport across many subsystem boundaries (spec_builder, coherence,\npresets, customization, mechanical translator, runtime patcher, GUI\nendpoints, persisted state, every existing generated/<lang>/), not to\nassert in isolation.\n\nTogether they exercise:\n\n  - Kata audit (49 checks): helpers field plumbing, mode=run vs\n    mode=submit semantics, kata data-model completeness,\n    content-hashed cache invalidation, no_mutation -> recursive-variant\n    routing, mechanical translator backend selection (CLike /\n    Phrasebook / PythonLike / static-typed bail), runtime\n    string-indexing patcher idempotency, stub-rescue path, GUI-side\n    concerns (tag filter refresh, force-reload kata refresh, draft-key\n    cleanup, result panel reset), and every classic on toylang for\n    both iterative and recursive variants.\n\n  - Language-generation audit (43 checks): cartesian (syntax x typing\n    x memory) builds + validates, every extended option setting, every\n    loop-form subset, coherence rules (hard-error vs warning combos),\n    8 personas, 5 eras, 5 themes, 4 phrasebooks, 6 bans, every\n    customization layer (keyword overrides, operator overrides, file\n    extension, naming convention, null model, extra design notes,\n    natural_language phrasebook, feature_bans), components_for\n    ordering for static vs dynamic, every component prompt loads +\n    interpolates, verifier on toylang plus every existing generated\n    language, repair component picker, GUI listing endpoints.\n\nReports are regenerated next to the scripts on each run; running both\ntakes well under a minute. Both currently exit 0 (no bugs).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f04f9cb9ee94c70d3a92e631e81ef7050cd611f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/f04f9cb9ee94c70d3a92e631e81ef7050cd611f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/dce657abf39e7a7f0478aa2b732c94ffdfe3c896","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/dce657abf39e7a7f0478aa2b732c94ffdfe3c896","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGRjZTY1N2FiZjM5ZTdhN2YwNDc4YWEyYjczMmM5NGZmZGZlM2M4OTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/c576ec4dc8935d9e20fdd30d358e30fbf855d345","sha":"c576ec4dc8935d9e20fdd30d358e30fbf855d345","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/c576ec4dc8935d9e20fdd30d358e30fbf855d345"}],"sha":"dce657abf39e7a7f0478aa2b732c94ffdfe3c896","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/dce657abf39e7a7f0478aa2b732c94ffdfe3c896"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/c576ec4dc8935d9e20fdd30d358e30fbf855d345/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-02T21:37:01Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-02T21:37:56Z","email":"theagingboy05@gmail.com","name":"Joel-Wwalker"},"message":"Initial commit: language-forge\n\nGenerate working compilers from a small set of design choices. Forge\ntakes three core options (syntax, typing, memory model) plus optional\ncustomization layers and produces a runnable transpiler: lexer, parser,\ncodegen, runtime, stdlib, canonical tests, README, and a self-contained\nHTML REPL. A verifier runs eight reference programs against the result;\na repair loop rewrites broken components and re-runs.\n\nIncludes:\n\n  - Spec builder + JSON-Schema validation for every option combination\n  - Coherence pre-validator that catches contradictions before any LLM\n    call (no_exceptions + exceptions, no_mutation + mutable default,\n    etc.)\n  - LLM resolver that fills in spec gaps from the high-level options\n  - Parallel per-component generator with sibling-context awareness\n  - Verifier that runs canonical tests and attributes failures to the\n    likely component (lexer / parser / typechecker / codegen / runtime)\n  - Repair loop that picks the failing component and rewrites it\n  - Customization layers: keyword overrides, operator overrides, file\n    extension, naming convention, null model, extra design notes\n  - Presets: 8 designer personas, 5 era presets, 5 keyword themes,\n    4 natural-language phrasebooks, 6 feature bans\n  - Hand-written toylang as the canonical c_like reference compiler\n  - Flask GUI with split-screen Create / Library / Playground / Katas\n    views, SSE-streamed generation progress, in-browser CodeMirror\n    editor, per-language Pyodide REPL, and an LLM pair-programmer chat\n  - Kata system: LeetCode-style problem library with auto-grader.\n    Curated classics pack with mechanical translator backends for\n    c_like, phrasebook, and python_like target families. Per-kata\n    helpers (linked-list / tree node constructors) prepended to user\n    submissions so the test wrapper always resolves. Recursive variant\n    of the classics for no_mutation languages. Stub-rescue keeps\n    untranslatable problems visible (no auto-check) instead of dropping\n    them. Run vs Submit modes (sample tests vs full hidden suite).\n    Content-hashed cache invalidates when the source pack changes.\n\nRun `python -m forge gui` and open http://localhost:5173/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43d1315a6bc1552b89c9ab5386cd1d00e15d0cae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/trees/43d1315a6bc1552b89c9ab5386cd1d00e15d0cae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/git/commits/c576ec4dc8935d9e20fdd30d358e30fbf855d345","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127682092?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker","id":127682092,"login":"Joel-Wwalker","node_id":"U_kgDOB5xGLA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joel-Wwalker","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commit/c576ec4dc8935d9e20fdd30d358e30fbf855d345","node_id":"C_kwDOSSsrdNoAKGM1NzZlYzRkYzg5MzVkOWUyMGZkZDMwZDM1OGUzMGZiZjg1NWQzNDU","parents":[],"sha":"c576ec4dc8935d9e20fdd30d358e30fbf855d345","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits/c576ec4dc8935d9e20fdd30d358e30fbf855d345"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/Joel-Wwalker/language-forge/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=9c1a56bca19b2b58495c6a0ecc242cf20d3c9641&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T16%3A25%3A07.588Z"}');
