https://api.github.com/users/ItsThompson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ItsThompson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ItsThompson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ItsThompson/gofin/commits/d2c3e113b5a2b058ab0b0e33fa916d5a44401723/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T20:33:32Z","email":"hi.thompson@hotmail.com","name":"thompson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T20:46:04Z","email":"hi.thompson@hotmail.com","name":"thompson"},"message":"refactor: address review feedback on validator rollout\n\nThree fixes from code review:\n\n- Delete budgetAmountError and inline the validator at its two call sites\n  (UpdateDefaults, UpdatePeriod). The v.Check(false, ...) constant made the\n  validator a verbose map builder with unreachable return nil; inlining puts\n  the condition at the check site and makes all three budgetAmount sites\n  consistent with CreatePeriodWithProRata.\n\n- Migrate the expense service''s validateTransactionCurrency to the shared\n  validator and delete its unsupportedCurrencyError helper. The expense\n  service still built the fields map with a raw composite literal; it now\n  follows the finance validateSupportedCurrency pattern, preserving the\n  ErrUnsupportedCurrency code and the exact wire contract\n  ({transactionCurrency: \"unsupported currency\"}).\n\n- docs/validation.md: add trailing newline, update the validator locations\n  table, document the error-mapper exception (mapFxError) alongside the\n  transport-detection exception, and add a No v.Check(false, ...) rule so\n  the anti-pattern does not reappear.","tree":{"sha":"d9d2b15d482689d1bf5e5afb7080fa4d63a6f984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ItsThompson/gofin/git/trees/d9d2b15d482689d1bf5e5afb7080fa4d63a6f984"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ItsThompson/gofin/git/commits/d2c3e113b5a2b058ab0b0e33fa916d5a44401723","verification":{"payload":null