tal/tongue/nasal) in the seed, trending as the MAD\n  treats palatal best (its share declines; tongue-base is the holdout).\n- useSnoreDetector now classifies each live snore by the spectral band where its\n  energy sits → a live type mix on the Night screen as you snore.\n- Science screen: the acoustic fingerprint + breakdown are now data-driven, with\n  a 14-night type-mix trend ribbon and a cosine \"% like your baseline\" readout.\n- Store key bumped v2 -> v3 for the new Night shape.\n\nProactive coach + suggested prompts (Chat):\n- Tappable starter-question chips above the composer (lightly data-tailored).\n- A data-driven proactive opener from Dr. Sommers on open (weekend+wine heads-up,\n  snore-spike note, streak milestone, or a calm check-in) — rule-based, no API.\n\nOnboarding questionnaire:\n- Real 7-step triage at /onboarding that writes onboarding.answers, then routes\n  to the findings screen — which now derives its read from the actual answers.\n- Findings moved to /onboarding/findings.\n\nBuilds clean (tsc + vite, 445 modules). Verified each surface renders on-brand:\nScience breakdown 52/40/9 + ribbon, the proactive wine opener + chips, the\n7-step questionnaire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2a6d81f1780cae664bbd728e9b1905a2a760c15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/b2a6d81f1780cae664bbd728e9b1905a2a760c15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/fde24d9e8facd5fe22ec3ec69099db9955d01917","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/fde24d9e8facd5fe22ec3ec69099db9955d01917","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKGZkZTI0ZDllOGZhY2Q1ZmUyMmVjM2VjNjkwOTlkYjk5NTVkMDE5MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/63cceaf5cf9e2b2b5733e669d5b07c74b2091f79","sha":"63cceaf5cf9e2b2b5733e669d5b07c74b2091f79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/63cceaf5cf9e2b2b5733e669d5b07c74b2091f79"}],"sha":"fde24d9e8facd5fe22ec3ec69099db9955d01917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/fde24d9e8facd5fe22ec3ec69099db9955d01917"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/63cceaf5cf9e2b2b5733e669d5b07c74b2091f79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T08:45:27Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T08:45:27Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"message":"Replace demo gear FAB with a 5th \"Demo\" tab; tighten bottom tab bar\n\n- Remove the floating demo gear (DemoControls) and add a fifth bottom tab,\n  \"Demo\" (cog icon), opening a proper /demo screen with the staging actions\n  (simulate a new night, jump to live tracking, replay onboarding, reset) plus\n  quick-jumps to every screen. Cleaner than a FAB overlapping the content.\n- Tab bar is now 5 columns and sits flush at the bottom: reduced the bottom\n  padding so the icons rest just above the home indicator (was floating ~24px+\n  up), while the bar background still fills the safe area.\n\nVerified at mobile width: 5 tabs (Home/Trends/Chat/Profile/Demo), no gear FAB,\ntab bar height 58px + safe-bottom, Demo tab renders its screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e2f75122555b00e2df6b7c371a1e3629fc14358","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/9e2f75122555b00e2df6b7c371a1e3629fc14358"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/63cceaf5cf9e2b2b5733e669d5b07c74b2091f79","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/63cceaf5cf9e2b2b5733e669d5b07c74b2091f79","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKDYzY2NlYWY1Y2Y5ZTJiMmI1NzMzZTY2OWQ1YjA3Yzc0YjIwOTFmNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/8f60cb16475fd7b288b3df75e9bac756c63efcd6","sha":"8f60cb16475fd7b288b3df75e9bac756c63efcd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/8f60cb16475fd7b288b3df75e9bac756c63efcd6"}],"sha":"63cceaf5cf9e2b2b5733e669d5b07c74b2091f79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/63cceaf5cf9e2b2b5733e669d5b07c74b2091f79"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/8f60cb16475fd7b288b3df75e9bac756c63efcd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T08:16:06Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T08:16:06Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"message":"Native fullscreen PWA on mobile: kill navy bands, gear to top\n\nThe phone showed navy bands top and bottom — the old \"device frame\" bezel\nleaking onto a real screen: .device kept a navy background and padded the\nsafe areas with it.\n\n- Edge-to-edge: drop the .device bezel padding + navy background on mobile so\n  the screen''s own gradient fills the safe areas (light on the day dashboard).\n- Status bar style black-translucent -> default, so the iOS status-bar text is\n  dark and readable on the light top (black-translucent forces white text,\n  which is why the design needed a dark band behind it).\n- Tab bar extends into the home-indicator area with its own light background\n  and pads its labels above the indicator (no navy strip at the bottom).\n- Demo gear moves to top-right on mobile (next to Track sleep) instead of\n  floating over the bottom edge.\n\nVerified at 390px: device padding 0, background transparent, tab bar uses\ncalc(.. + safe-bottom), full render, no errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb5c8f1002899689160c872baa2921ac27691d86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/bb5c8f1002899689160c872baa2921ac27691d86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/8f60cb16475fd7b288b3df75e9bac756c63efcd6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/8f60cb16475fd7b288b3df75e9bac756c63efcd6","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKDhmNjBjYjE2NDc1ZmQ3YjI4OGIzZGY3NWU5YmFjNzU2YzYzZWZjZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/4e44e4736f03e24d8564e57f0ed0756f787b67db","sha":"4e44e4736f03e24d8564e57f0ed0756f787b67db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/4e44e4736f03e24d8564e57f0ed0756f787b67db"}],"sha":"8f60cb16475fd7b288b3df75e9bac756c63efcd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/8f60cb16475fd7b288b3df75e9bac756c63efcd6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/4e44e4736f03e24d8564e57f0ed0756f787b67db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T07:49:36Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T07:49:36Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"message":"Fix iOS blank: backfill stale persisted state + bump store version\n\nRoot cause of the WebKit crash (\"undefined is not an object — A.name\"): an\niPhone had localStorage from an older deploy that predates the `partner`\n(Sarah) field. The schema guard only checked for `user` + `nights`, so the\nstale state passed, then Dashboard read `state.partner.name` → crash → blank.\nFresh state (desktop) always had `partner`, so it never reproduced there.\n\n- Merge any loaded state over a fresh seed (`{...buildSeedState(), ...loaded}`)\n  so a field missing from an older persisted shape is backfilled with a default\n  instead of being undefined at access.\n- Bump the storage key v1 → v2 so currently-broken devices reseed cleanly.\n\nVerified: with a persisted state that has 30 valid nights but no `partner`,\nthe app renders (Sarah backfilled), no error boundary, 0 console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"363dab59a708b351975b3cc1d3f5e250b66ba187","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/363dab59a708b351975b3cc1d3f5e250b66ba187"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/4e44e4736f03e24d8564e57f0ed0756f787b67db","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/4e44e4736f03e24d8564e57f0ed0756f787b67db","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKDRlNDRlNDczNmYwM2UyNGQ4NTY0ZTU3ZjBlZDA3NTZmNzg3YjY3ZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/011f13e08987ac8cf5a2ef3afef94f1c06d13166","sha":"011f13e08987ac8cf5a2ef3afef94f1c06d13166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/011f13e08987ac8cf5a2ef3afef94f1c06d13166"}],"sha":"4e44e4736f03e24d8564e57f0ed0756f787b67db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/4e44e4736f03e24d8564e57f0ed0756f787b67db"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/011f13e08987ac8cf5a2ef3afef94f1c06d13166/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T07:42:28Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T07:42:28Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"message":"Diagnose/fix iOS blank screen: error surfacing + es2020 target\n\nThe app renders on desktop/Blink (incl. 390px mobile width) with zero console\nerrors, but blanks on iOS (both Safari and Chrome are WebKit there) — a\nWebKit-specific startup failure that white-screens silently because there was\nno error handling.\n\n- ErrorBoundary around <App> → a branded, recoverable screen (with a reload\n  that also clears stale SW/caches) instead of a blank page on any render error.\n- Inline boot-error catcher in index.html (runs before the bundle) → surfaces\n  ANY startup error on screen, including a bundle/WebKit error that would\n  white-screen before React mounts. Only ever shows if something fails.\n- Lower build target es2022 → es2020 so esbuild emits syntax compatible with\n  older iOS Safari (the most likely root cause). (safari14 target trips an\n  esbuild destructuring-lowering limitation, so es2020 is the safe choice.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"411992a16cb70b49c878d1a3effd94e1d0a0746a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/411992a16cb70b49c878d1a3effd94e1d0a0746a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/011f13e08987ac8cf5a2ef3afef94f1c06d13166","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/011f13e08987ac8cf5a2ef3afef94f1c06d13166","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKDAxMWYxM2UwODk4N2FjOGNmNWEyZWYzYWZlZjk0ZjFjMDZkMTMxNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/9c0d6b6052fe9c15f5ee26b85d5494056f7b7f32","sha":"9c0d6b6052fe9c15f5ee26b85d5494056f7b7f32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/9c0d6b6052fe9c15f5ee26b85d5494056f7b7f32"}],"sha":"011f13e08987ac8cf5a2ef3afef94f1c06d13166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/011f13e08987ac8cf5a2ef3afef94f1c06d13166"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/9c0d6b6052fe9c15f5ee26b85d5494056f7b7f32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T14:42:51Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T14:42:51Z","email":"matt@ebmitchell.com","name":"Matt Edmund"},"message":"Fix PWA on mobile: single service worker, purge stale worker/caches\n\nThe repo carried a hand-written public/sw.js (from the old HTML-prototype era —\nit precached /screens/*.html that no longer exist) plus a duplicate static\npublic/manifest.webmanifest, both colliding with the vite-plugin-pwa output.\nA phone that ever loaded an earlier deploy could stay stuck on the old worker\nserving missing/stale assets (blank screen).\n\n- Delete public/sw.js and public/manifest.webmanifest — vite-plugin-pwa is now\n  the single source of truth for both.\n- Drop manifest.webmanifest from includeAssets accordingly.\n- workbox: cleanupOutdatedCaches + clientsClaim + skipWaiting so a returning\n  phone immediately adopts the new worker and old precaches are purged.\n\nVerified dist: one workbox sw.js (no /screens refs), correct generated\nmanifest (Dr. Never Snore, #1E2544), skipWaiting/clientsClaim present.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc163aa6589d674cd21210a00edc149d88442073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/dc163aa6589d674cd21210a00edc149d88442073"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/9c0d6b6052fe9c15f5ee26b85d5494056f7b7f32","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/9c0d6b6052fe9c15f5ee26b85d5494056f7b7f32","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKDljMGQ2YjYwNTJmZTljMTVmNWVlMjZiODVkNTQ5NDA1NmY3YjdmMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/967d3e3aee4a0cb51491f36a17ca3abe6706e0e6","sha":"967d3e3aee4a0cb51491f36a17ca3abe6706e0e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/967d3e3aee4a0cb51491f36a17ca3abe6706e0e6"}],"sha":"9c0d6b6052fe9c15f5ee26b85d5494056f7b7f32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/9c0d6b6052fe9c15f5ee26b85d5494056f7b7f32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147274900?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/33prime","id":147274900,"login":"33prime","node_id":"U_kgDOCMc8lA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/967d3e3aee4a0cb51491f36a17ca3abe6706e0e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T14:34:21Z","email":"147274900+33prime@users.noreply.github.com","name":"33prime"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T14:34:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Make chat visibly stream + add a discoverable \"Track sleep\" entry (#5)\n\nChat streaming:\n- The reply was arriving token-by-token at the data layer but appeared all at\n  once because the store kept the same `chat` array reference on append, so the\n  selective subscriber (useStore(s => s.chat)) never re-rendered mid-stream.\n  Now the chat array is replaced immutably on every token → the reply streams\n  in, and auto-scroll follows it. That''s the magical feel.\n\nDiscoverability:\n- Live sleep tracking was only reachable from the debug gear menu. Added a\n  \"Track sleep\" pill to the dashboard top bar → /night → Start listening.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Edmund <matt@ebmitchell.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fcdc398d6dc6be96a9d6cfac153cdcecec5cd308","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/fcdc398d6dc6be96a9d6cfac153cdcecec5cd308"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/967d3e3aee4a0cb51491f36a17ca3abe6706e0e6","verification":{"payload":"tree fcdc398d6dc6be96a9d6cfac153cdcecec5cd308\nparent 2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103\nauthor 33prime <147274900+33prime@users.noreply.github.com> 1780670061 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780670061 +0200\n\nMake chat visibly stream + add a discoverable \"Track sleep\" entry (#5)\n\nChat streaming:\n- The reply was arriving token-by-token at the data layer but appeared all at\n  once because the store kept the same `chat` array reference on append, so the\n  selective subscriber (useStore(s => s.chat)) never re-rendered mid-stream.\n  Now the chat array is replaced immutably on every token → the reply streams\n  in, and auto-scroll follows it. That''s the magical feel.\n\nDiscoverability:\n- Live sleep tracking was only reachable from the debug gear menu. Added a\n  \"Track sleep\" pill to the dashboard top bar → /night → Start listening.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Edmund <matt@ebmitchell.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIt5uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALMsQACZKpl0aUC1jjPB2b8M1VMIw\n6eca1RvrgS87boSTlZXD9OoDeUUpDV0avv4bqb1m/nHWD3+9AI6bRhuBgDVrGU/i\nuNgjKmhHSJW3NZVJ4dw0eTqxzZRRQDh+ti7YovWzZULLpSXnewribs4N6bRMwreS\nlBqN1WUOzeZZcR/x02YLchO2MQPZxba23ki6AP5Eh3xJpwNaXs/W6uhgla0cvgsC\nwrcr/8XO4OGEKHzjapGGLUksKpEz1QltJ1qm8BKUq7jaEydxeyG0cIgJZH/hvmAE\nVAzneAvs0nD8qYQw2V5wAMfI7dOkLhB3ZWW5T9ZcFA9XqQCsYkAa8aX+Ttkm/yQP\nXxJU0VV7pjCdyIKzJeuNHUYWUyifLa1o0uh7bxrOrwYQOibD4GUsPFricXHvq5Pe\nO3ATuZxh20MOk72fzlBX21h5wjwAyfAVG8MalC0knuSLnvKDBMkFxQ9ngZCR5mJJ\nsEL/QrKNRJK8XEGjTfhHFSsDA3POMK4lgfI5l8+R8BS/hWFrgm9jY4ztGeQ5DDIk\nLGaGrmLpvn4rKQdlu1uEIjgVgQjGWegZ3nBWLkfs/qcWkwvcboHzFwOct95ejdDn\n2kBB3eREN+b5vkr6nNU2DBtNgFvq3aXATEvQVQnzFPkgziKQGVUDqeLUwV/dXStu\nKdlmZz96VhetkZfeEkIA\n=h1hM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-05T14:34:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/967d3e3aee4a0cb51491f36a17ca3abe6706e0e6","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKDk2N2QzZTNhZWU0YTBjYjUxNDkxZjM2YTE3Y2EzYWJlNjcwNmUwZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103","sha":"2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103"}],"sha":"967d3e3aee4a0cb51491f36a17ca3abe6706e0e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/967d3e3aee4a0cb51491f36a17ca3abe6706e0e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147274900?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/33prime","id":147274900,"login":"33prime","node_id":"U_kgDOCMc8lA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T14:25:13Z","email":"147274900+33prime@users.noreply.github.com","name":"33prime"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T14:25:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Live mic snore detection — the core sensing loop, for real (#4)\n\nThe \"we listen to you sleep\" premise was entirely simulated. This makes it\nreal on the device, no backend required:\n\n- useSnoreDetector hook: getUserMedia + Web Audio AnalyserNode. Detects snores\n  by thresholding loudness against an adaptive noise floor AND requiring\n  low-frequency (~60–500 Hz) dominance, with a refractory window so one snore\n  counts once (taps/claps/typing don''t register). Tracks live level + peak dB.\n  Audio is analysed on-device in real time and never recorded or sent anywhere.\n- Night screen is now genuinely live: a \"Start listening\" permission flow, the\n  orb pulses to the real mic level, a snore counter that flashes on each\n  detection, peak dB, \"last snore Ns ago\", and a live loudness waveform.\n- Graceful fallback: if the mic is blocked/unsupported, a one-tap demo mode\n  keeps the flow working.\n- \"End night\" feeds the REAL detected snore count into the new night, so the\n  morning reveal reflects what was actually heard.\n\nNeeds a real mic + HTTPS (or localhost) + a user gesture — all true on the\ndeployed site.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Edmund <matt@ebmitchell.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"46835838bb53fe9ba197f5c892c0174058afbe0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/46835838bb53fe9ba197f5c892c0174058afbe0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103","verification":{"payload":"tree 46835838bb53fe9ba197f5c892c0174058afbe0e\nparent ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb\nauthor 33prime <147274900+33prime@users.noreply.github.com> 1780669513 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780669513 +0200\n\nLive mic snore detection — the core sensing loop, for real (#4)\n\nThe \"we listen to you sleep\" premise was entirely simulated. This makes it\nreal on the device, no backend required:\n\n- useSnoreDetector hook: getUserMedia + Web Audio AnalyserNode. Detects snores\n  by thresholding loudness against an adaptive noise floor AND requiring\n  low-frequency (~60–500 Hz) dominance, with a refractory window so one snore\n  counts once (taps/claps/typing don''t register). Tracks live level + peak dB.\n  Audio is analysed on-device in real time and never recorded or sent anywhere.\n- Night screen is now genuinely live: a \"Start listening\" permission flow, the\n  orb pulses to the real mic level, a snore counter that flashes on each\n  detection, peak dB, \"last snore Ns ago\", and a live loudness waveform.\n- Graceful fallback: if the mic is blocked/unsupported, a one-tap demo mode\n  keeps the flow working.\n- \"End night\" feeds the REAL detected snore count into the new night, so the\n  morning reveal reflects what was actually heard.\n\nNeeds a real mic + HTTPS (or localhost) + a user gesture — all true on the\ndeployed site.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Edmund <matt@ebmitchell.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqItxJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0YoQABDfGusQDuBZaos72S6nIQO+\nDkNtU6yBCvn9HKZSHDRUsNuLxClrcFhvfo7gEn641cO+uyV3F2WoiIMcKwWPiPX9\n83rKM1bk5GeIKlsZ4ARSN8LLSSL9nr/w9BQA45caaDlrAQrA6TYOWqaMvZ3LxcZ0\nhUM/G58oFMXImlOJUYEBH8btdhWR28YoRDEyLWWFaAugN6hWMFlhuLmMy6GSOC2Y\nli8VT/GiC5/su7iWbhCbFrq2rrV3CPRmWMCj/yqe4uUe6roWy+sSybY1yIV02TVj\neehA2IyxzrTbY6BBROkh03GCHvadh20jmMksSqCRcUaO8EoAfUf2zP46O45TjyNg\nIWifjXrgGr3WmgE7DTZ61Q6Zfhaz6Z34Fyxujv8NPS2tphPtv2hwaEcX9gtUIff3\n2tfT7H6vMrAmuhVdUi3/Tfc6qVwQXjySEZ+SvFLbFTSu/ErtirSfJ9jSQpBtfEtr\nSZiPb6msC2oUvBN46j9cuscrraMerlk4rog8jgu0fV8xEhBccKx97Lqxmw1brXJ5\nezZv/9dMB8aKYEifbVi88GcKoyuTrZLXcLU/TLaMFLiL73XEnUTnytUmrWc/ZGZw\novu31QAhzYBQmuOxUUkPKm37kvg6wYxrBWAL8RvAySZhal419Q7a8PPrG92FbAtf\n4LP9IN6GjmZ+Kl+1Tmlx\n=Hsui\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-05T14:25:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKDJiMWI0MjFhZTM3YTZkZDJiYTAxYmZmYmNhMzlmMmI1YjdlOGQxMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb","sha":"ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb"}],"sha":"2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/2b1b421ae37a6dd2ba01bffbca39f2b5b7e8d103"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147274900?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/33prime","id":147274900,"login":"33prime","node_id":"U_kgDOCMc8lA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T14:06:42Z","email":"147274900+33prime@users.noreply.github.com","name":"33prime"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T14:06:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Real-app pass: Profile/Settings screen, first-run gate, derived metrics (#3)\n\nTurn the demo into a coherent product — proper account/settings surface,\nreal navigation, and metrics that move with the data.\n\nProfile / Settings (new):\n- The Profile tab now opens a real Profile screen (was: the Reorder screen\n  mislabeled). Shows identity + cohort, a device-status card (strap position,\n  nights in use, % life) linking to the device overview, and a Reorder entry.\n- Real, persisted settings that previously lived only in the debug menu:\n  Appearance (Auto/Light/Dark) and \"Notify <partner> each morning\".\n- Links to The Science, Re-fit the device, and Replay onboarding; Sign out.\n- Reorder moved to /reorder as a sub-page (back → Profile). Dashboard avatar\n  → Profile; the supplement recommendation card → Reorder.\n\nNavigation correctness:\n- First-run gate: users with incomplete onboarding are routed through it;\n  returning users (with data) land on the dashboard.\n- Removed the placeholder \"Not found / Coming in commit 2\" stub — unknown\n  routes now redirect home. Every navigate() target resolves to a real route.\n\nDerived metrics (were hardcoded):\n- Dashboard Sleep/Efficiency stat tiles now compute their delta vs the prior\n  14 nights.\n- Trends mini-cards (efficiency / HRV / resting HR) compute their delta vs the\n  pre-device baseline week, with correct better/worse direction.\n\nBuilds clean (tsc --noEmit + vite). Chat untouched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Edmund <matt@ebmitchell.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c4d37b8d625078d9e485b015c6559b1f75039182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/c4d37b8d625078d9e485b015c6559b1f75039182"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb","verification":{"payload":"tree c4d37b8d625078d9e485b015c6559b1f75039182\nparent 455bde75cdd1e44abe1ed64478094c8dddd1797c\nauthor 33prime <147274900+33prime@users.noreply.github.com> 1780668402 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780668402 +0200\n\nReal-app pass: Profile/Settings screen, first-run gate, derived metrics (#3)\n\nTurn the demo into a coherent product — proper account/settings surface,\nreal navigation, and metrics that move with the data.\n\nProfile / Settings (new):\n- The Profile tab now opens a real Profile screen (was: the Reorder screen\n  mislabeled). Shows identity + cohort, a device-status card (strap position,\n  nights in use, % life) linking to the device overview, and a Reorder entry.\n- Real, persisted settings that previously lived only in the debug menu:\n  Appearance (Auto/Light/Dark) and \"Notify <partner> each morning\".\n- Links to The Science, Re-fit the device, and Replay onboarding; Sign out.\n- Reorder moved to /reorder as a sub-page (back → Profile). Dashboard avatar\n  → Profile; the supplement recommendation card → Reorder.\n\nNavigation correctness:\n- First-run gate: users with incomplete onboarding are routed through it;\n  returning users (with data) land on the dashboard.\n- Removed the placeholder \"Not found / Coming in commit 2\" stub — unknown\n  routes now redirect home. Every navigate() target resolves to a real route.\n\nDerived metrics (were hardcoded):\n- Dashboard Sleep/Efficiency stat tiles now compute their delta vs the prior\n  14 nights.\n- Trends mini-cards (efficiency / HRV / resting HR) compute their delta vs the\n  pre-device baseline week, with correct better/worse direction.\n\nBuilds clean (tsc --noEmit + vite). Chat untouched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Edmund <matt@ebmitchell.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqItfyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAebgQAD6o6oi+LlL1Ay/GHRfF/VMR\nvywuX1v2RXi4hN4ZjcRFjzfWYk4kiAOp91UcCaUAxsqQs7NqXz59zfACM9Ebp16a\nNK+YhD7qNu30AIIXUgZ1gDs7YN3zNAnaHnV1Hv0k14BNJ5WcgyWmvRAFxvgY7MmG\n/3EZSiDbfkMPUbzC6Zos2kLjbx/pSAb5QkG2SrBihB1ojSzXSRugHL8wm4Qpb8DQ\nIes2qmH9iqIrjOAaeJwKjndm6JU1jSCtec6G7L6LN7rak6gORQ8Nod4HCw+ltzbj\nASLd8NSPG0spe43e7GfGZrqFGcLUeNGjxoFl1RnaHaznxi5sRgigrhajc5mS/Yuy\nkVM2OVtEshaGOXpma5o5RnsSgm3Urlr1695Xu25DPFU/GDzTxjZak/PpcRvRQz5/\nTOhSiQobY4xueYvh9phH4cE+fChOTc0+LDd2hNu6dw+uGh2oqbUeRJyICf8YiQiM\nIEifZNjiNbq1Gcj4FEntaRMAZrHRuoUpg7e45qhBh49DNkDEjcYs4JOfHJB+FUbQ\niQqtJJ1vohunacbaaqEbAzANlJLCgOsbyQAbpOOoUXVVG4TvTwxQ8UMRkI3q550J\nV3SWSrfTatoUKz76wjEBYkxNkpDlRbjD3FFNv/OU6Q8Mq3p5YkrVZ/z5tgtIq61Y\nhUEkaI8HhZylGvS3kUkq\n=YDPD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-05T14:06:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb","node_id":"C_kwDOSSyqG9oAKGNlMDQwMmZhMGU4NDA1NGY1OTVkYmUzMjM3ODUzMDFlNzQxZTBhZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commit/455bde75cdd1e44abe1ed64478094c8dddd1797c","sha":"455bde75cdd1e44abe1ed64478094c8dddd1797c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/455bde75cdd1e44abe1ed64478094c8dddd1797c"}],"sha":"ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/ce0402fa0e84054f595dbe323785301e741e0adb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147274900?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/33prime","id":147274900,"login":"33prime","node_id":"U_kgDOCMc8lA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/33prime","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/commits/455bde75cdd1e44abe1ed64478094c8dddd1797c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T13:51:05Z","email":"147274900+33prime@users.noreply.github.com","name":"33prime"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T13:51:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Make the app demo-ready: brand icons + wire dead controls + fix logic bugs (#2)\n\nBrand icons:\n- Replace generic PWA icons with a teal crescent moon on Midnight Blue\n  (the brand''s sleep motif), generated at every size incl. maskable.\n\nWire up previously-inert controls (no more dead taps on the happy path):\n- New reusable Menu component (accessible popover; closes on outside-click/Esc).\n- Dashboard: avatar opens Profile; removed the no-op Search; the three stat\n  tiles now open Trends.\n- Header \"⋯/More\" menus: Chat -> Detailed night report (surfaces the orphaned\n  /chat/rich showcase); DetailedNight -> Share with Sarah / Add a note;\n  DeviceOverview -> Re-run fitting / Adjustment guide; Reorder -> Manage\n  subscription / Order history; ChatRich -> Share with Sarah, and the audio\n  Play button now responds.\n- Reorder: shipping-address Edit now responds.\n\nCorrectness fixes:\n- BoilAndBite: Pause no longer restarts the countdown (preserves remaining).\n- Trends: range delta uses first-half vs second-half mean instead of two noisy\n  endpoint nights, so a good-news trend can''t show a jarring spike.\n- MorningReveal: deltas/\"quieter than N of 14\" derived from real data.\n- Comparisons: percentile is deterministic from the active cohort filters\n  (no random jumps) so it never contradicts the distribution chart.\n- Demo \"simulate/end night\" advances the date by a day (no duplicate-dated nights).\n\nChat API left untouched (driven by the real Anthropic key).\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Edmund <matt@ebmitchell.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a5c94193ac4797ba6f8b57f2b9c85949a468cf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/trees/9a5c94193ac4797ba6f8b57f2b9c85949a468cf9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/33prime/dr-better-sleep-anchorage/git/commits/455bde75cdd1e44abe1ed64478094c8dddd1797c","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a5c94193ac4797ba6f8b57f2b9c85949a468cf9\nparent e731f8eed286120d18765f4d20fb0e1fd3a96983\nauthor 33prime <147274900+33prime@users.noreply.github.com> 1780667465 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780667465 +0200\n\nMake the app demo-ready: brand icons + wire dead controls + fix logic bugs (#2)\n\nBrand icons:\n- Replace generic PWA icons with a teal crescent moon on Midnight Blue\n  (the brand''s sleep motif), generated at every size incl. maskable.\n\nWire up previously-inert controls (no more dead taps on the happy path):\n- New reusable Menu component (accessible popover; closes on outside-click/Esc).\n- Dashboard: avatar opens Profile; removed the no-op Search; the three stat\n  tiles now open Trends.\n- Header \"⋯/More\" menus: Chat -> Detailed night report (surfaces the orphaned\n  /chat/rich showcase); DetailedNight -> Share with Sarah / Add a note;\n  DeviceOverview -> Re-run fitting / Adjustment guide; Reorder -> Manage\n  subscription / Order history; ChatRich -> Share with Sarah, and the audio\n  Play button now responds.\n- Reorder: shipping-address Edit now responds.\n\nCorrectness fixes:\n- BoilAndBite: Pause no longer restarts the countdown (preserves remaining).\n- Trends: range delta uses first-half vs second-half mean instead of two noisy\n  endpoint nights, so a good-news trend can''t show a jarring spike.\n- MorningReveal: deltas/\"quieter than N of 14\" derived from real data.\n- Comparisons: percentile is deterministic from the active cohort filters\n  (no random jumps) so it never contradicts the distribution chart.\n- Demo \"simulate/end night\" advances the date by a day (no duplicate-dated nights).\n\nChat API left untouched (driven by the real Anthropic key).\n\nCo-authored-by: Matt Edmund <matt@ebmitchell.com>\nCo-aut